"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/c9b8e5b97c06526154dd96cf9d47ba1c83485ea9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:05:10Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:05:10Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"fix: restore the formatted errors and unify the custom tags write path\n\nThe merge of #537 reverted `formatError(error)` in eight message answers back\nto the raw error object, which JSON.stringify turns into `{}`: the caller of\ngetRetention, test, destroy, getDatapoints and getRawEntries received an empty\nerror instead of its text. Follow-up to f110458.\n\n- src/main.ts: enableHistory writes through a single path again. Instead of\n  choosing extendForeignObject or setForeignObject depending on whether\n  customTags is an array, writeCustomConfig() always reads, merges and writes\n  the object, so arrays are replaced instead of being merged element by element\n  - for every option, not only for customTags. The object is still created if\n  it does not exist yet.\n- src/lib/customTags.ts: normalizeCustomTags() also accepts the name -> value\n  map that getEnabledDPs reports, so a configuration read from there and\n  written back through enableHistory keeps its tags instead of losing them\n  silently.\n- .github/workflows: install src-admin before linting it. `npm ci` installs\n  only the root, so the React and ioBroker types did not resolve in src-admin\n  and eslint reported them as real errors. check-and-lint therefore failed on\n  master and the InfluxDB 1.x/2.x suites were skipped. The adapter test jobs\n  get this install through `npm run build`, this job did not.\n- README.md, docs/de/influxdb.md: changelog, the German section about custom\n  tags, the downgrade note for influxdata.json and the hint that an aggregated\n  getHistory over a tag change aggregates each series on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"feccf06fce8ad37e4e752b153ed04650c1bc9ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/trees/feccf06fce8ad37e4e752b153ed04650c1bc9ed7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/commits/c9b8e5b97c06526154dd96cf9d47ba1c83485ea9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commit/c9b8e5b97c06526154dd96cf9d47ba1c83485ea9","node_id":"C_kwDOAts889oAKGM5YjhlNWI5N2MwNjUyNjE1NGRkOTZjZjlkNDdiYTFjODM0ODVlYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commit/8814ceb648e32da8a33c2e627093eee89c9f4981","sha":"8814ceb648e32da8a33c2e627093eee89c9f4981","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/8814ceb648e32da8a33c2e627093eee89c9f4981"}],"sha":"c9b8e5b97c06526154dd96cf9d47ba1c83485ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/c9b8e5b97c06526154dd96cf9d47ba1c83485ea9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96919536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jb-io","id":96919536,"login":"jb-io","node_id":"U_kgDOBcbf8A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jb-io","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/8814ceb648e32da8a33c2e627093eee89c9f4981/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:48:38Z","email":"96919536+jb-io@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JB"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T18:48:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add custom tags per datapoint (#32) (#537)\n\n* feat: add validation of custom tags of a datapoint\n\nConverts the custom tags as stored in the datapoint settings (rows of\n{name, value}) into the tags to write. Rows without name or value are\nskipped (InfluxDB drops tags with an empty value, and the admin table adds\nempty rows with \"+\"), as are names that collide with what the adapter\nwrites itself (value, q, ack, from), the InfluxQL keyword time and names\nstarting with \"_\", which InfluxDB 2.x reserves.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* refactor: build the points for InfluxDB 1.x in one place\n\nwriteSeries, writePoints and writePoint each converted the values into a\npoint with an identical copy of the same loop. No functional change.\n\n* feat: write tags of a point to InfluxDB 1.x and 2.x\n\nA point can carry tags (name -> value) now, they are written as InfluxDB\ntags with the point. For 2.x this does not depend on \"Store metadata as\ntags\": custom tags can not collide with q/ack/from, whose names are\nreserved.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* feat: write the custom tags of a datapoint with each of its values\n\nThe custom config of a datapoint gets the new attribute customTags, a\nlist of {name, value}. It is validated when the config is read (invalid\nrows are reported as warning and ignored), and every value of the\ndatapoint is written with these tags. The tags are part of the buffered\npoint, so a change of the tags only affects values logged afterwards.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* fix: allow removing custom tags via enableHistory\n\nenableHistory extends the object, and extendObject merges arrays element\nby element: an empty or shorter list of custom tags kept the old rows, so\nthe last tag could never be removed. If customTags is given, the custom\nconfig of the instance is now replaced as a whole.\n\nThis was reported in the review of #278.\n\n* feat(admin): edit the custom tags in the datapoint settings\n\nAdds the table \"Custom tags\" (name/value) to the InfluxDB settings of a\ndatapoint, with translations. Names must be unique and not reserved, a\nrow needs both name and value - a completely empty row is allowed and\nignored. Unlike the first attempt in #278, there is no list of allowed tag\nnames in the instance settings and the table is shown independent of\n\"Store metadata as tags\", because custom tags work in both modes.\n\n* test: cover custom tags in the integration tests\n\nRuns in every suite (InfluxDB 1.x, 2.x with fields and with tags, buffered\nand with existing data): enables a datapoint with custom tags, checks the\nnormalized config, writes values, selects them by their tags directly in\nthe database and via getHistory, and removes all tags again.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* docs: describe custom tags\n\nRefs #32\n\n* chore: make io-package.json match the current schema\n\nThe package file test validates against the io-package.json schema of the\njs-controller master and failed with:\n- /common: must NOT have additional properties \"subscribe\"\n- /common/docs: must have required property ''en''\n\n\"subscribe\": \"messagebox\" is the legacy way to receive messages, the\nadapter already declares \"messagebox\": true. The English documentation is\nthe README.","tree":{"sha":"634a88ea95ad8ecd7ace8503c092cb7f14f2fa88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/trees/634a88ea95ad8ecd7ace8503c092cb7f14f2fa88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/commits/8814ceb648e32da8a33c2e627093eee89c9f4981","verification":{"payload":"tree 634a88ea95ad8ecd7ace8503c092cb7f14f2fa88\nparent 0a69f11ec327982ee18b3e609d3867a2671eca82\nauthor JB <96919536+jb-io@users.noreply.github.com> 1791053318 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791053318 +0200\n\nAdd custom tags per datapoint (#32) (#537)\n\n* feat: add validation of custom tags of a datapoint\n\nConverts the custom tags as stored in the datapoint settings (rows of\n{name, value}) into the tags to write. Rows without name or value are\nskipped (InfluxDB drops tags with an empty value, and the admin table adds\nempty rows with \"+\"), as are names that collide with what the adapter\nwrites itself (value, q, ack, from), the InfluxQL keyword time and names\nstarting with \"_\", which InfluxDB 2.x reserves.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* refactor: build the points for InfluxDB 1.x in one place\n\nwriteSeries, writePoints and writePoint each converted the values into a\npoint with an identical copy of the same loop. No functional change.\n\n* feat: write tags of a point to InfluxDB 1.x and 2.x\n\nA point can carry tags (name -> value) now, they are written as InfluxDB\ntags with the point. For 2.x this does not depend on \"Store metadata as\ntags\": custom tags can not collide with q/ack/from, whose names are\nreserved.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* feat: write the custom tags of a datapoint with each of its values\n\nThe custom config of a datapoint gets the new attribute customTags, a\nlist of {name, value}. It is validated when the config is read (invalid\nrows are reported as warning and ignored), and every value of the\ndatapoint is written with these tags. The tags are part of the buffered\npoint, so a change of the tags only affects values logged afterwards.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* fix: allow removing custom tags via enableHistory\n\nenableHistory extends the object, and extendObject merges arrays element\nby element: an empty or shorter list of custom tags kept the old rows, so\nthe last tag could never be removed. If customTags is given, the custom\nconfig of the instance is now replaced as a whole.\n\nThis was reported in the review of #278.\n\n* feat(admin): edit the custom tags in the datapoint settings\n\nAdds the table \"Custom tags\" (name/value) to the InfluxDB settings of a\ndatapoint, with translations. Names must be unique and not reserved, a\nrow needs both name and value - a completely empty row is allowed and\nignored. Unlike the first attempt in #278, there is no list of allowed tag\nnames in the instance settings and the table is shown independent of\n\"Store metadata as tags\", because custom tags work in both modes.\n\n* test: cover custom tags in the integration tests\n\nRuns in every suite (InfluxDB 1.x, 2.x with fields and with tags, buffered\nand with existing data): enables a datapoint with custom tags, checks the\nnormalized config, writes values, selects them by their tags directly in\nthe database and via getHistory, and removes all tags again.\n\nRefs #32\n\n* docs: describe custom tags\n\nRefs #32\n\n* chore: make io-package.json match the current schema\n\nThe package file test validates against the io-package.json schema of the\njs-controller master and failed with:\n- /common: must NOT have additional properties \"subscribe\"\n- /common/docs: must have required property ''en''\n\n\"subscribe\": \"messagebox\" is the legacy way to receive messages, the\nadapter already declares \"messagebox\": true. The English documentation is\nthe README.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwU4GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcdMQAJx0xvO9EbQNZsE3A8z39XRo\nLY7v3cuYkEvoGLdQVcXos8ZOqHJWni9ll19hnAgbyGsI3sHd43ED53dcscOq5UiS\nW7nKw6LyOBwj0Fg67xvR615sLJ9YgozPwC6ngblKIGtPoaIUdbCk2B1/2YfKQJbQ\nwfhMxyyRss1LVeOqUpxNz6Gc5f6yScgZRLiUhPT+Ujd1oxExzLa1bjXFfmN2nBI/\nhML52xcjhW6JNxNHoZK3XytZodWdUQjLZV4FN6VQ1tFWCAwH8shw6QC9W5QbM71R\n+18q71NLJ7+ah4gFp9L/TlbBTBoIRxDv0K4M/J1ELK0L7JOyUDvqC+L5kLDbzXgr\nWfaBCqFVoVK9A/kwlvHGrJPOte13QIoy0SEK/SaVre5BKw47eT8ELavi4/z3ZPNI\nNaj31nbq8//v3K50JXdYZF22t5r6SL8oJ1eqZUt+jtfhuAljqnrUGtX6tZ+a238o\nAq0x7+I2CwXBWM03GA97s3pglnAb3zqfmI7ghpct1Q6MEbaa2uKHT9fYPq+fay5b\nkkJj5U/XvEKLers/agh9C58uRVVcVQe6VrDKILKBFMf8pUN1KzTV7+AaNqOm4RV/\ngAqt8ZLd5qXOMKfiD3T6HCjoXn+mw8Z2fwA76wsOMhLmmFDfF7673iPdv1u5V7zF\nYlwLdyN/ynV9ctbJEThl\n=iTfZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T18:48:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/fol