er.influxdb/commits/7a96e3d5ae44516116dea62f39244a2804d80da6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/c98f7b97750aaf71e6b0f299e4c1c7e5dac06ba7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:40:16Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:40:16Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Make the integration tests report the real failure and stop the flaky integral expectations\n\nA failed expectation inside a sendTo callback was swallowed by the messaging\nlayer, so done() was never reached and mocha reported \"Timeout of 25000ms\nexceeded\" instead of the value that was wrong - that is what the two integral\ntests looked like in CI. The callbacks are wrapped once now and re-throw\noutside the callback, where mocha attributes the exception to the running\ntest (the mechanism test/mocha.setup.js already uses for rejections); the two\nasync tests hand their rejection to done() instead of dropping it.\n\nThe integral tests themselves asserted an exact bucket count. Flux aligns the\nwindows of window(every: <step>) to the epoch, not to the queried range, and\nthe adapter queries one step more at each end for the chart. Whether those two\nextra buckets end up outside the requested range - and are dropped again by\nremoveBorderValues - depends on where \"now\" sits on that grid, so the result\nholds count..count+2 buckets. CI showed 5, 6 and 7 for the same test, on\nunrelated commits as well.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017ieUDXZRokLVjqaHVBvta2","tree":{"sha":"f4a3e1d8229a6a7170ce4c8ca8dd280f9cfbd4c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/trees/f4a3e1d8229a6a7170ce4c8ca8dd280f9cfbd4c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/commits/c98f7b97750aaf71e6b0f299e4c1c7e5dac06ba7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commit/c98f7b97750aaf71e6b0f299e4c1c7e5dac06ba7","node_id":"C_kwDOAts889oAKGM5OGY3Yjk3NzUwYWFmNzFlNmIwZjI5OWU0YzFjN2U1ZGFjMDZiYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commit/aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a","sha":"aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a"}],"sha":"c98f7b97750aaf71e6b0f299e4c1c7e5dac06ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/c98f7b97750aaf71e6b0f299e4c1c7e5dac06ba7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:17:12Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:17:41Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Report the real host availability instead of a hardcoded 1\n\ngetHostsAvailable() returned a constant 1 in both database classes since the\nTypeScript port. In v4 it was client.request.getHostsAvailable().length, i.e.\nthe host list of the driver pool, so all 13 \"host not available\" checks in\nmain.ts have been dead code: an unreachable InfluxDB never buffered, never\nsignalled \"no hosts available\" and ran into the per-point escalation instead.\n\nThe base class now tracks it: a request that fails with a connection error\ntakes the host out of rotation, a successful one brings it back, and after a\nshort backoff it is tried again - the same behaviour the 1.x driver pool has\ninternally, and it works for 2.x as well. Verified against a closed port with\nboth drivers: writePoints() rejects, getHostsAvailable() becomes 0, and after\nthe backoff it is 1 again.\n\nOnly connection errors change the state - a rejected point (\"field type\nconflict\", \"unauthorized\") says nothing about the reachability of the server.\n\nFollow-ups this makes necessary, because those code paths can now actually run:\n- storeBufferedSeries() throws a typed HostUnavailableError, so the callers\n  throttle it like any other connection error instead of logging it for every\n  buffered value.\n- The buffer flush interval catches the rejection: an unhandled one terminates\n  the process on current Node.js versions.\n- Repeated connection errors are tracked per message now, so writes, pings and\n  reconnects do not cancel each other''s throttling out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017ieUDXZRokLVjqaHVBvta2","tree":{"sha":"44f5905822bd94ed7e33c7e5a0e1bb35579f3e65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/trees/44f5905822bd94ed7e33c7e5a0e1bb35579f3e65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/commits/aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commit/aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a","node_id":"C_kwDOAts889oAKGFhNmZlZDZiZWI3MTU3NDYwMWE1YTQ3MTMxMGEzY2IwNTcxODA0N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commit/f11045812947430a70538d0b6d794e7c8339fe4e","sha":"f11045812947430a70538d0b6d794e7c8339fe4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/f11045812947430a70538d0b6d794e7c8339fe4e"}],"sha":"aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/aa6fed6beb71574601a5a471310a3cb05718047a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/f11045812947430a70538d0b6d794e7c8339fe4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:09:56Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:17:41Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"Recognize connection errors and stop the log flood of an unreachable DB\n\nNode reports a failed TCP connect as an AggregateError whose own message is\nempty (happy-eyeballs, verified with both drivers against a closed port), so\nneither `error.message === ''timeout''` nor `errorText.includes(''timeout'')`\ncould ever match it. A stopped InfluxDB therefore ran into the \"find the\nconflicting point\" escalation: every batch was split down to single points,\nevery point was logged, and the ioBroker log (and syslog) filled up.\n\n- src/lib/errors.ts: formatError() (shared implementation with ioBroker.sql)\n  plus isConnectionError(), which classifies by error code, driver error name\n  and gateway status code instead of by message text.\n- The write path, connect(), checkMetaDataStorageType() and ping() now use it:\n  points are buffered and a reconnect is scheduled, and the repeated error is\n  logged once and afterwards only once an hour.\n- checkMetaDataStorageType() schedules a reconnect on a connection error - it\n  swallowed it before, so a 2.x instance stayed disconnected forever.\n\nFollow-up to #518: pushHelper() throws again for values InfluxDB cannot store,\nso storeState() answers with an error instead of a silent \"success: true\"\nwhile the state-change path keeps logging them only once per datapoint. The\nsame throttling now covers the \"state value undefined\" warning.\n\nAlso applies #455 (dependabot schedule) and adds test/testErrors.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017ieUDXZRokLVjqaHVBvta2","tree":{"sha":"0b462a63a2d5ddca13645900a412762c33708693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/trees/0b462a63a2d5ddca13645900a412762c33708693"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/commits/f11045812947430a70538d0b6d794e7c8339fe4e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/st