ub.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/commits/f56df5425e6986b1bc41ebf872e4d456e4ea9621/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:07:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:07:57Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v5.0.2\n\n* (@GermanBluefox) Added the data browser to the configuration, so the stored values can be viewed, edited and deleted.\n* (@GermanBluefox) The aggregation is used now from `@iobroker/aggregate` and is shared with the history and SQL adapters.\n* (@joltcoke) Fixed average and total returning null for every interval that contains a null value: parseFloat(null) is NaN and poisoned the sum of the whole interval (thanks to @joltcoke, ioBroker/ioBroker.sql#526). As the result was NaN and not null, ignoreNull could not act on it either\n* (@joltcoke) Fixed min returning a wrong value if the interval contains a null, minmax losing the minimum if the interval starts with a null, and percentile/quantile counting a null as 0","tree":{"sha":"44bdafa90e0991b18317ca666a5ead343618f7a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/trees/44bdafa90e0991b18317ca666a5ead343618f7a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ioBroker/ioBroker.influxdb/git/commits/f56df5425e6986b1bc41ebf872e4d456e4ea9621","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github