s://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.telegram/commits/87f265c44e2d65820ff340f0019c3b054d14ac08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:35:17Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T11:35:17Z","email":"dogafox@gmail.com","name":"GermanBluefox"},"message":"chore: release v6.0.0\n\n- (@GermanBluefox) Adapter requires Node.js >= 22.19 now (required by undici 8)\n- (@GermanBluefox) The connection to the telegram servers can be routed through an HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 proxy (new \"Use proxy\" settings; the old proxy fields had been without function for years)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Migrated to `node-telegram-bot-api` v2. Updates are now received via long polling, so the \"Polling interval\" setting became obsolete and was removed from the configuration dialog. Errors thrown while processing an update are logged by the adapter instead of ending up on the console\n- (@GermanBluefox) An empty \"API URL\" field no longer breaks every API call with \"EFATAL: Failed to parse URL\" - the default `https://api.telegram.org` is used again (#1371)\n- (@GermanBluefox) A `text2command`/`assistant` instance stored in the long form (`system.adapter.text2command.0`, written by the config UI before v1.12.6) is migrated to the short form on startup, so the config dialog shows the selected instance again (#1365)\n- (@GermanBluefox) Added the states `communicate.requestLocationLive` (live location is still being shared), `communicate.requestLocationHeading` and `communicate.requestLocationAccuracy` for received (live) locations","tree":{"sha":"14b58ed97ece8b04065b403d4eb40862463b4c6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.telegram/git/trees/14b58ed97ece8b04065b403d4eb40862463b4c6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.telegram/git/commits/87f265c44e2d65820ff340f0019c3b054d14ac08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4582016?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GermanBluefox","id":4582016,"login":"GermanBluefox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1ODIwMTY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GermanBluefox","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.telegram/commit/87f265c44e2d65820ff340f0019c3b054d14ac08","node_id":"C_kwDOAxRrTtoAKDg3ZjI2NWM0NGUyZDY1ODIwZmYzNDBmMDAxOWMzYjA1NGQxNGFjMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.telegram/commit/057b3f3aa4faa1e9055e248f695d8aa46ecc3dc0","sha":"057b3f3aa4faa1e9055e248f695d8aa46ecc3dc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iobroker-community-adapters/ioBroker.telegram/commits/057b3f3aa4faa1e9055e248f695d8aa46ecc3dc0"}],"sha":"87f265c44e2d65820ff340f0019c3b054d14ac08","url":"https://api.githu