tps://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/08c87a3dddcad31b967bc7e81e1eb96a7ae47f76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:34:56Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:34:56Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"message":"[SPEC:docs/specs/epic/phase-topology] ♻️ refactor(parameters): Remove the AICCRA AF start phase parameter\n\ncrp_aiccra_af_start_phase only fed BaseAction.isAFPhase(), which compared\nglobal auto-increment phase ids against it (default 423, an AICCRA phase).\nEvery phase of AICCRA_III, TEST and any new Global Unit is above that id, so\nthey were always in AF mode; only AICCRA''s closed 2019-2023 phases were not.\nThe AF labels are now always shown and the parameter is removed.\n\n- Drop getStartAFPhase() / isAFPhase() and the constant in both APConstants\n- Keep only the AF branch in the five FTL spots and ProjectExpectedStudiesAction\n- The second contributions table now always renders the Performance Indicator\n  header, matching the row macro, which always wrote that cell\n- Migration backfills rep_ind_stage_studies.description_af where empty, then\n  deletes custom_parameters and parameters rows by key. DML only, no assumed\n  ids, idempotent; run twice on a throwaway copy of aiccradb2 tables\n- Pass the exception to three logger.error calls that dropped it, translate a\n  Spanish comment and remove a leftover dev marker\n\nVerified with a clean recompile of marlo-data + marlo-web (BUILD SUCCESS,\n2416 + 1046 files), Checkstyle at zero delta against HEAD, and a clean\nJava hygiene check.","tree":{"sha":"1da7d0f6618fe08e9db4c4c33765c978cd22b664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/trees/1da7d0f6618fe08e9db4c4c33765c978cd22b664"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/commits/08c87a3dddcad31b967bc7e81e1eb96a7ae47f76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":nul