:"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenjitm","id":17478511,"login":"kenjitm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDc4NTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/63d24f29c9f8cbe4f9205a0d9fd82bb42642633e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:31:28Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:31:28Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"message":"🐛 fix(global): Restore the save confirmation messages\n\ngeneralMessages.ftl feeds showNotificationMessages() in global.js, which\nreads $(''#generalMessages'').find(\"#message\"). Commenting out the two\niterators in e8cb9a02a1 left that lookup with no data source, so every\nPOST-and-redirect save in the site stopped confirming anything. They sit\ninside a hidden <ul> and render nothing on their own, which is why removing\nthem looked harmless.\n\nParameters was one of the screens with nothing to show even once the\niterators are back, since its save never added a message; it now reports\nsuccess like the rest.","tree":{"sha":"2138a2b52ed1567db6e492a780bee932b60badf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/trees/2138a2b52ed1567db6e492a780bee932b60badf2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/commits/63d24f29c9f8cbe4f9205a0d9fd82bb42642633e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17478511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenjitm","id":17478511,"login":"kenjitm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDc4NTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/CCAFS/MARLO/commit/63d24f29c9f8cbe4f9205a0d9fd82bb42642633e","node_id":"C_kwDOA329DNoAKDYzZDI0ZjI5YzlmOGNiZTRmOTIwNWEwZDlmZDgyYmI0MjY0MjYzM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/CCAFS/MARLO/commit/580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217","sha":"580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217"}],"sha":"63d24f29c9f8cbe4f9205a0d9fd82bb42642633e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/63d24f29c9f8cbe4f9205a0d9fd82bb42642633e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17478511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenjitm","id":17478511,"login":"kenjitm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDc4NTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:31:20Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:31:20Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"message":"🐛 fix(oicr reports): Map the queue endpoint''s error result and log its failures\n\nsendOICRsQueueMessage returns ERROR on every failure path, but the action\nmapped only \"success\". Struts then raised \"No result defined\", which the\nglobal Exception mapping turned into an unhandled-exception page and email --\nso a queue failure reported itself as a crash. Both outcomes are now plain\nstatus codes: 200 on success, 500 on error, with no view to render for a\nfire-and-forget endpoint.\n\nThe failure traces were going to System.out, which no appender collects, and\ncarried only getMessage() with no stack trace and no queue name. They are now\nLOG.error calls with the queue as a parameter, and the field follows the\nrepository''s static LOG convention.","tree":{"sha":"849cfcc5996814332adff626182bfc0a5be855aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/trees/849cfcc5996814332adff626182bfc0a5be855aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/commits/580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17478511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenjitm","id":17478511,"login":"kenjitm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDc4NTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/CCAFS/MARLO/commit/580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217","node_id":"C_kwDOA329DNoAKDU4MGMwYmNjMDU5YzIwOTYzMzhjNDJiYmQ2ZDhhYmI3ODBiNmUyMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/CCAFS/MARLO/commit/2e2ccfdd0c5ea8ebe492e1848954f1ddb30eb38c","sha":"2e2ccfdd0c5ea8ebe492e1848954f1ddb30eb38c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/2e2ccfdd0c5ea8ebe492e1848954f1ddb30eb38c"}],"sha":"580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/580c0bcc059c2096338c42bbd6d8abb780b6e217"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17478511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kenjitm","id":17478511,"login":"kenjitm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDc4NTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenjitm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/commits/2e2ccfdd0c5ea8ebe492e1848954f1ddb30eb38c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:31:11Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:31:11Z","email":"k.tanaka@cgiar.org","name":"Kenji Tanaka"},"message":"♻️ refactor(parameters): Remove seven parameters that no code reads\n\nSuper Admin offered seven switches that nothing in the application\nconsumes; saving them wrote a value no reader ever looked at.\n\nSpecificities tab (category 2):\n\n  crp_generic_project          efef7a5655 added the constants and nothing else\n  crp_generic_project_value    same commit; the stored 0 is not a project id\n  crp_budgetbycoas             its section was deleted in 1e982f09a3 (2019)\n  melia_score_field_active     its only reader went in 43e3f3f358 (2025-04)\n  display_user_menu_new_style  retired: the user menu is chrome for every unit\n  crp_email_pl_crpAdmin_fl     no constant and no reader\n\nSettings tab (category 3):\n\n  crp_timeline_week_parameter_visualization\n\nThe timeline setting reached the front end only through\ngetTimelineWeeksParameter.do, which no JavaScript or template calls. The\nschedule card keeps its zoom in localStorage, decided in the\nhomepage-schedule spec precisely because this parameter''s seeded default\n''423'' is outside the 1..8 scale the feature accepts. Its action, its Struts\nmapping and the hardcoded \"4\" that GlobalUnitCreationManagerImpl used to\ndodge that default go with it.\n\nDropping that workaround is only safe together with the migration: with the\nparameter row still present, a Global Unit created by this code inherits the\ninvalid ''423''. Flyway migrates at startup before the app serves traffic, so\na normal deployment has no such window.\n\ncrp_budgetbycoas turned out to be a two-method chain, not one:\ngetCrpEnableBudgetByCoas() was called by canEditBudgetByCoAs(long), which is\nitself called by nothing. Both are removed. The clean recompile found that\ncall; a key search alone had missed it because it sits inside BaseAction.\n\nmarloParameters.ftl loses the crpAdmin -> systemAdmin display exception,\nwhich existed only for crp_email_pl_crpAdmin_fl, and main-menu.ftl no longer\nnames a specificity that no longer exists.\n\nThe migration deletes custom_parameters before parameters, since\ncustom_parameters_ibfk_1 points at parameters(id) and the reverse order\nfails with MySQL 1452 and leaves the migration half applied. It matches on\nkey and category, never on a global_unit_id, so it is a no-op wherever the\nrows were never seeded.\n\nVerified with a clean recompile of marlo-data + marlo-web (BUILD SUCCESS,\n2415 + 1044 files), Checkstyle at zero delta against HEAD, the 80 Pentaho\n.prpt bundles and the database routines and views searched for every key,\nand the four statements run step by step against an untouched AICCRA copy\ninside a rolled-back transaction: 99 + 2 custom_parameters rows and 18 + 3\ncatalog rows removed, 0 orphans, roles untouched.","tree":{"sha":"af8da46af5479bf9bcb373566b7f771384ac074b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/trees/af8da46af5479bf9bcb373566b7f771384ac074b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CCAFS/MARLO/git/commits/2e2ccfdd0c5ea8ebe492e1848954f1ddb30eb38c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"h