thor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161816721?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Meriem-BenIsmail","id":161816721,"login":"Meriem-BenIsmail","node_id":"U_kgDOCaUgkQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meriem-BenIsmail","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/1fab236f4326388b363f7467d814bdc105581b73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:48:10Z","email":"161816721+Meriem-BenIsmail@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meriem Ben Ismail"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:48:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Implement view only mode  (#19707)\n\n<!--\nThanks for contributing to JupyterLab!\nPlease fill out the following items to submit a pull request.\nSee the contributing guidelines for more information:\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n## References\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/issues/18369\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/issues/3251\n<!-- Note issue numbers this pull request addresses (should be at least\none, see contributing guidelines above). -->\n\n<!-- Note any other pull requests that address this issue and how this\npull request is different. -->\n\n## Code changes\n\nThis PR adds view-only behavior for notebooks that are not writable.\n\n- `Context` now sets `model.readOnly` from the server-reported\n`contentsModel.writable`. `NotebookPanel`/`Notebook` derive their own\n`viewOnly` state from it and cascade it to all cells, including ones\ninserted later — so the behavior lives in the widgets themselves rather\nthan only in `notebook-extension`.\n- `notebook-extension`''s `isViewOnly()` helper reads the widget''s own\n`viewOnly` state and is used across notebook commands (running,\ninserting/deleting/cutting/pasting/merging/splitting cells, changing\ncell type, collapsing code/output, trust, kernel operations, undo/redo,\nand more) to block operations that modify the notebook or its kernel\nstate. These commands are also hidden from the command palette and menus\nin view-only mode, not just disabled.\n- The Notebook Tools (Property Inspector) sidebar is now also protected:\nmetadata fields (tags, editable/deletable, slideshow type, raw metadata\nJSON) reject edits and render as disabled instead of silently discarding\nchanges.\n\n<!-- Describe the code changes and how they address the issue. -->\n\n## User-facing changes\nOpening a non-writable notebook now presents it as view-only.\n\nUsers can:\n\n- Scroll through the notebook\n- Select cells\n- Select and copy text\n- Copy cells\n- Search the notebook\n\nUsers cannot:\n\n- Edit cell contents\n- Add, delete, move, split, or merge cells\n- Cut or paste cells\n- Change cell types\n- Undo or redo changes\n- Execute cells\n- Interrupt or restart the kernel\n- Switch kernels\n\nEditing-related notebook UI is also hidden while in view-only mode.\n\n\n<!-- Describe any visual or user interaction changes and how they\naddress the issue. -->\n\n<!-- For visual changes, include before and after screenshots or\nGIF/mp4/other video demo here. -->\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\nNone.\n<!-- Describe any backwards-incompatible changes to JupyterLab public\nAPIs. -->\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **<!-- YES -->YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was\ngenerated by AI.\n- **<!-- YES -->YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR\nand run this code (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: claude-sonnet-5 <!-- FILL IN -->","tree":{"sha":"359ff88ddbc45c9e3c6943f6ba67a609641f0d1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/359ff88ddbc45c9e3c6943f6ba67a609641f0d1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/1fab236f4326388b363f7467d814bdc105581b73","verification":{"payload":"tree 359ff88ddbc45c9e3c6943f6ba67a609641f0d1d\nparent 9d200e662edc3e6f7b0f85f9d8188912d120e6ff\nauthor Meriem Ben Ismail <161816721+Meriem-BenIsmail@users.noreply.github.com> 1791460090 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791460090 +0200\n\nImplement view only mode  (#19707)\n\n<!--\nThanks for contributing to JupyterLab!\nPlease fill out the following items to submit a pull request.\nSee the contributing guidelines for more information:\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n## References\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/issues/18369\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/issues/3251\n<!-- Note issue numbers this pull request addresses (should be at least\none, see contributing guidelines above). -->\n\n<!-- Note any other pull requests that address this issue and how this\npull request is different. -->\n\n## Code changes\n\nThis PR adds view-only behavior for notebooks that are not writable.\n\n- `Context` now sets `model.readOnly` from the server-reported\n`contentsModel.writable`. `NotebookPanel`/`Notebook` derive their own\n`viewOnly` state from it and cascade it to all cells, including ones\ninserted later — so the behavior lives in the widgets themselves rather\nthan only in `notebook-extension`.\n- `notebook-extension`''s `isViewOnly()` helper reads the widget''s own\n`viewOnly` state and is used across notebook commands (running,\ninserting/deleting/cutting/pasting/merging/splitting cells, changing\ncell type, collapsing code/output, trust, kernel operations, undo/redo,\nand more) to block operations that modify the notebook or its kernel\nstate. These commands are also hidden from the command palette and menus\nin view-only mode, not just disabled.\n- The Notebook Tools (Property Inspector) sidebar is now also protected:\nmetadata fields (tags, editable/deletable, slideshow type, raw metadata\nJSON) reject edits and render as disabled instead of silently discarding\nchanges.\n\n<!-- Describe the code changes and how they address the issue. -->\n\n## User-facing changes\nOpening a non-writable notebook now presents it as view-only.\n\nUsers can:\n\n- Scroll through the notebook\n- Select cells\n- Select and copy text\n- Copy cells\n- Search the notebook\n\nUsers cannot:\n\n- Edit cell contents\n- Add, delete, move, split, or merge cells\n- Cut or paste cells\n- Change cell types\n- Undo or redo changes\n- Execute cells\n- Interrupt or restart the kernel\n- Switch kernels\n\nEditing-related notebook UI is also hidden while in view-only mode.\n\n\n<!-- Describe any visual or user interaction changes and how they\naddress the issue. -->\n\n<!-- For visual changes, include before and after screenshots or\nGIF/mp4/other video demo here. -->\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\nNone.\n<!-- Describe any backwards-incompatible changes to JupyterLab public\nAPIs. -->\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **<!-- YES -->YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was\ngenerated by AI.\n- **<!-- YES -->YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR\nand run this code (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: claude-sonnet-5 <!-- FILL IN -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx4L6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArhAQAKoYfYz6vlOOOPhv0RFIKAMS\nDSnqb6AhNzMR2D1vkWDhvnwsj952VU4qZTE