30dc931d0be878333ff67505e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/2cb664805ccd6630dc931d0be878333ff67505e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5832902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/krassowski","id":5832902,"login":"krassowski","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MzI5MDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/9bf52205c6cae8f91f4ed42f79ed88a712ea5b1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:24:18Z","email":"5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Michał Krassowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T11:24:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Further harden the new galata update workflow (#19946)\n\n## References\n\n- Follows #18896, which hardened this workflow''s expression handling.\n- Fixes #18623\n- Closes #18802 (supersedes), which filtered by head commit but kept the\nfilter client side.\n\n\n## Code changes\n\n- Restricts the snapshot unpacker to the snapshot directories, refusing\nany destination that resolves outside the checkout once symlinks are\nfollowed.\n- Moves the artifact download, the unpacker and `optipng` into a job\nthat holds no bot token, and which only passes on the snapshot files it\ncollected.\n- Re-checks the allowlist and the resolved destination in the job that\ndoes hold the token, before anything reaches the checkout.\n- Disables Git hooks for both jobs, because `--no-verify` covers neither\n`post-checkout` nor `post-commit`.\n- Asks the API for the head commit''s test asset runs instead of\nfiltering the twenty most recent runs locally, which matched a branch\nname that two forks can share and missed the run once twenty other\ngalata.yml runs had completed.\n- Checks out one commit in both jobs, resolved once the artifact is in\nhand, so the snapshot commit still fast-forwards the branch.\n- Looks up and opens the snapshot PR through the API by its\n`galata-snapshots-bot:<branch>` head, and on a repeat request rewrites\nthe body to name the commit the new snapshots came from.\n- Caps the artifact wait inside the job timeout.\n- Lets a new request cancel the run in flight on the same pull request.\nOther comments, the bot''s own replies included, do not cancel it, and a\ncancelled run does not reply.\n- Adds tests for the destinations the unpacker refuses.\n\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {\"themeVariables\": {\"fontSize\": \"12px\"}, \"flowchart\": {\"nodeSpacing\": 10, \"rankSpacing\": 14, \"padding\": 6, \"wrappingWidth\": 360}}}%%\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph before[\"Before: main\"]\n    direction TB\n    b1[\"Request: runs in parallel\"] --> b2[\"get-snapshot-updates: last 20 runs, by branch\"]\n    b2 --> b3[\"create-branch (bot token): unpacks, no path checks\"]\n    b3 --> b4[\"open-pr\"] --> b5[\"comment-back: replies after a cancel\"]\n  end\n  subgraph after[\"After: #19946\"]\n    direction TB\n    a1[\"Request: replaces the run in flight\"] --> a2[\"get-snapshot-updates: run by head SHA\"]\n    a2 --> a3[\"prepare-snapshots (no token): unpacks to *-snapshots/ only\"]\n    a3 --> a4[\"create-branch (bot token): re-checks paths, no symlinks\"]\n    a4 --> a5[\"open-pr: names the source commit\"] --> a6[\"comment-back: silent after a cancel\"]\n  end\n  before ~~~ after\n  classDef risk stroke:#d73a49,stroke-width:3px\n  classDef new stroke:#28a745,stroke-width:3px\n  class b3 risk\n  class a3 new\n```\n\nRed: the job that unpacked the PR''s files while holding the bot token.\nGreen: the new job that unpacks them without the token.\n\n\n## Developer-facing changes\n\n### Before\n\nSnapshots could come from an earlier run on the same branch instead of\nthe head commit, and the run was not found at all once twenty newer UI\ntest runs had completed. A request made before the UI tests finished hit\nthe 20-minute job timeout, and the bot then reported a failure while\npreparing or pushing the update branch.\n\nTwo requests on one pull request could run side by side, and each\nreplied. The snapshot PR did not say which commit its images came from.\n\n### After\n\nOnly the head commit''s own run is used, and it is found however long ago\nit ran. If the head commit''s UI tests do not finish within 18 minutes,\nthe bot says it found no test assets. A new request replaces the run in\nflight on the same pull request, and only the new run replies. The\nsnapshot PR names the commit its images came from, and a repeat request\nupdates that line.\n\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **Yes**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **Yes**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Opus 5, Opus 5.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a6eea86047e28215125087e0cec0bc5bd418c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/4a6eea86047e28215125087e0cec0bc5bd418c28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/9bf52205c6cae8f91f4ed42f79ed88a712ea5b1e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a6eea86047e28215125087e0cec0bc5bd418c28\nparent 2106fe1021db04bd5e47ade0868375bcca885def\nauthor Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com> 1791285858 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791285858 +0100\n\nFurther harden the new galata update workflow (#19946)\n\n## References\n\n- Follows #18896, which hardened this workflow''s expression handling.\n- Fixes #18623\n- Closes #18802 (supersedes), which filtered by head commit but kept the\nfilter client side.\n\n\n## Code changes\n\n- Restricts the snapshot unpacker to the snapshot directories, refusing\nany destination that resolves outside the checkout once symlinks are\nfollowed.\n- Moves the artifact download, the unpacker and `optipng` into a job\nthat holds no bot token, and which only passes on the snapshot files it\ncollected.\n- Re-checks the allowlist and the resolved destination in the job that\ndoes hold the token, before anything reaches the checkout.\n- Disables Git hooks for both jobs, because `--no-verify` covers neither\n`post-checkout` nor `post-commit`.\n- Asks the API for the head commit''s test asset runs instead of\nfiltering the twenty most recent runs locally, which matched a branch\nname that two forks can share and missed the run once twenty other\ngalata.yml runs had completed.\n- Checks out one commit in both jobs, resolved once the artifact is in\nhand, so the snapshot commit still fast-forwards the branch.\n- Looks up and opens the snapshot PR through the API by its\n`galata-snapshots-bot:<branch>` head, and on a repeat request rewrites\nthe body to name the commit the new snapshots came from.\n- Caps the artifact wait inside the job timeout.\n- Lets a new request cancel the run in flight on the same pull request.\nOther comments, the bot''s own replies included, do not cancel it, and a\ncancelled run does not reply.\n- Adds tests for the destinations the unpacker refuses.\n\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {\"themeVariables\": {\"fontSize\": \"12px\"}, \"flowchart\": {\"nodeSpacing\": 10, \"rankSpacing\": 14, \"padding\": 6, \"wrappingWidth\": 360}}}%%\nflowchart LR\n  subgraph before[\"Before: main\"]\n    direction TB\n    b1[\"Request: runs in parallel\"] --> b2[\"get-snapshot-updates: last 20 runs, by branch\"]\n    b2 --> b3[\"create-branch (bot token): unpacks, no path checks\"]\n    b3 --> b4[\"open-pr\"] --> b5[\"comment-back: replies after a cancel\"]\n  end\n  subgraph after[\"After: #19946\"]\n    direction TB\n    a1[\"Request: replaces the run in flight\"] --> a2[\"get-snapshot-updates: run by head SHA\"]\n    a2 --> a3[\"prepare-snapshots (no token): unpacks to *-snapshots/ only\"]\n    a3 --> a4[\"create-branch (bot token): re-checks paths, no symlinks\"]\n    a4 --> a5[\"open-pr: names the source commit\"] --> a6[\"comment-back: silent after a cancel\"]\n  end\n  before ~~~ after\n  classDef risk stroke:#d73a49,stroke-width:3px\n  classDef new stroke:#28a745,stroke-width:3px\n  class b3 risk\n  class a3 new\n```\n\nRed: the job that unpacked the PR''s files while holding the bot token.\nGreen: the new job that unpacks them without the token.\n\n\n## Developer-facing changes\n\n### Before\n\nSnapshots could come from an earlier run on the same branch instead of\nthe head commit, and the run was not found at all once twenty newer UI\ntest runs had completed. A request made before the UI tests finished hit\nthe 20-minute job timeout, and the bot then reported a failure while\npreparing or pushing the update branch.\n\nTwo requests on one pull request could run side by side, and each\nreplied. The snapshot PR did not say which commit its images came from.\n\n### After\n\nOnly the head commit''s own run is used, and it is found however long ago\nit ran. If the head commit''s UI tests do not finish within 18 minutes,\nthe bot says it found no test assets. A new request replaces the run in\nflight on the same pull request, and only the new run replies. The\nsnapshot PR names the commit its images came from, and a repeat request\nupdates that line.\n\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **Yes**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **Yes**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Opus 5, Opus 5.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNpiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9soQAA78mYGBhCDmoG4+iqDr7iD/\ndDKMMlkE2oGnwwhEgqcBj9F1i/PHuzqEyVP5JoVJTeOt7nVGkzdqwGU+RmJAC4DK\nQblDWTljJYs1iWWxLBx8xx5aZnTsglQEclvcNbCmzSZy9lrsIlbzpLQUbmGXfpH9\njafOCd22x2PgLlIJc985vbM/Y2c3zpiN4Y+/yyykXgUXBLP6Pimem0KV+YSadYPM\ntBNjtg8Ui27VgPS7pNtStSY1B1/mH1zxxncXKAT8lSNE5/z/JyDOzqG6D/GnKjqE\ncWF2vdznWXhQsluV48qNcZHIJ8kVR+fvEhkU/l/lptFRD8qWjfWcOCXj2xuzOZHR\nP4sJgD02qjuUjz8rbIuK2zW7XIaOlhMZ9t42viBsGk81TQ476RDLeTLuF+hm5spB\nUeMOx6GIl33yV5+XtRyVcgJPdeJ5Bv8aMsbv4bz7vFe/UdjeHKtVQsDyCz4T/KNO\nvl9eqMGb0wGN5y7A6t9Xu2TQUTsyYV+BjltSWyfDqaKy/wEG9y49Js77Sz4ed3Lo\nnoNmyHMsgLhmOnoonbC3Ah+zE5uS9AOgbuoVei9VG9NmVUoSgVsBvAPOoL0KCsHP\nuFgBKBsVi6GgHxt3thino7ysVWX+B+rdeyMOoB5BBGaCXYzaYKUEMZIXHn92qFx+\nb7d9nj6MF0rNFtSHypz8\n=63cI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T11:24:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin"