.com/users/pjdoland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pjdoland","id":924350,"login":"pjdoland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNDM1MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/8a520d00cce4076972fccbcbd91d01954340eedf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:51:44Z","email":"pjdoland@users.noreply.github.com","name":"PJ Doland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:51:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Do not display kernel sources once the debugger has stopped (#19962)\n\n## References\n\nFollow-up to the review of #19937.\n\n## Code changes\n\n`_applyKernelSources` runs after the `modules` request and a 500 ms\ndebounce, so a debugger stopped in between had the list that `stop()`\ncleared filled again. It now checks that the debugger is still started,\nlike `displayModules`, and `stop()` cancels a pending display, which\ncovers a restart within the debounce. Unit tests cover a stop, a reply\nreceived after the stop, and a restart.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nRun a cell with the debugger on, then stop the debugger straight away.\nKernel Sources a couple of seconds later:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img width=\"250\" alt=\"Kernel Sources before: the list is filled again\nafter the debugger stopped\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b2cf9b98-ca7b-491d-b396-e4859f28430c\"\n/> | <img width=\"250\" alt=\"Kernel Sources after: the list stays empty\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebbe3f28-71b3-4e11-8950-88afec2af9f0\"\n/> |\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)","tree":{"sha":"12066e37180637681dacb88c071959aeea829591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/12066e37180637681dacb88c071959aeea829591"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/8a520d00cce4076972fccbcbd91d01954340eedf","verification":{"payload":"tree 12066e37180637681dacb88c071959aeea829591\nparent 5e954ff77f890dfad24b5c89ada7fb6708ca301a\nauthor PJ Doland <pjdoland@users.noreply.github.com> 1790855504 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790855504 +0100\n\nDo not display kernel sources once the debugger has stopped (#19962)\n\n## References\n\nFollow-up to the review of #19937.\n\n## Code changes\n\n`_applyKernelSources` runs after the `modules` request and a 500 ms\ndebounce, so a debugger stopped in between had the list that `stop()`\ncleared filled again. It now checks that the debugger is still started,\nlike `displayModules`, and `stop()` cancels a pending display, which\ncovers a restart within the debounce. Unit tests cover a stop, a reply\nreceived after the stop, and a restart.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nRun a cell with the debugger on, then stop the debugger straight away.\nKernel Sources a couple of seconds later:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img width=\"250\" alt=\"Kernel Sources before: the list is filled again\nafter the debugger stopped\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b2cf9b98-ca7b-491d-b396-e4859f28430c\"\n/> | <img width=\"250\" alt=\"Kernel Sources after: the list stays empty\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebbe3f28-71b3-4e11-8950-88afec2af9f0\"\n/> |\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvklQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO6AQAD/lOdXXCoW0Z0z0djJ9FDNz\nUaOgcloKqGXwx0tlLVSPZ+ehE4XxW4iZ57R4Bbp7m0h85wnoEocfp2L6z0n1b2lj\n4sQZ7ZwUZ1Pzbxt4hiIzBjgO0OmSWmDNTqtlWtGmiIdwG7oP5kB6j/MZyg1NKLYd\n+Oth/8xk68xOR0nTfoq1xOdy//pm6V3mFlA+lzInyR6gnPi19q349AlBdxToa1Pc\ndDupZ8upFboO50xX/JiHi84xvHXd6yJRJodVlTJN9e/p2ObSOYjwowvAr58Q/6EH\ngCJtuRGJvKtZrrdCbPyNKvMEFYRzBOAD1G/8bx5PoHD3TgCqq9asE9in+VbfOS48\nAewfV6XQq1g9w+feouJ/omMbGhlUMqujJcsYwXe42THRdoJV+B3n6Q16Qbov92Th\nXQOraI26krdf/bVoMPtJyvQHtZVYCAHGcrpQs/15Lo2ZmgK8ExHFNleNRYh0V5d+\nMYUGbiUoFUiHyxDb0ivMuxDnjeZs7O24cgzidazdN8cGAFDZ2zjLDZlGn8r6C+m6\nKZ37thES2+zETgb2IIkH3ZWm19rsM4uFd49af+yg+IBeFmAUiIk6YoruAHvREL0m\n6sLJp4HF3qi4mJnsdhC8pDWNcqQg7yEi5NowGZFfxAec9x71O8DRMKCsvsdaxIxF\nbfGckCR9pvvQvSSkaxsh\n=zNCZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T11:51:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_u