c1ZjBmYmUyMTc3MDY1MDZmYWMxN2MxYjkzYzUwNGZiNWJhN2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/ca6acfbe41bbc11c4f5ff93db001fc69d66dc17b","sha":"ca6acfbe41bbc11c4f5ff93db001fc69d66dc17b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/ca6acfbe41bbc11c4f5ff93db001fc69d66dc17b"}],"sha":"15f75f0fbe217706506fac17c1b93c504fb5ba7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/15f75f0fbe217706506fac17c1b93c504fb5ba7b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/924350?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pjdoland","id":924350,"login":"pjdoland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNDM1MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/ca6acfbe41bbc11c4f5ff93db001fc69d66dc17b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:32:21Z","email":"pjdoland@users.noreply.github.com","name":"PJ Doland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:32:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stabilize the metadata form UI tests (#19944)\n\n## References\n\nFrom the flakiness reports in #19153 (three `metadataform.test.ts`\ntests).\n\n## Code changes\n\nTest-only. The metadata form tests now open the notebook without a\nkernel (@krassowski''s commit) and wait for the form fields to render\nbefore reading metadata. A kernel writes `language_info` when it\nconnects, which rebuilds the form, and the form writes its default\nvalues only once rendered; both made the direct metadata reads race. The\nearlier `expect.poll` changes are gone.\n\nLocally on macOS, `main` fails the three tests on every run with one\nworker. With this branch the file passed 120 of 120 in Chromium with one\nand with two workers, and 60 of 60 in Firefox, and it runs about 10%\nfaster (0.53 against 0.60 minutes per repeat of the file with one\nworker).\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nNone.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"653884c960f951b1dfcab7cfe04492f831c411cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/653884c960f951b1dfcab7cfe04492f831c411cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/ca6acfbe41bbc11c4f5ff93db001fc69d66dc17b","verification":{"payload":"tree 653884c960f951b1dfcab7cfe04492f831c411cb\nparent 62189d4224cb17ad3e49aedfa605c3ed2530c594\nauthor PJ Doland <pjdoland@users.noreply.github.com> 1790775141 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790775141 +0100\n\nStabilize the metadata form UI tests (#19944)\n\n## References\n\nFrom the flakiness reports in #19153 (three `metadataform.test.ts`\ntests).\n\n## Code changes\n\nTest-only. The metadata form tests now open the notebook without a\nkernel (@krassowski''s commit) and wait for the form fields to render\nbefore reading metadata. A kernel writes `language_info` when it\nconnects, which rebuilds the form, and the form writes its default\nvalues only once rendered; both made the direct metadata reads race. The\nearlier `expect.poll` changes are gone.\n\nLocally on macOS, `main` fails the three tests on every run with one\nworker. With this branch the file passed 120 of 120 in Chromium with one\nand with two workers, and 60 of 60 in Firefox, and it runs about 10%\nfaster (0.53 against 0.60 minutes per repeat of the file with one\nworker).\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nNone.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvQ9lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcwwQAGze/qo+nvPGhUkkWFiVytp+\nJVs03ii6H834KnhETJUr6w/djCZe+J3lda9tOz1fZOZ63h5xwZbMjKGN3xsK/F1c\nXzbtn9bbz5UTsO3WDE27+zLEecsS/NMSHWqI0yTJE4QOeaq+sYTlulAWzA9Bw3nB\nqmI47RVs1ewBFSGkxswUMvdE/uybYJYDknqxIG7i1WX1eYJHcgnGR/a7i0p9II+w\n5U6WVaQ+aIlNtwi9qH8r8B1e+d2xdH2mPWav4VLrTf/wLi0mee+Zi+JIHOGb1+m6\naslFQUVeeKp0khDaVZsEFh2QdBzviHGDd8l58rqj8npn7lyq5imTXqVggT79rj6d\nKv6ajIQW6JVG7t/9C6K6vFRsjjubOdJlLR8+RMl4IQooJ3WwaFOGldBM2R2uIv+y\nqKDEYWsmSYRgNN77qRDED8jcMkKxljBAmFGQ90cCKATT4UgNjwvWTpjkX8mEFjN+\n4rdQmXpUFaCKQLNtKYDe6NwJ1OF2fgZDDf6sbgp9y8vEnI4JeUfgiy6eP5jN3QPU\nuJcPnvXC98ICSSiH3x6qoWuNpAxkd581wbaLKpZxv6nVWOVQKIs556OVvu7v9dm4\nzfu9MEC7o2zYrux+pYPpqcJzWd3pgf19EmcxgANw9LtEjvO/sEbO7OZk/BHZuN4P\nv2VJU9nHY6/AcccZDiCA\n=aE1W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:32:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","