s/pjdoland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pjdoland","id":924350,"login":"pjdoland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyNDM1MA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pjdoland","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/5c883bd6a541de57850b1eecdeac89eb003ecf1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:41:54Z","email":"pjdoland@users.noreply.github.com","name":"PJ Doland"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T09:41:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Do not request kernel sources when the debugger is not started (#19937)\n\n## References\n\nFixes #19936\n\nFollow-up to #18081 (4.6.0), whose automatic Kernel Sources refresh is a\nnice improvement. This only keeps it from running when no debugger\nsession is started. It would be good to have in 4.6.x as well.\n\n## Code changes\n\n`DebuggerService.displayModules()` now returns early unless the debugger\nis started (`!this.session?.isStarted`), instead of throwing \"No active\ndebugger session\". This is the same guard `updateBreakpoints`,\n`pauseOnExceptions` and `pauseOnExceptionsFilter` use. The\n`IDebugger.displayModules` docstring says so.\n\nSince #18081, `debugger-extension` connects\n`DebuggerHandler.executionDone`, which fires on every `execute_reply`\nfor every widget, directly to `displayModules`. So:\n\n- with only kernels without debugger support open, there is no session\nand every cell run ended in an unhandled rejection;\n- with a debug-capable kernel and the debugger off, every run sent a\n`modules` request and refilled the Kernel Sources model that stopping\nthe debugger clears.\n\nWhile the debugger is started nothing changes: the other callers (start\nand restore in `handler.ts`) only call it once started.\n\nI put the guard in the service rather than in the extension''s\n`executionDone` connections so it also covers any other caller.\n`executionDone` itself is unchanged; its spec covers emitting on every\nexecution. If you would prefer the check elsewhere, for example in the\nhandler before emitting, I am happy to move it.\n\nTests:\n\n- `service.spec.ts`: `displayModules` resolves quietly without a\nsession, sends nothing before the debugger is started or after it is\nstopped, and still requests and displays the modules once started.\n- `galata/test/jupyterlab/debugger.test.ts`: marks every kernelspec\n`debugger: false` through a route on `/api/kernelspecs`, runs a cell,\nand checks that no page error was raised.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\n- No \"No active debugger session\" error in the console when running\ncells with kernels that do not support the debugger.\n- While the debugger is off, Kernel Sources no longer refreshes after\neach execution. It refreshes when the debugger starts and after each\nexecution while it runs, as before.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone. `displayModules()` resolves instead of rejecting when there is no\nstarted session.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll local, on macOS 27.0 with Chromium 151, against `main` at bb166a7.\n\n- **jest** (`packages/debugger`): 5 suites, 70 passed, 2 skipped\n(skipped on `main` too).\n- Without the change to `service.ts`, the two new \"not started\" tests\nfail and the \"started\" test passes.\n- The \"started\" test fails, as it should, when the fetched modules are\nnot applied to the model.\n- **Galata, new test**: fails 5 of 5 without the fix (each time on \"No\nactive debugger session\"), passes 10 of 10 with it.\n- **Galata, the whole `debugger.test.ts`**: 13 of 13 on two consecutive\nruns with the fix, including \"Kernel Sources panel updates after\nexecute_reply\" from #18081.\n- The repository only keeps Linux screenshots, so I generated macOS\nbaselines locally and did not commit them.\n- The build without the fix matches those baselines too (only the new\ntest fails there), so the change does not alter those screens.\n- **Flakiness seen**:\n- The \"Debugger Variables\" tests time out now and then whether or not\nthe fix is applied: 58 of 60 passed with it and 37 of 40 without it,\nover several repeated runs. The timeouts were in \"Copy to globals\",\n\"Copy to clipboard\" and \"Kernel Sources panel updates after\nexecute_reply\".\n- In those tests the debugger is started before any cell runs, so the\nfix takes the same path as `main` there.\n- **Manual Playwright scenarios** on a second server with a real\n`\"debugger\": false` kernelspec, all sessions shut down between\nscenarios:\n\n  | Scenario | Before | After |\n  | --- | --- | --- |\n| Notebook on a kernel without debugger support, alone on the page | \"No\nactive debugger session\" | no error, no `modules` request |\n  | Console on that kernel | \"No active debugger session\" | no error |\n| `python3` open with the debugger off, then run in the other kernel |\n`modules` request sent | none |\n| `python3`, debugger off, run a cell | `modules` request sent | none |\n| `python3`, debugger on, run a cell | Kernel Sources refreshed | same |\n| Debugger on in `python3`, run a cell in the other kernel | `modules`\nrequest sent | same |\n  | Debugger on, then off, run a cell | no request | same |\n| Debugger on, cell raises an error | refreshed, no page error | same |\n  | Debugger on, page reloaded, run a cell | refreshed | same |\n\n- **A kernel from outside JupyterLab**: the Chatbook kernel from\nnotebook-intelligence 6.1.0 (which does not declare debugger support) on\nthis branch runs a cell with no page error.\n\nNot changed here, and already the case on `main`:\n\n- A `modules` request from a started session can still reject unhandled,\nfor example if the debugged kernel was shut down or does not implement\n`modules`.\n- A refresh that is in flight or debounced when the debugger stops can\nstill fill the cleared model.","tree":{"sha":"137de6bfa8ee086f996a6b7178ab17a1ac4b1bb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/137de6bfa8ee086f996a6b7178ab17a1ac4b1bb8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/5c883bd6a541de57850b1eecdeac89eb003ecf1d","verification":{"payload":"tree 137de6bfa8ee086f996a6b7178ab17a1ac4b1bb8\nparent 463fa674984f9a72dd29c30e25c134ed5ffbf965\nauthor PJ Doland <pjdoland@users.noreply.github.com> 1790761314 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790761314 +0100\n\nDo not request kernel sources when the debugger is not started (#19937)\n\n## References\n\nFixes #19936\n\nFollow-up to #18081 (4.6.0), whose automatic Kernel Sources refresh is a\nnice improvement. This only keeps it from running when no debugger\nsession is started. It would be good to have in 4.6.x as well.\n\n## Code changes\n\n`DebuggerService.displayModules()` now returns early unless the debugger\nis started (`!this.session?.isStarted`), instead of throwing \"No active\ndebugger session\". This is the same guard `updateBreakpoints`,\n`pauseOnExceptions` and `pauseOnExceptionsFilter` use. The\n`IDebugger.displayModules` docstring says so.\n\nSince #18081, `debugger-extension` connects\n`DebuggerHandler.executionDone`, which fires on every `execute_reply`\nfor every widget, directly to `displayModules`. So:\n\n- with only kernels without debugger support open, there is no session\nand every cell run ended in an unhandled rejection;\n- with a debug-capable kernel and the debugger off, every run sent a\n`modules` request and refilled the Kernel Sources model that stopping\nthe debugger clears.\n\nWhile the debugger is started nothing changes: the other callers (start\nand restore in `handler.ts`) only call it once started.\n\nI put the guard in the service rather than in the extension''s\n`executionDone` connections so it also covers any other caller.\n`executionDone` itself is unchanged; its spec covers emitting on every\nexecution. If you would prefer the check elsewhere, for example in the\nhandler before emitting, I am happy to move it.\n\nTests:\n\n- `service.spec.ts`: `displayModules` resolves quietly without a\nsession, sends nothing before the debugger is started or after it is\nstopped, and still requests and displays the modules once started.\n- `galata/test/jupyterlab/debugger.test.ts`: marks every kernelspec\n`debugger: false` through a route on `/api/kernelspecs`, runs a cell,\nand checks that no page error was raised.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\n- No \"No active debugger session\" error in the console when running\ncells with kernels that do not support the debugger.\n- While the debugger is off, Kernel Sources no longer refreshes after\neach execution. It refreshes when the debugger starts and after each\nexecution while it runs, as before.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone. `displayModules()` resolves instead of rejecting when there is no\nstarted session.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)\n\n## Testing\n\nAll local, on macOS 27.0 with Chromium 151, against `main` at bb166a7.\n\n- **jest** (`packages/debugger`): 5 suites, 70 passed, 2 skipped\n(skipped on `main` too).\n- Without the change to `service.ts`, the two new \"not started\" tests\nfail and the \"started\" test passes.\n- The \"started\" test fails, as it should, when the fetched modules are\nnot applied to the model.\n- **Galata, new test**: fails 5 of 5 without the fix (each time on \"No\nactive debugger session\"), passes 10 of 10 with it.\n- **Galata, the whole `debugger.test.ts`**: 13 of 13 on two consecutive\nruns with the fix, including \"Kernel Sources panel updates after\nexecute_reply\" from #18081.\n- The repository only keeps Linux screenshots, so I generated macOS\nbaselines locally and did not commit them.\n- The build without the fix matches those baselines too (only the new\ntest fails there), so the change does not alter those screens.\n- **Flakiness seen**:\n- The \"Debugger Variables\" tests time out now and then whether or not\nthe fix is applied: 58 of 60 passed with it and 37 of 40 without it,\nover several repeated runs. The timeouts were in \"Copy to globals\",\n\"Copy to clipboard\" and \"Kernel Sources panel updates after\nexecute_reply\".\n- In those tests the debugger is started before any cell runs, so the\nfix takes the same path as `main` there.\n- **Manual Playwright scenarios** on a second server with a real\n`\"debugger\": false` kernelspec, all sessions shut down between\nscenarios:\n\n  | Scenario | Before | After |\n  | --- | --- | --- |\n| Notebook on a kernel without debugger support, alone on the page | \"No\nactive debugger session\" | no error, no `modules` request |\n  | Console on that kernel | \"No active debugger session\" | no error |\n| `python3` open with the debugger off, then run in the other kernel |\n`modules` request sent | none |\n| `python3`, debugger off, run a cell | `modules` request sent | none |\n| `python3`, debugger on, run a cell | Kernel Sources refreshed | same |\n| Debugger on in `python3`, run a cell in the other kernel | `modules`\nrequest sent | same |\n  | Debugger on, then off, run a cell | no request | same |\n| Debugger on, cell raises an error | refreshed, no page error | same |\n  | Debugger on, page reloaded, run a cell | refreshed | same |\n\n- **A kernel from outside JupyterLab**: the Chatbook kernel from\nnotebook-intelligence 6.1.0 (which does not declare debugger support) on\nthis branch runs a cell with no page error.\n\nNot changed here, and already the case on `main`:\n\n- A `modules` request from a started session can still reject unhandled,\nfor example if the debugged kernel was shut down or does not implement\n`modules`.\n- A refresh that is in flight or debounced when the debugger stops can\nstill fill the cleared model.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvNliCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwt4QAFQuwymkJHB7HD7kmRRziFY8\nI9CyIlXfYr+0lczGu1F/RQbYJx8W8VGOmXbv3NuGx3a2eCdjn+SQw9aE2PkMX2PR\nhkbHIYzAwksq+tSnn2EDdQE+7y93EycsG2+yWCp430Ak1oZRmCRRlSsRGsRYwPs7\n1iLsnfPynEtele8gOYiV8mwHSLIK8A08akXv1gquNR85+JZx8ViS6Z/mQSQd7zah\n0iJ/h5ojQnmxHsdrKT0rKHc2AEqPJHWwLwOyS6SXAyLRPcd4e1eJp1WlEnsKCHUe\nYAf01mqT8LbiyqGb3i+KXdbMAIcKgRTSNNb0pF3EFlAPIx19GXhKX0KLgMLY0SzA\noeDshfM1XJSDP8tArZsxjlE+mzHKNOtpP25P9W8SS3wjlKRE2T2Ad+W2RTxc/oXM\nbrD/aGm746QuPbofvFJW5dGZZaqvSN7RWsUsOw8VRhVSOoyHzKKQ6OEcK2uwPPGf\nljUGHn7ulfihscwsm/ID5fEcYgAoIlfw/W4UooootsWaBH5RBdVv0v2tcUeadNAN\nMUTT5tivEBFpcOQmen8Nfvc0iVz4PNyhuIGM0wqVru58I/3j+YxRNLYpdhvJ/CDb\nV/3fr5rdUrayLc8SfhNU6Yv7vzOqmcbZlK+EszO/l5bHYlCkmCWXd+LnIOAQfvf2\nrUNQcXExCHtTQLSDGOON\n=BRee\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T09:41:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/5c883bd6a541de57850b1eecdeac89eb003ecf1d","node_id":"C_kwDOA5k_I9oAKDVjODgzYmQ2YTU0MWRlNTc4NTBiMWVlY2RlYWM4OWViMDAzZWNmMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/463fa674984f9a72dd29c30e25c134ed5ffbf965","sha":"463fa674984f9a72dd29c30e25c134ed5ffbf965","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/463fa674984f9a72dd29c30e25c134ed5ffbf965"}],"sha":"5c883bd6a541de57850b1eecdeac89eb003ecf1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/5c883bd6a541de57850b1eecdeac89eb003ecf1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/463fa674984f9a72dd29c30e25c134ed5ffbf965/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:19:24Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:19:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump colord from 2.9.3 to 2.10.0 (#19715)\n\nBumps [colord](https://github.com/omgovich/colord) from 2.9.3 to 2.10.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/omgovich/colord/releases\">colord''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.10 (RGB color mixing)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>mix</code>, <code>tints</code>, <code>shades</code> and\n<code>tones</code> (<code>mix</code> plugin) now accept an optional\ninterpolation color space. LAB stays the default; pass\n<code>&quot;rgb&quot;</code> to interpolate RGB channels instead — the\nway browsers and design tools (such as Figma) composite translucent\nlayers.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre lang=\"js\"><code>import { colord, extend } from &quot;colord&quot;;\nimport mixPlugin from &quot;colord/plugins/mix&quot;;\n<p>extend([mixPlugin]);</p>\n<p>colord(&quot;#ff0000&quot;).mix(&quot;#ffffff&quot;, 0.5,\n&quot;rgb&quot;).toHex(); // &quot;#ff8080&quot;\ncolord(&quot;#f0f3f1&quot;).mix(&quot;#007d40&quot;, 0.14,\n&quot;rgb&quot;).toHex(); // &quot;#cee2d8&quot; — same as compositing\nrgba(0, 125, 64, 0.14) over #f0f3f1\ncolord(&quot;#ff0000&quot;).tints(3, &quot;rgb&quot;).map((c) =&gt;\nc.toHex()); // [&quot;#ff0000&quot;, &quot;#ff8080&quot;,\n&quot;#ffffff&quot;]\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/omgovich/colord/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">colord''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h3>2.10.0</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Improve <code>mix</code> plugin by adding an optional\n<code>&quot;rgb&quot;</code> interpolation mode to <code>mix</code>,\n<code>tints</code>, <code>tones</code> and <code>shades</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.9.7</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Make HEX parsing and serialization more than 2x faster</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.9.6</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Rotate the unrounded hue so <code>rotate</code> and\n<code>harmonies</code> preserve the original color</li>\n<li>Fix: Normalize HWB whiteness + blackness over 100% to gray ❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/spokodev\"><code>@​spokodev</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.9.5</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Use adjusted chroma for the CIEDE2000 rotation term ❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maximilliangrand\"><code>@​maximilliangrand</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix: Keep the hue within <code>[0, 360)</code> in every color model\n❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sarathfrancis90\"><code>@​sarathfrancis90</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both fixes change returned numbers for a small set of colors;\n<code>toHex()</code> output is unchanged. Snapshots holding <code>h:\n360</code>, <code>&quot;hsl(360, …)&quot;</code> or a\n<code>delta()</code> value may need updating.</p>\n<h3>2.9.4</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Reject malformed color strings in linear time ❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GAP-dev\"><code>@​GAP-dev</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/omgovich/colord/commits/v2.10\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=colord&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=2.9.3&new-version=2.10.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"36f75af83dc40cfc6cb1135081492a52b87fe1fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/36f75af83dc40cfc6cb1135081492a52b87fe1fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/463fa674984f9a72dd29c30e25c134ed5ffbf965","verification":{"payload":"tree 36f75af83dc40cfc6cb1135081492a52b87fe1fd\nparent 6cff679a2d5fe8a02cd130f28e119a754dc8b898\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790673564 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790673564 +0100\n\nBump colord from 2.9.3 to 2.10.0 (#19715)\n\nBumps [colord](https://github.com/omgovich/colord) from 2.9.3 to 2.10.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/omgovich/colord/releases\">colord''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.10 (RGB color mixing)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>mix</code>, <code>tints</code>, <code>shades</code> and\n<code>tones</code> (<code>mix</code> plugin) now accept an optional\ninterpolation color space. LAB stays the default; pass\n<code>&quot;rgb&quot;</code> to interpolate RGB channels instead — the\nway browsers and design tools (such as Figma) composite translucent\nlayers.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre lang=\"js\"><code>import { colord, extend } from &quot;colord&quot;;\nimport mixPlugin from &quot;colord/plugins/mix&quot;;\n<p>extend([mixPlugin]);</p>\n<p>colord(&quot;#ff0000&quot;).mix(&quot;#ffffff&quot;, 0.5,\n&quot;rgb&quot;).toHex(); // &quot;#ff8080&quot;\ncolord(&quot;#f0f3f1&quot;).mix(&quot;#007d40&quot;, 0.14,\n&quot;rgb&quot;).toHex(); // &quot;#cee2d8&quot; — same as compositing\nrgba(0, 125, 64, 0.14) over #f0f3f1\ncolord(&quot;#ff0000&quot;).tints(3, &quot;rgb&quot;).map((c) =&gt;\nc.toHex()); // [&quot;#ff0000&quot;, &quot;#ff8080&quot;,\n&quot;#ffffff&quot;]\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/omgovich/colord/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">colord''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h3>2.10.0</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Improve <code>mix</code> plugin by adding an optional\n<code>&quot;rgb&quot;</code> interpolation mode to <code>mix</code>,\n<code>tints</code>, <code>tones</code> and <code>shades</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.9.7</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Make HEX parsing and serialization more than 2x faster</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.9.6</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Rotate the unrounded hue so <code>rotate</code> and\n<code>harmonies</code> preserve the original color</li>\n<li>Fix: Normalize HWB whiteness + blackness over 100% to gray ❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/spokodev\"><code>@​spokodev</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.9.5</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Use adjusted chroma for the CIEDE2000 rotation term ❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/maximilliangrand\"><code>@​maximilliangrand</code></a></li>\n<li>Fix: Keep the hue within <code>[0, 360)</code> in every color model\n❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sarathfrancis90\"><code>@​sarathfrancis90</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both fixes change returned numbers for a small set of colors;\n<code>toHex()</code> output is unchanged. Snapshots holding <code>h:\n360</code>, <code>&quot;hsl(360, …)&quot;</code> or a\n<code>delta()</code> value may need updating.</p>\n<h3>2.9.4</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix: Reject malformed color strings in linear time ❤️ <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/GAP-dev\"><code>@​GAP-dev</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/omgovich/colord/commits/v2.10\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=colord&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=2.9.3&new-version=2.10.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nt