api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MUFFANUJ","id":151390316,"login":"MUFFANUJ","node_id":"U_kgDOCQYIbA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/3daf43dac618ef494341b29d18c8095a70c11586/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:10:49Z","email":"anujsinghhero292@gmail.com","name":"ANUJ KUMAR SINGH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:10:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enable lazy import ESLint rule and bump Eslint version (#19751)\n\n## References\n\nEnables the `prefer-lazy-imports` rule from [jupyterlab/eslint-plugin\n`v1.3.0`](https://github.com/jupyterlab/eslint-plugin/releases/tag/v1.3.0).\n\n## Code changes\n\n- Bumps `@jupyter/eslint-plugin` to 1.3.0 and enables\n`jupyter/prefer-lazy-imports` as an error, off for test files.\n- Defers `@codemirror/search` to first use: the editor keymaps go\nthrough lazily loading `StateCommands`, and the file editor find and\ngo-to-line commands import it when run.\n- Defers `@rjsf/validator-ajv8` to the first metadata form or CodeMirror\nsettings form.\n- Loads the LSP settings renderer, the keyboard shortcuts UI and the\nactive cell tool with `React.lazy` on first render.\n- Keeps the startup imports of the running and log console plugins\nstatic with an inline disable, since their activation needs them at\nonce.\n- Moves `WORKSPACE_ITEM_CLASS` into a shared module instead of\nduplicating it.\n- Makes `jlpm integrity` count dynamic `import()` calls as imports,\ndrops the known-unused entries that only covered them, and declares\nthree dependencies that were used only through dynamic imports.\n- Documents lazy imports in the developer guide.\n- Translates the strings that the 1.3.0 `no-untranslated-string` rule\nreports, and disables the rule inline for file format names, the\nbenchmark report and a test settings schema\n- Uses `deferredPackages` to ensure this won''t regress\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nBefore: a cold load of the launcher page fetched the search, form\nvalidator, shortcuts UI, LSP settings and active cell tool code although\nnone of them is used until a panel or form opens.\n\nAfter: those load on first use. The keyboard shortcuts panel, the\nlanguage server settings and the notebook metadata form render one frame\nlater the first time they open.\n\nCold load of the launcher page, main at f41e1caa against this PR at\ne0a3abea, each build served from its own directory and measured in\nalternating rounds:\n\n| | main | this PR | difference |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| JavaScript fetched before `restored` | 5,354 KB in 133 requests |\n5,270 KB in 131 requests | 84 KB and 2 requests less (1.6%) |\n| time to `restored` at localhost, 20 runs | 894 ms | 873 ms | -22 ms\n(-114 to +47) |\n| time to `restored` at 10 Mbps with 50 ms latency, 12 runs | 5,520 ms |\n5,466 ms | -54 ms (-174 to +40) |\n| time to `restored` at Fast 3G (1.6 Mbit/s, 562 ms latency), 5 runs |\n34.2 s | 33.6 s | -0.5 s (-0.6 to -0.3) |\n| time to `restored` at Slow 3G (400 kbit/s, 2 s latency), 5 runs |\n131.1 s | 128.6 s | -2.5 s (-2.6 to -2.4) |\n\nThe last column is the difference of medians with a bootstrap 95%\ninterval. The user-facing impact is greater at slower connection speeds\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **Yes**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **Yes**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.4, Claude Fable 5.1\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"89ce94a12984a17976d8305f24bacce06af17181","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/89ce94a12984a17976d8305f24bacce06af17181"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/3daf43dac618ef494341b29d18c8095a70c11586","verification":{"payload":"tree 89ce94a12984a17976d8305f24bacce06af17181\nparent a62365d745fee48f7d59c60bda377a2ed14415a8\nauthor ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com> 1790514649 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790514649 +0100\n\nEnable lazy import ESLint rule and bump Eslint version (#19751)\n\n## References\n\nEnables the `prefer-lazy-imports` rule from [jupyterlab/eslint-plugin\n`v1.3.0`](https://github.com/jupyterlab/eslint-plugin/releases/tag/v1.3.0).\n\n## Code changes\n\n- Bumps `@jupyter/eslint-plugin` to 1.3.0 and enables\n`jupyter/prefer-lazy-imports` as an error, off for test files.\n- Defers `@codemirror/search` to first use: the editor keymaps go\nthrough lazily loading `StateCommands`, and the file editor find and\ngo-to-line commands import it when run.\n- Defers `@rjsf/validator-ajv8` to the first metadata form or CodeMirror\nsettings form.\n- Loads the LSP settings renderer, the keyboard shortcuts UI and the\nactive cell tool with `React.lazy` on first render.\n- Keeps the startup imports of the running and log console plugins\nstatic with an inline disable, since their activation needs them at\nonce.\n- Moves `WORKSPACE_ITEM_CLASS` into a shared module instead of\nduplicating it.\n- Makes `jlpm integrity` count dynamic `import()` calls as imports,\ndrops the known-unused entries that only covered them, and declares\nthree dependencies that were used only through dynamic imports.\n- Documents lazy imports in the developer guide.\n- Translates the strings that the 1.3.0 `no-untranslated-string` rule\nreports, and disables the rule inline for file format names, the\nbenchmark report and a test settings schema\n- Uses `deferredPackages` to ensure this won''t regress\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nBefore: a cold load of the launcher page fetched the search, form\nvalidator, shortcuts UI, LSP settings and active cell tool code although\nnone of them is used until a panel or form opens.\n\nAfter: those load on first use. The keyboard shortcuts panel, the\nlanguage server settings and the notebook metadata form render one frame\nlater the first time they open.\n\nCold load of the launcher page, main at f41e1caa against this PR at\ne0a3abea, each build served from its own directory and measured in\nalternating rounds:\n\n| | main | this PR | difference |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| JavaScript fetched before `restored` | 5,354 KB in 133 requests |\n5,270 KB in 131 requests | 84 KB and 2 requests less (1.6%) |\n| time to `restored` at localhost, 20 runs | 894 ms | 873 ms | -22 ms\n(-114 to +47) |\n| time to `restored` at 10 Mbps with 50 ms latency, 12 runs | 5,520 ms |\n5,466 ms | -54 ms (-174 to +40) |\n| time to `restored` at Fast 3G (1.6 Mbit/s, 562 ms latency), 5 runs |\n34.2 s | 33.6 s | -0.5 s (-0.6 to -0.3) |\n| time to `restored` at Slow 3G (400 kbit/s, 2 s latency), 5 runs |\n131.1 s | 128.6 s | -2.5 s (-2.6 to -2.4) |\n\nThe last column is the difference of medians with a bootstrap 95%\ninterval. The user-facing impact is greater at slower connection speeds\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **Yes**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **Yes**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.4, Claude Fable 5.1\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquRXZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuokQAHicVC+WY83OPSqX3XWLk8qj\nXE3hwKVWp7aBsGcHvVrGpu1V+UdLJCLHLEFjB9ImLb3jVszfycBh1CLI8p5P0rWH\nFFrmV7PfueX1PZvzhiPGVtz+uorfrso1ODcrGdOcY9CA1bMCJ3J+LHYmoEI84HDB\nB5IRWqBMvxQv7Pv3zjjjoSBMiCPs2xOyhnfRPhilNOwX13uBDsajR5fSkcl5hOz3\n1XSG66w8UU4r6tNLhqrZvgHHfgi0X1SCxnvC/rasTshKU+28ULdOWLgxpO/o8drd\nmXwjyBL76MdPhnMwmB9lWtO+auB5PKSlEbmtrYCwsCKD7fwcc/5mhonH/SgPVyKI\nQ5PFC7wFbjmHT6D1g5xLgsPL4Vv6nTtlsvbkLInlaW0xTSLABfvdf6zs+JQVQQzU\nYTfqJA/uoHEIzfIWa7xhgbFgjoP5tnkOrYTM6IwjflZgqSSKsH2qtbhkHBjJdVDj\nGMwQHrlP3CwlGgZDGA6rhl9PRf3+Sun4cv6bp6tD7Cf+OKtX07yFaqJ2JmHNAxbm\n8N3AMuSUvXPVFFN9sNcjgM88A7aKauBn3X/WEYxv4UMZ/y3sIglnzgwP836h4qIO\nExcAXnlSjRFcjzQoRQLSQ2LqSKFNr8FgxzJiiGLbMARoNUrnJBvmrUj56mpeT4E3\nPOUUkpNBfbwpCkU982As\n=KMfI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T13:10:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_ur