node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/f8d8b855be61dc887f05a0d94833af8829c1b215","node_id":"C_kwDOA5k_I9oAKGY4ZDhiODU1YmU2MWRjODg3ZjA1YTBkOTQ4MzNhZjg4MjljMWIyMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/ea0eba630e78e0eeeb28af11b372b68d4a365081","sha":"ea0eba630e78e0eeeb28af11b372b68d4a365081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/ea0eba630e78e0eeeb28af11b372b68d4a365081"}],"sha":"f8d8b855be61dc887f05a0d94833af8829c1b215","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/f8d8b855be61dc887f05a0d94833af8829c1b215"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56285471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nexus-hash","id":56285471,"login":"nexus-hash","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Mjg1NDcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus-hash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/ea0eba630e78e0eeeb28af11b372b68d4a365081/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T12:46:11Z","email":"56285471+nexus-hash@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Soumya Ranjan Tripathy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T12:46:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Defer tab to the completer only when its actually bound (#19714)\n\n## References\n\n- closes #16164\n\nThe check stays inside the CodeMirror command because a competing `Tab`\nshortcut cannot preempt the editor keymap, as tracked in #15897.\n\n## Code changes\n\n- Adds a `commandRegistry` editor extension holding the command registry\nin a facet, registered by the CodeMirror services plugin.\n- Adds `hasKeyBinding`, reporting whether an enabled shortcut is bound\nto a keystroke for an editor.\n- Types the facet as `IReadonlyCommandRegistry`, an allow list of\n`keyBindings`, `keyBindingChanged` and `isEnabled`.\n- Declines `Tab` in `indentMoreOrInsertTab` only when a shortcut claims\nit, instead of whenever the completer could apply.\n- Falls back to the completer classes when no command registry is\nprovided.\n- Adds `@lumino/commands` to `@jupyterlab/codemirror`.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nBefore: `Tab` invoked the completer whenever there was text before the\ncursor. Disabling or rebinding `completer:invoke-notebook`,\n`completer:invoke-console` or `completer:invoke-file` did not change\nthat, and `Tab` moved focus instead of inserting anything.\n\nAfter: `Tab` inserts a tab, or indents at the start of a line, unless an\nenabled shortcut claims it. Defaults are unchanged.\n\nOther `Tab` shortcuts, such as the debugger console completer, now take\nthe key too.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Sonnet 5, Opus 5, Fable 5.1)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"74a86200b4075be49c3b78e98259a3c7e1d04a75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/74a86200b4075be49c3b78e98259a3c7e1d04a75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/ea0eba630e78e0eeeb28af11b372b68d4a365081","verification":{"payload":"tree 74a86200b4075be49c3b78e98259a3c7e1d04a75\nparent 6e0d532acf1a1f67cceb35d7bd4d6709e7d17d5d\nauthor Soumya Ranjan Tripathy <56285471+nexus-hash@users.noreply.github.com> 1790167571 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790167571 +0100\n\nDefer tab to the completer only when its actually bound (#19714)\n\n## References\n\n- closes #16164\n\nThe check stays inside the CodeMirror command because a competing `Tab`\nshortcut cannot preempt the editor keymap, as tracked in #15897.\n\n## Code changes\n\n- Adds a `commandRegistry` editor extension holding the command registry\nin a facet, registered by the CodeMirror services plugin.\n- Adds `hasKeyBinding`, reporting whether an enabled shortcut is bound\nto a keystroke for an editor.\n- Types the facet as `IReadonlyCommandRegistry`, an allow list of\n`keyBindings`, `keyBindingChanged` and `isEnabled`.\n- Declines `Tab` in `indentMoreOrInsertTab` only when a shortcut claims\nit, instead of whenever the completer could apply.\n- Falls back to the completer classes when no command registry is\nprovided.\n- Adds `@lumino/commands` to `@jupyterlab/codemirror`.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nBefore: `Tab` invoked the completer whenever there was text before the\ncursor. Disabling or rebinding `completer:invoke-notebook`,\n`completer:invoke-console` or `completer:invoke-file` did not change\nthat, and `Tab` moved focus instead of inserting anything.\n\nAfter: `Tab` inserts a tab, or indents at the start of a line, unless an\nenabled shortcut claims it. Defaults are unchanged.\n\nOther `Tab` shortcuts, such as the debugger console completer, now take\nthe key too.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone.\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Code (Sonnet 5, Opus 5, Fable 5.1)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs8oTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9/IQAHqsyC0oJXkFa6GOBYiOADRy\njXFyovkWEd0rBGTiDFyi9GMswCe0GZfcY80N/HtBeZaGtdnZ3MwQoi9Z5GhwzlAo\nizyww+LoRzLKyF4QafoKsPlRVWQ1+OcNzl58pTffVf4plsekGeOA8Yr5brLb8XSW\noOcTDuGDn5gLTdTQsEM8A6nOtE0fHfkKdvNN+N7PYzFjdg63R1INdMNuKziLxPX7\no/5P+z4GOYlECZm7cIeIl009q+YGneymKF6i+EJholxcTl/ouOVFQU83ci1+h47W\niELbyrfd/E3ig4Dj3xLx2wBSGd7W2ZfX5eTFUac6sZuymm4/MjuxrxQW8Nuv+BDh\nua9VfvxmTAa3qmhVCvDpqwQPptqcmIMUte4b9sQkgarak2gBVzJZPsSO/nWPYzSN\nelWiB6awwlxEk3St6ujOauUELec/h6gR8kz4rOth0DyvtOIB6GdgwacZbyg3YV5Q\nJmL06Q1HVBMIGBk28iDG0XcfLGJgWrSkqWP1qs+yDzxWjXyuUIDoDWn4oBaG1U6x\njviFRErTlRrp/p2xVSSvNHf96uCp49xio5+AFjdm7uLGnWl9DaOXvong2uB4T8dF\nDPZAh2iRmUwLqL3co0slgU0wa2macRL6PlRnAYUaMJKtYxQRtgecNra9gnNsYm7c\nDSOOsZimfxne+S+I4tgt\n=3zbb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T12:46:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gith