ithub.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/f41e1caaba0adbf1317c3fc390e28796be3d2f60","node_id":"C_kwDOA5k_I9oAKGY0MWUxY2FhYmEwYWRiZjEzMTdjM2ZjMzkwZTI4Nzk2YmUzZDJmNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/cd7f6133a5809c83ebbede50673b06aa2fd0c311","sha":"cd7f6133a5809c83ebbede50673b06aa2fd0c311","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/cd7f6133a5809c83ebbede50673b06aa2fd0c311"}],"sha":"f41e1caaba0adbf1317c3fc390e28796be3d2f60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/f41e1caaba0adbf1317c3fc390e28796be3d2f60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5832902?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/krassowski","id":5832902,"login":"krassowski","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4MzI5MDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krassowski","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/cd7f6133a5809c83ebbede50673b06aa2fd0c311/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:44:19Z","email":"5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Michał Krassowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:44:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix resizing optimization for larger notebooks (#19620)\n\nLumino''s `LayoutItem` caches the geometry it writes. The resize freeze\ninterfered with the cache, corrupting the layout of every node\npositioned through a `LayoutItem`. Widget nodes that are not positioned\nvia layout were unharmed and are frozen without side effects.\n- This PR fixes the issue by skipping the lumino-positioned widgets\n- it reclaims the cost of the fix by explicitly freezing height on all\nelements; this means resizing gets even faster\n- it moves some repetitive logic to helper functions and fixes minor\nedge cases with drag handling and timer disposal\n- the bulk of the changeset are new tests\n\n## References\n\n- Fixes #19611.\n- Follow-up to #18877, which added `OptimizedDockPanelSvg` and was\nreleased in 4.6.0.\n\n## Code changes\n\n- The freeze now skips elements Lumino positions, tested by their inline\n`position: absolute`, and applies to the plain DOM inside them. For a\nnotebook that moves it from `.jp-Notebook` down to\n`.jp-WindowedPanel-outer`.\n- Every frozen element now gets a definite `height`, where only the\noutermost one did before. A maximum alone still leaves the browser\ncomputing the height of a large text node from its content on every\nframe.\n- The frozen sizes are re-measured as the drag moves. Two of those\nre-measures could run at once, only one of them could be cancelled, and\nthe other wrote pixel sizes onto elements that had already been\nunfrozen.\n- A second pointer going down during a drag no longer ends the drag\nearly and leaves the panels frozen for good.\n- The freeze now ends exactly when Lumino''s drag ends: on a left-button\n`pointerup`, or on Escape. Any `pointerup` and any key press used to end\nit, leaving the rest of the drag unoptimized.\n- `pointercancel` now ends the freeze too. Lumino does not listen for it\nbut a pen or touch drag ends when a system gesture takes over.\n- `dispose()` and `onAfterDetach()` now end the drag, so the re-measure\ntimer stops instead of running on for the life of the page.\n\nThe benchmark from #18877 renders one very heavy cell. The freeze also\nhas to handle an output area holding many modest outputs, so it now\nraises `maxNumberOutputs` and measures that shape too.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nPreviously, dragging a split handle in the main area could leave a\nnotebook stuck at its pre-drag width, either narrower than its panel and\ncentred in it, or wider and clipped. Expanding the browser window did\nnot always recover it. This PR fixes it.\n\n### Before\n\n\n[dockpanel-resize-before.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0dd012f1-2518-4918-8ffc-075b54846025)\n\n### After\n\n\n[dockpanel-resize-after.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/77110cf9-a879-4f1c-80e0-92504fcb3805)\n\nTo reproduce the issue one needs a notebook over the heaviness threshold\n(a thousand rendered nodes), with those nodes spread across many cells\nrather than concentrated in one.\n\nResize is now even faster, because every frozen element now gets a\ndefinite height rather than the outermost one alone:\n\n```bash\nBENCHMARK_NUMBER_SAMPLES=20 jlpm test:benchmark --grep \"Notebook Resize\"\n```\n\n| Variant | Mode | runs | n | avg | median | sd | min | max |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| before this PR | optimized | 2 | 40 | 937 ms | 902 ms | 140 ms | 744\nms | 1292 ms |\n| before this PR | unoptimized | 2 | 40 | 1952 ms | 1931 ms | 119 ms |\n1766 ms | 2242 ms |\n| this PR | optimized | 2 | 40 | 865 ms | 831 ms | 103 ms | 756 ms |\n1240 ms |\n| this PR | unoptimized | 2 | 39 | 1959 ms | 1956 ms | 116 ms | 1758 ms\n| 2244 ms |\n\nThat is 2.14x faster before and 2.35x faster after, on the medians.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **Yes**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **Yes**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Opus 5 and Fable 5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"cba4e49b0825dd68442f4d6aa982bd19abf49c51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/cba4e49b0825dd68442f4d6aa982bd19abf49c51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/cd7f6133a5809c83ebbede50673b06aa2fd0c311","verification":{"payload":"tree cba4e49b0825dd68442f4d6aa982bd19abf49c51\nparent d1222ad2fab2c9ccaaf09974614ce6fd18f1c979\nauthor Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com> 1789224259 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789224259 +0100\n\nFix resizing optimization for larger notebooks (#19620)\n\nLumino''s `LayoutItem` caches the geometry it writes. The resize freeze\ninterfered with the cache, corrupting the layout of every node\npositioned through a `LayoutItem`. Widget nodes that are not positioned\nvia layout were unharmed and are frozen without side effects.\n- This PR fixes the issue by skipping the lumino-positioned widgets\n- it reclaims the cost of the fix by explicitly freezing height on all\nelements; this means resizing gets even faster\n- it moves some repetitive logic to helper functions and fixes minor\nedge cases with drag handling and timer disposal\n- the bulk of the changeset are new tests\n\n## References\n\n- Fixes #19611.\n- Follow-up to #18877, which added `OptimizedDockPanelSvg` and was\nreleased in 4.6.0.\n\n## Code changes\n\n- The freeze now skips elements Lumino positions, tested by their inline\n`position: absolute`, and applies to the plain DOM inside them. For a\nnotebook that moves it from `.jp-Notebook` down to\n`.jp-WindowedPanel-outer`.\n- Every frozen element now gets a definite `height`, where only the\noutermost one did before. A maximum alone still leaves the browser\ncomputing the height of a large text node from its content on every\nframe.\n- The frozen sizes are re-measured as the drag moves. Two of those\nre-measures could run at once, only one of them could be cancelled, and\nthe other wrote pixel sizes onto elements that had already been\nunfrozen.\n- A second pointer going down during a drag no longer ends the drag\nearly and leaves the panels frozen for good.\n- The freeze now ends exactly when Lumino''s drag ends: on a left-button\n`pointerup`, or on Escape. Any `pointerup` and any key press used to end\nit, leaving the rest of the drag unoptimized.\n- `pointercancel` now ends the freeze too. Lumino does not listen for it\nbut a pen or touch drag ends when a system gesture takes over.\n- `dispose()` and `onAfterDetach()` now end the drag, so the re-measure\ntimer stops instead of running on for the life of the page.\n\nThe benchmark from #18877 renders one very heavy cell. The freeze also\nhas to handle an output area holding many modest outputs, so it now\nraises `maxNumberOutputs` and measures that shape too.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nPreviously, dragging a split handle in the main area could leave a\nnotebook stuck at its pre-drag width, either narrower than its panel and\ncentred in it, or wider and clipped. Expanding the browser window did\nnot always recover it. This PR fixes it.\n\n### Before\n\n\n[dockpanel-resize-before.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0dd012f1-2518-4918-8ffc-075b54846025)\n\n### After\n\n\n[dockpanel-resize-after.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/77110cf9-a879-4f1c-80e0-92504fcb3805)\n\nTo reproduce the issue one needs a notebook over the heaviness threshold\n(a thousand rendered nodes), with those nodes spread across many cells\nrather than concentrated in one.\n\nResize is now even faster, because every frozen element now gets a\ndefinite height rather than the outermost one alone:\n\n```bash\nBENCHMARK_NUMBER_SAMPLES=20 jlpm test:benchmark --grep \"Notebook Resize\"\n```\n\n| Variant | Mode | runs | n | avg | median | sd | min | max |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| before this PR | optimized | 2 | 40 | 937 ms | 902 ms | 140 ms | 744\nms | 1292 ms |\n| before this PR | unoptimized | 2 | 40 | 1952 ms | 1931 ms | 119 ms |\n1766 ms | 2242 ms |\n| this PR | optimized | 2 | 40 | 865 ms | 831 ms | 103 ms | 756 ms |\n1240 ms |\n| this PR | unoptimized | 2 | 39 | 1959 ms | 1956 ms | 116 ms | 1758 ms\n| 2244 ms |\n\nThat is 2.14x faster before and 2.35x faster after, on the medians.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **Yes**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **Yes**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Opus 5 and Fable 5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpWVDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF7YQAHWd5xFX9g1RrgIH1BqqlGoK\nvua37ZgtriQwNRNPQk7tXmuKm7D2Ax051Hb50nh1ldnjCLGaQAK1Jld6iCIKNHQW\nhSHJjkl5/vHTw/vSHOiONsjntuKXckzwi+Nbji6SB8WMyiPhl4wFRfDqKiWlMJ0f\n0FhAXRLK7kr0OkcBESEMKs7GGnW4OarvIQredmopNQgI6sAzbnMwp9itl4ZGqxZI\n+opE3u6lSPQ/Yi8xnKMxoIDrCpBzeLdi3WrD6GT6KLRHvd28aq1ceCO2ahsA/Kb2\nbpbLmI8FtigVgq/TCKGOBeTL7WTcUiyvm4b929aGkCgzKnDN0pMQgSuZJD95CpZs\nzAyPK/zEHNfqFmQO3f+CBZ4CB9pBfLAfl4b4gnHZwHlDFgy4hn4XPPm80p9m7Av6\ntHit93gL/DCcg2383ZpTfoJrqASGjSqftAl2g0IwilHd+/TJCTZohvVMvb7wTioQ\nzI5e0F8CYNvRcuwD4Ra9p0QgXPrDLrV5ST8aaubQAyVeQEwrJiZxgv6nnKVXmRf5\n9JPBEKkFvvF9POO1MUvZh5HLeTQbRnq4bdpjtMX3jofXnkgzMqrIx3nc3FstAguS\nVEmPNDIRTpI5/7M1ByoeveDXwcYIkQYtVa3ZKyapX2IHv9kdDM2BkqYFpmOQY0KY\nNB/TlXzxb54KMjg3S2p2\n=EMrg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T14:44:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/priv