ub.com/users/MUFFANUJ/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/d1222ad2fab2c9ccaaf09974614ce6fd18f1c979/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:28:51Z","email":"anujsinghhero292@gmail.com","name":"ANUJ KUMAR SINGH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T18:28:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add CI memory leak regression tests (#19665)\n\n## References\nCloses #19362 \n\n## Code changes\n\nAdds a dedicated Galata memory-leak Playwright project that uses\nChromium DevTools Protocol to count retained notebook-related objects\nafter common notebook lifecycle workflows. The new suite covers deleting\nexecuted cells, repeatedly opening and closing notebooks, closing cloned\nnotebook views, and switching cells with the metadata editor open. The\nCI workflow now runs this project on pull requests with a single worker\nfor deterministic object counts, and the excessive leak-investigation\ncomments from earlier fixes are cleaned up.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nNone\n\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce5619e7acb7f74ffb97cc12acb326e5e907b16c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/ce5619e7acb7f74ffb97cc12acb326e5e907b16c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/d1222ad2fab2c9ccaaf09974614ce6fd18f1c979","verification":{"payload":"tree ce5619e7acb7f74ffb97cc12acb326e5e907b16c\nparent 3903cf54e9b1f9dc65283fa38878e263d470538c\nauthor ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com> 1789151331 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789151331 +0530\n\nAdd CI memory leak regression tests (#19665)\n\n## References\nCloses #19362 \n\n## Code changes\n\nAdds a dedicated Galata memory-leak Playwright project that uses\nChromium DevTools Protocol to count retained notebook-related objects\nafter common notebook lifecycle workflows. The new suite covers deleting\nexecuted cells, repeatedly opening and closing notebooks, closing cloned\nnotebook views, and switching cells with the metadata editor open. The\nCI workflow now runs this project on pull requests with a single worker\nfor deterministic object counts, and the excessive leak-investigation\ncomments from earlier fixes are cleaned up.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nNone\n\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpEhjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPR4QACpnCQ7zqkD2c3eIZX4Qdm9i\nZ7hbra1LXOZe3Ulq2u3VhaPbKGd1GDVzj+GdVn8N/NVL5Fza35xCBucfZXqmSn7U\npbCzP6IlscwRp/8kwgnXaGNpLHo9cA52Y7f/7a7EJctdujs/RUqaj3ZR1CNckYXM\nDaAGcwJT8ku9/M+1xyJ3pA6VF1I0yGH0/1Hwzq1s8roOOefxwmZ0I/tc4ZIfy9Zr\nyp5O1jwCu2zRqG18LipFDBQMt4DbQ2rqhtqzpc58ZFgOyTsXQ8bYByYnOKCoafaY\nALzDVJ5F4WWf49UpFiNYtHaJJ4ikse91QSaqhuv/M6VjFUXCCLcJ3PGBi7lkB7Ii\nTjezAwteloDPfw3RLniMZ8EZ44TjCIh7Y9jVYoBi5tMW1IarJDM7dzu56iRjFr3M\nYP6n8XAKoqFnGatjx+5xkY9ivGpp6kjqsJkktnZjq05G94O0Woefr35YV6I12uyy\nZuH/U