shan808/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Darshan808/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Darshan808/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Darshan808","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/4d07601fe800fb0e8a122a8e706e7359cfa68ada/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:16:35Z","email":"pranishpoudel10@gmail.com","name":"Darshan Paudyal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T16:16:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Use Galata filebrowser helpers in tests (#19645)\n\n<!--\nThanks for contributing to JupyterLab!\nPlease fill out the following items to submit a pull request.\nSee the contributing guidelines for more information:\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n## References\n- Follow-up to https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/pull/19307\n\n### Description\n\nFixes the 53 `jupyter/galata-prefer-filebrowser-helper` warnings. Three\nspots keep the raw double-click with an eslint disable and the reason in\nthe comment.\n\n\n<!-- Note issue numbers this pull request addresses (should be at least\none, see contributing guidelines above). -->\n\n<!-- Note any other pull requests that address this issue and how this\npull request is different. -->\n\n## Code changes\n\n<!-- Describe the code changes and how they address the issue. -->\nMost of them were \"double-click the folder, then double-click the file\",\nwhich collapses into a single helper call:\n```ts\n    await page.notebook.openByPath(''notebooks/Lorenz.ipynb'');\n    await page.filebrowser.open(''narrative/jupyterlab.md'');\n    await page.filebrowser.openDirectory(''notebooks'');\n```\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nNone\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Opus\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef26c19c32f4ff6d6a2564e42b256704e739c07e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/ef26c19c32f4ff6d6a2564e42b256704e739c07e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/4d07601fe800fb0e8a122a8e706e7359cfa68ada","verification":{"payload":"tree ef26c19c32f4ff6d6a2564e42b256704e739c07e\nparent 731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86\nauthor Darshan Paudyal <pranishpoudel10@gmail.com> 1789143395 +0545\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789143395 +0100\n\nUse Galata filebrowser helpers in tests (#19645)\n\n<!--\nThanks for contributing to JupyterLab!\nPlease fill out the following items to submit a pull request.\nSee the contributing guidelines for more information:\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n## References\n- Follow-up to https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/pull/19307\n\n### Description\n\nFixes the 53 `jupyter/galata-prefer-filebrowser-helper` warnings. Three\nspots keep the raw double-click with an eslint disable and the reason in\nthe comment.\n\n\n<!-- Note issue numbers this pull request addresses (should be at least\none, see contributing guidelines above). -->\n\n<!-- Note any other pull requests that address this issue and how this\npull request is different. -->\n\n## Code changes\n\n<!-- Describe the code changes and how they address the issue. -->\nMost of them were \"double-click the folder, then double-click the file\",\nwhich collapses into a single helper call:\n```ts\n    await page.notebook.openByPath(''notebooks/Lorenz.ipynb'');\n    await page.filebrowser.open(''narrative/jupyterlab.md'');\n    await page.filebrowser.openDirectory(''notebooks'');\n```\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nNone\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: Claude Opus\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCljCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw5EQAH8wIKvwDhw+eRIbZ+ZKi00n\nQDSb8bp/qXTeHrkDjxYo455kdHC9eZAiedayAt/Z3FcMf7PO3kmB20CEi1wXTtOL\nIulUVX1K9Fs+RSyJ8aZO1fzQELyu16tLaZZjmODPngyiGLSvdWPnfuGPzBqkAQp9\nayRQztsvQBAMyP3G2IMwWhyVSeoIrc0lNHHJaGpw/6SNK0xAPaInH8GELXKSV/Q/\nzbkgPUrvcaA+IU79SsQRS7fpACHzferyu7SsDVaXdJOXrGY//rTjJR+QKOIoWFjq\nWRvlk1qzn3204g/vwS5Trez2aBP3DY+LGuxnLp79U1nt2AvpOO4DQ2CsEZ0eZT0D\nX0jkPhlPSxcjX7Kx6o5gdPgLZLTz0zR/2qwHJKjW25EHSi4fR13REu3j7rEJpfuZ\nlaZT6QfIZQrr1xH5hC2uIcO3Ly2mJENqLHjYJU2DnmLLTJC8ObS7UpMAMiG9Xmt8\nHUymFgDnAAbdiJIgF0THQL0UpPqWWxJwBC2rf8tE836lSH0nkboHAdXL4kpGYcJg\nibpjMWGThYLc5L7yqMcvb9nZ0Cj0bx5p4VPVVP6S5naj8xWZ5tkZ+gyatKKbpDdh\nh32V9qa/6bXS/FLnH+VT3IFXs6Cb3sWV407CivXSdoSYUsZGVWVZtIKtifKd2chd\nPgkl+fixKa4BAgIvYuo+\n=P7Su\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T16:16:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/4d07601fe800fb0e8a122a8e706e7359cfa68ada","node_id":"C_kwDOA5k_I9oAKDRkMDc2MDFmZTgwMGZiMGU4YTEyMmE4ZTcwNmU3MzU5Y2ZhNjhhZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86","sha":"731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86"}],"sha":"4d07601fe800fb0e8a122a8e706e7359cfa68ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/4d07601fe800fb0e8a122a8e706e7359cfa68ada"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151390316?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MUFFANUJ","id":151390316,"login":"MUFFANUJ","node_id":"U_kgDOCQYIbA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:55:11Z","email":"anujsinghhero292@gmail.com","name":"ANUJ KUMAR SINGH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:55:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Sanitize bottom-panel pager MIME output (#19677)\n\n<!--\nThanks for contributing to JupyterLab!\nPlease fill out the following items to submit a pull request.\nSee the contributing guidelines for more information:\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n## References\n\nCloses #19675 \n\n## Code changes\n\nThis fixes bottom-panel pager rendering so kernel-supplied `source:\n\"page\"` MIME bundles are treated as untrusted. The pager handler now\nuses the existing trusted-output MIME selection pattern and creates the\nMimeModel with `trusted: false`, allowing ordinary pager HTML to render\nwhile forcing `renderHTML` through sanitization and preventing inline\nscripts from executing. Regression coverage was added for the default\npager fallback path and for helpInBottomPanel: true to verify HTML\nrenders in the Help panel without preserving or executing script tags.\n\nThe change is a hardening of the Help panel, matching the classic\nnotebook pager that showed `text/plain` only.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nWith the PR, `text/html` pager content in the bottom panel is sanitized\n(as is the contextual help menu). This mostly matters for side-effects\nbut somewhat hardens against a potential attack vector.\n\nMost users won''t see any difference because few kernels send `text/html`\npager data (e.g. IPython when `enable_html_pager` is on).\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5","tree":{"sha":"46097b4ef7f8560979612c21134a703375d357a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/46097b4ef7f8560979612c21134a703375d357a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86","verification":{"payload":"tree 46097b4ef7f8560979612c21134a703375d357a0\nparent d982d1fe7deb559f02203fbfe4dc0f8c9db976e5\nauthor ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com> 1789142111 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789142111 +0100\n\nSanitize bottom-panel pager MIME output (#19677)\n\n<!--\nThanks for contributing to JupyterLab!\nPlease fill out the following items to submit a pull request.\nSee the contributing guidelines for more information:\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\n-->\n\n## References\n\nCloses #19675 \n\n## Code changes\n\nThis fixes bottom-panel pager rendering so kernel-supplied `source:\n\"page\"` MIME bundles are treated as untrusted. The pager handler now\nuses the existing trusted-output MIME selection pattern and creates the\nMimeModel with `trusted: false`, allowing ordinary pager HTML to render\nwhile forcing `renderHTML` through sanitization and preventing inline\nscripts from executing. Regression coverage was added for the default\npager fallback path and for helpInBottomPanel: true to verify HTML\nrenders in the Help panel without preserving or executing script tags.\n\nThe change is a hardening of the Help panel, matching the classic\nnotebook pager that showed `text/plain` only.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nWith the PR, `text/html` pager content in the bottom panel is sanitized\n(as is the contextual help menu). This mostly matters for side-effects\nbut somewhat hardens against a potential attack vector.\n\nMost users won''t see any difference because few kernels send `text/html`\npager data (e.g. IPython when `enable_html_pager` is on).\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCRfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIdgQAB6W2f63XPviWwdOTE9WIis4\nEpdGdJ3mj9wPoo+l8i3OFaNjXMUMF3aVjFRMbHERdLM+HLpY1LhDoyF98zbSy/Jn\nlcBow3V5viIbWKkpEPOJCEdATAEqMDELUJcasmFBIcZCOc0/50GcCjmSFqLZSAja\n+66960DJyQzxUnMhQ4UOuox3eFwZTAEcoggLnVU47t7BvHXxv9YqXX/QaAG/dg9R\njeIbPw4/xtsk52I4ejMBCUbVjL8nqivECfKR9vazbgxGZN2DjpidWZx3xHsXKgx5\no4+Z5NUg5DwIOjxtiuzE9hMmISiJbdhhkcF379UkDtlVj/Xhi9EMPmnGbgm89V55\nIuf8IOKyuA4rULwxhx7b/lb+eJhpH0c7TO8q+j22NYXfjmWYct+OW9ghIGcbvaXm\nnSVpVGhvUAKPzmO9LgVDDPSEq5hDaWQIeLOLc5S11YapYnvrZl83/H796F77we3T\nj+6qnkD0IRtniErAkeVgQV0APBY2IEiBaErukbCEv4LSfu64mMDNrYMjFzE9kPLa\nkHLtPKbwz3/wMgvA8WJjD8+eOZvM9C//BVt6X2yPrQlU1xu+rDA8HLDq1Ub6PGIH\nLRz1ZByisfu5F4ZE5D3VwQXTLBJU+rnsKCTOKrprixXrUKdFiV1Fjk+PZC/Zbv/4\nGI8BWYMFHGYLjSiQ50fO\n=LRPp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T15:55:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86","node_id":"C_kwDOA5k_I9oAKDczMWYzYTgxYmI4MDdlZmNlOWU3MDZlMmQ2NDE4YTk1ZDlhNDRkODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commit/d982d1fe7deb559f02203fbfe4dc0f8c9db976e5","sha":"d982d1fe7deb559f02203fbfe4dc0f8c9db976e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/d982d1fe7deb559f02203fbfe4dc0f8c9db976e5"}],"sha":"731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/731f3a81bb807efce9e706e2d6418a95d9a44d86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151390316?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MUFFANUJ","id":151390316,"login":"MUFFANUJ","node_id":"U_kgDOCQYIbA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/d982d1fe7deb559f02203fbfe4dc0f8c9db976e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:38:35Z","email":"anujsinghhero292@gmail.com","name":"ANUJ KUMAR SINGH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:38:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix PyPI extension manager `package.json` inspection for `tar.gz` archives (#19613)\n\n## References\n\nFixes #19608 \n\n## Code changes\n\nFixes the PyPI extension manager’s `.tar.gz` source distribution\ninspection path by opening downloaded archive bytes with\n`TarFile.open(fileobj=..., mode=\"r:gz\")`. This lets JupyterLab read\n`package.json` metadata from sdists after install and correctly include\nkernel and server restart follow-ups from `jupyterlab.discovery`.\n\nAdds a focused regression test that creates an in-memory .tar.gz\ncontaining package.json, mocks the pip dry-run/install flow, and\nverifies the install result includes frontend, kernel, and server\nrestart needs.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nThe PyPI extension manager now correctly reads `package.json` from\n`.tar.gz` source distributions and reports the required restart\nfollow-ups, including kernel and server, after installing an extension.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.4\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d651a55ad91e0b3d386b23f221b135c94c23f183","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/d651a55ad91e0b3d386b23f221b135c94c23f183"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/d982d1fe7deb559f02203fbfe4dc0f8c9db976e5","verification":{"payload":"tree d651a55ad91e0b3d386b23f221b135c94c23f183\nparent 3c5af3b91877cc04f67fef60fa5a0fac7179bf1d\nauthor ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com> 1789141115 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789141115 +0530\n\nFix PyPI extension manager `package.json` inspection for `tar.gz` archives (#19613)\n\n## References\n\nFixes #19608 \n\n## Code changes\n\nFixes the PyPI extension manager’s `.tar.gz` source distribution\ninspection path by opening downloaded archive bytes with\n`TarFile.open(fileobj=..., mode=\"r:gz\")`. This lets JupyterLab read\n`package.json` metadata from sdists after install and correctly include\nkernel and server restart follow-ups from `jupyterlab.discovery`.\n\nAdds a focused regression test that creates an in-memory .tar.gz\ncontaining package.json, mocks the pip dry-run/install flow, and\nverifies the install result includes frontend, kernel, and server\nrestart needs.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nThe PyPI extension manager now correctly reads `package.json` from\n`.tar.gz` source distributions and reports the required restart\nfollow-ups, including kernel and server, after installing an extension.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNone\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.4\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpCB7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3eoQACRXSkKwHSuTZGWW9Li2kRi8\nYLDkZlLrpfeMuitpRx5mxZrJRAbUKVe6hG8g0qJL8iuHRaAlD33Jpwb9cIuQpU5O\nR9nPjczhoKo/KyKHGOOEDKSZtMRCdE88XzyjtVaZ3aXOm18L/akEaUG3jX/4taaR\nlGas6JPKcyz9zPOzew7D+jqHUtVPdV4zpte0VTsNYsS6WdLO09Fvntl8n6jEo6F4\nRAvyMf7Kq1cuWYYtHVwK1RazKxOT8AvvkY4llcJpZyn8vIRYIMS9XQ87UlWd20x8\nyK9SbK8gPpUBB94nzVGWrTH9x63DnygaSJU5F+RiNAP2snS01Ye115FFoNytnjiU\nJEAfs8NIycLyoGFm+pyOIrqeZfpxTlF/92QuJryiekGCl9yTDR6bLsmyh5RAe7Y5\n/h5UWGCPxQZTsva8YW/uog6JJolwax4zazE0KCJWsrHthwHjYMsiKRj/qZQo8iZL\n4JDftG3mfwlILqj+vJU3AK3HmiGpW8K7UpPo//plHa2DVfvra09Gsd/8s9wT7i3K\n2e7iYrt2noDQ/cRtFaLaS2OV2RsDr7a01PcTbvGVDnsjkc3WN42x0FMDQX2SBwTS\nRxdXLPgxJL6TR617CIMxIc1afPsUDRjTNqQjOJOfgDbsFsNseHhajw7v7e/qvwSB\nqPguTVp+Ry1wRQDxN9e9\n=JDXT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified