nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MUFFANUJ","id":151390316,"login":"MUFFANUJ","node_id":"U_kgDOCQYIbA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/c9277f586523f97ec65756bcdc2ade53adbf25e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:41:39Z","email":"anujsinghhero292@gmail.com","name":"ANUJ KUMAR SINGH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T11:41:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Defer loading disabled federated extensions during startup (#19627)\n\n## References\n\nCloses #19623\n\n## Code changes\n\nDefers loading package-level disabled federated extension modules during\ninitial JupyterLab startup. Previously, `dev_mode/index.js` called\n`createModule()` for every federated extension and mime extension, even\nwhen the entire extension package was disabled. The change queues\ndisabled federated extension and mime extension modules, then loads them\nafter `lab.restored` only to collect plugin metadata. Disabled plugins\nare still not registered or activated.\nThe late-loaded disabled plugin metadata is added to\n`JupyterLab.IInfo.availablePlugins`, and discovered disabled plugin IDs\nare added to `JupyterLab.IInfo.disabled.matches`. `JupyterLab.Info` now\nexposes helper methods for these late updates and emits\navailablePluginsChanged when available plugin metadata changes.\nThe Plugin Manager model now listens for `availablePluginsChanged`,\nrefreshes its internal available-plugin list, and disconnects the signal\non dispose.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nDisabled prebuilt/federated extensions are no longer loaded during the\ninitial page load, improving startup behavior when users or\nadministrators have disabled extension packages.\nDisabled extensions still appear in the Advanced Plugin Manager after\nstartup, so users can continue to inspect and re-enable them.\nNo visual UI changes.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nListing an extension package name in `disabledExtensions` now disables\nevery plugin that package provides. Before, a plugin whose id did not\nstart with the package name stayed enabled, so a package not following\nthe plugin id convention could not be disabled as a whole. Each such\nplugin is named in a browser console warning. To keep it enabled, list\nthe plugin ids to disable in `disabledExtensions` instead of the package\nname\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f566a063424295eec2353dadfdb0e36ef9bed2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/4f566a063424295eec2353dadfdb0e36ef9bed2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/c9277f586523f97ec65756bcdc2ade53adbf25e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f566a063424295eec2353dadfdb0e36ef9bed2d\nparent 4053a8631a74f4812827d8b0310bb6b6bfbac97b\nauthor ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com> 1789126899 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789126899 +0100\n\nDefer loading disabled federated extensions during startup (#19627)\n\n## References\n\nCloses #19623\n\n## Code changes\n\nDefers loading package-level disabled federated extension modules during\ninitial JupyterLab startup. Previously, `dev_mode/index.js` called\n`createModule()` for every federated extension and mime extension, even\nwhen the entire extension package was disabled. The change queues\ndisabled federated extension and mime extension modules, then loads them\nafter `lab.restored` only to collect plugin metadata. Disabled plugins\nare still not registered or activated.\nThe late-loaded disabled plugin metadata is added to\n`JupyterLab.IInfo.availablePlugins`, and discovered disabled plugin IDs\nare added to `JupyterLab.IInfo.disabled.matches`. `JupyterLab.Info` now\nexposes helper methods for these late updates and emits\navailablePluginsChanged when available plugin metadata changes.\nThe Plugin Manager model now listens for `availablePluginsChanged`,\nrefreshes its internal available-plugin list, and disconnects the signal\non dispose.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nDisabled prebuilt/federated extensions are no longer loaded during the\ninitial page load, improving startup behavior when users or\nadministrators have disabled extension packages.\nDisabled extensions still appear in the Advanced Plugin Manager after\nstartup, so users can continue to inspect and re-enable them.\nNo visual UI changes.\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nListing an extension package name in `disabledExtensions` now disables\nevery plugin that package provides. Before, a plugin whose id did not\nstart with the package name stayed enabled, so a package not following\nthe plugin id convention could not be disabled as a whole. Each such\nplugin is named in a browser console warning. To keep it enabled, list\nthe plugin ids to disable in `disabledExtensions` instead of the package\nname\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Michał Krassowski <5832902+krassowski@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo+jzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9LUQAIIZ+0uDxp1UGdPMRhtHzoya\nHxm08LdEZx9WKBC9JsKaSUyuolgHP9Iq0iMt6dC27ezr3UMx9IAWmAY8g99vVl20\n4heZdPXu/ae1smX+nlRwGbb2YJusylKVOuW5YjAKUXy2YQ6ufsHTTHIpob21aNgu\n9TfHI+LdO+grFRzx4a6YJAgDAo52rbT6w85qgFmpCAts9lvXEgEhoEFhMLPqJhbr\n5Bxo2h+PfmOCXr9lnNdauqljgHLuCi6EFYAr7EsiDvLoERGH9CLwsKwt8w2rUWI5\n00EjK3z9CwxwgP+rgWp3SRYmPty1sU0xPH2AAbfna/EkGI+JzSO0IwqH8D2Mfwcj\noEP0LQ0naBLJfvGOjYLZYPYS3R72YRMNf/TgKH/lJJwKdsbODCJVyUbXeCA8vj+d\nLvp2ii9S8nMRdv54Io2pu2GXKZwl7Pq3akFpe89A6D/7NtU2EywyzxEleiFC9ZXP\nNYdvPAWEB1R5YLtZ8D2KvabyNsseonYeW6V9Lc1/ygqeYslpKi+Obbz/6B4BmL+l\n83LgvFfpZKgnerXkam9sRCc++eU3LN/d+aLTgWwmH1vYbJiAnj+M1mJHRjghYrUr\nHlAPVRkv5J1tf5YoXcmHEoKc73WW+Wp51CMC5Zm1uaPS7WsBtLsEedeGpDQgMVwF\nLFIeJL+PBmoJ/f1Xn1YW\n=e86D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T11:41:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.