ps://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MUFFANUJ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/commits/06dfe441e3b42e94ad169aef91e74c5217c0f88d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T10:52:49Z","email":"anujsinghhero292@gmail.com","name":"ANUJ KUMAR SINGH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T10:52:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add Copy Image context menu action (#19516)\n\n## References\n\nCloses #19216 \n\n## Code changes\n\nThis adds an `application:copy-image` command and registers it in the\ncontext menu for images inside main area widgets. The command uses\nJupyterLab’s existing context menu hit testing to find the right-clicked\n`HTMLImageElement`, then writes PNG image data to the browser clipboard\nusing `navigator.clipboard.write` and `ClipboardItem`. The\nimplementation first tries to fetch the image source and reuse the PNG\nblob directly when possible. If the source is unavailable, not PNG, or\ncannot be fetched, it falls back to drawing the rendered image to a\ncanvas and exporting it as PNG. Copy success and failure both show\nJupyterLab notifications with a short auto-close timeout (5 sec).\nFailure messaging includes the browser security limitation for\ncross-origin images, since browsers can block JavaScript from reading\nimage bytes or canvas pixels when the remote server does not allow it. A\nGalata regression test was added for the image viewer context menu. It\nopens a local PNG image, right-clicks the rendered image, and verifies\nthat Copy Image is available.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nA new Copy Image item in the right-click context menu, plus\nsuccess/error notifications when they use it.\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a88c2cb-ce7e-4716-9da8-608c679ceac2\n\n\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNo\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5","tree":{"sha":"8cfce2ad786a2fe3630954d3d3467a387b89b61c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/trees/8cfce2ad786a2fe3630954d3d3467a387b89b61c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/git/commits/06dfe441e3b42e94ad169aef91e74c5217c0f88d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8cfce2ad786a2fe3630954d3d3467a387b89b61c\nparent 58cb91afcf6dde04527f7ce308f738dd6fe16257\nauthor ANUJ KUMAR SINGH <anujsinghhero292@gmail.com> 1787655169 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787655169 +0100\n\nAdd Copy Image context menu action (#19516)\n\n## References\n\nCloses #19216 \n\n## Code changes\n\nThis adds an `application:copy-image` command and registers it in the\ncontext menu for images inside main area widgets. The command uses\nJupyterLab’s existing context menu hit testing to find the right-clicked\n`HTMLImageElement`, then writes PNG image data to the browser clipboard\nusing `navigator.clipboard.write` and `ClipboardItem`. The\nimplementation first tries to fetch the image source and reuse the PNG\nblob directly when possible. If the source is unavailable, not PNG, or\ncannot be fetched, it falls back to drawing the rendered image to a\ncanvas and exporting it as PNG. Copy success and failure both show\nJupyterLab notifications with a short auto-close timeout (5 sec).\nFailure messaging includes the browser security limitation for\ncross-origin images, since browsers can block JavaScript from reading\nimage bytes or canvas pixels when the remote server does not allow it. A\nGalata regression test was added for the image viewer context menu. It\nopens a local PNG image, right-clicks the rendered image, and verifies\nthat Copy Image is available.\n\n## User-facing changes\n\nA new Copy Image item in the right-click context menu, plus\nsuccess/error notifications when they use it.\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a88c2cb-ce7e-4716-9da8-608c679ceac2\n\n\n\n## Backwards-incompatible changes\n\nNo\n\n## AI usage\n\n- **YES**: Some or all of the content of this PR was generated by AI.\n- **YES**: The human author has carefully reviewed this PR and run this\ncode (keep this PR \"draft\" until the answer is YES)\n- AI tools and models used: ChatGPT 5.5","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjXQBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkiwQACHbK41XCdK9StRVTuJTkquJ\n6a3R8CnspP8wf/+rTcNGfIwJxcbFcuZNw6w8keSbn9v8XDdMVh1nAEqskCxotNHM\nS+suVvCibTbHS9Ovxe0cBp122BC/kJHDfPwKTOa3G94xn7EtthzaNEVBnTu+1PVi\ntL1QJAwJ8suNV1k4btcdKMouEAYSZiXWx7TrPipR/PFGiUDhZqLP3XhiqrIjcUev\nu9vus57L1Du9/oA27qqBeqL0+bTlPlqJFNcn3tBnq1CggxMwE1LPBxq4hH7Hpmul\n1yXclnhdA0/oF9QpSHvNNvXqTQaLubO6SMtkRCUDVKDbNhso8NKhiN225L0QLCzY\njaSYbKSVekChosi1/SCRQpJfJL4XSAfmYRzTWiiyTfjVFXw/gRNMpsXbDZUSI4hz\n47x2NWnHkFofVkAG9PgzQkvoJ7n9g+/x9GDugrZHfUN2K1Mz77J08nW8DTSNGrpq\nhC0mdEtBBSWP09LoVw/DzDd1731bTbuMhDY83Wj0DbfdnhGi6Wq846uVZkZkPzI2\nG0SvYBGmNX8loaXuFOI81x035WW4ODCtoHw+0rIaQNMHzmi/e8wiW9GLOXWqezHG\nYo+692LfxMoUSSc9gqTLMvb61yM27FoxXW79iXt3jSNkN32LJxIWbWgddL/Iw8Wc\nmdsi94WWWxsE+HAUh26M\n=AaYT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T10:52:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"ht