,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/fd12c557e9504450408b9a4638b5ba457748e3d8","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKGZkMTJjNTU3ZTk1MDQ0NTA0MDhiOWE0NjM4YjViYTQ1Nzc0OGUzZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d","sha":"71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d"}],"sha":"fd12c557e9504450408b9a4638b5ba457748e3d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/fd12c557e9504450408b9a4638b5ba457748e3d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:11:50Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:11:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: render a readme''s relative links against its own branch (#8411)\n\n`processReadme` turns a raw readme url into the page it is rendered at so\nthat relative links resolve, and it did that by inserting `blob/` in front\nof the literal `master`:\n\n    .replace(/master/, \"blob/master\")\n\nA repository on `main` therefore got no `blob/` at all, and every relative\nlink in its readme resolved to `github.com/<owner>/<repo>/main/<path>`,\nwhich is not a url GitHub serves. Of the loader and plugin repositories\nthe site generates pages from, the nine sampled are all on `main` —\nincluding `diagnostics-webpack-plugin`, whose readme links `CHANGELOG.md`\nand `./LICENSE`.\n\nThe branch is read from the raw url now, whatever it is called, so the\nrendered url is built rather than patched. A repository or owner whose\nname contains `master` is no longer rewritten by accident either.\n\nThe suite pinned the old behaviour: \"rewrite relative url\" asserted the\n`main` url without `blob/` as what it should be. It asserts the link that\nresolves now, and a new case covers `master`, `main` and `next` together.","tree":{"sha":"5c5237b68839052f5991ce934ca2ebb8435676af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/5c5237b68839052f5991ce934ca2ebb8435676af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d","verification":{"payload":"tree 5c5237b68839052f5991ce934ca2ebb8435676af\nparent c5389729f458d16d065c7c7501a1978665bccf08\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789409510 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789409510 +0300\n\nfix: render a readme''s relative links against its own branch (#8411)\n\n`processReadme` turns a raw readme url into the page it is rendered at so\nthat relative links resolve, and it did that by inserting `blob/` in front\nof the literal `master`:\n\n    .replace(/master/, \"blob/master\")\n\nA repository on `main` therefore got no `blob/` at all, and every relative\nlink in its readme resolved to `github.com/<owner>/<repo>/main/<path>`,\nwhich is not a url GitHub serves. Of the loader and plugin repositories\nthe site generates pages from, the nine sampled are all on `main` —\nincluding `diagnostics-webpack-plugin`, whose readme links `CHANGELOG.md`\nand `./LICENSE`.\n\nThe branch is read from the raw url now, whatever it is called, so the\nrendered url is built rather than patched. A repository or owner whose\nname contains `master` is no longer rewritten by accident either.\n\nThe suite pinned the old behaviour: \"rewrite relative url\" asserted the\n`main` url without `blob/` as what it should be. It asserts the link that\nresolves now, and a new case covers `master`, `main` and `next` together.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqDjmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIWsQACsn0k58h94xACXSI1nhCsB5\nsyV5Dp0FITkzo6tURQ2qGIzSGow02SGlKAVcLKIJScI5uNypG+K6pSbBRkRw+gME\n6Frzhav5zQXr9L/7Rf+BuPadyCMIokB8P8E8jTCYziSJGpNBF/KP38LK+Zz8gTAV\nl3GSCTrhJpTCf/xGu6EF12M0q3qHNN4b+SE4JMVS34uGMRlYpSMC7NW+RiyDgIsu\nSu+owt/Lcv3XXfRS7xe9ELIww6WWcOqlOspkMj/zKYPlrGgp90GQUSz5BujBh/79\nD401fKJpQry53hmRmWqKHZPBDk0mEU9laJJy31DnBNcWGGl6H+rhJ4idc+IFCOGg\nBG9SEFQ1W1lg8uhDM3004ByZlqOYBmM8XjM60pquRMu0FGdifX943Ao5H2RpunRf\nIJDtuxnJvEBlen6HrSJJ67LriMe8iqnY1DrQ4LQz0KoAxuHvb1+H/bOv0x4eMv96\ntfQeX1zEVW5oCK6by6748zoGapDt2GOO21CpedDFzYwrntF9CEF2nF5xJwT1kSxo\nQmgDj7PAqATMjQZ5qlCUwiJPENEyAoSqJsvGbzBICldPp7XNm0ScxKX8Oi1N++hi\nWOen0yIRWGTQ9cgo5qzePiUsR74c01MMxZ67BCH8NEkMjjaPfbCPE5psmajAgCoD\nRNFDs7rwzvdib6V3DMbQ\n=8XOh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T18:11:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKDcxYWQ4MzdhZmU3NzViNzE0NTI4ODY2NDI3Mjc1Mzc3ODUzYmUyNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/c5389729f458d16d065c7c7501a1978665bccf08","sha":"c5389729f458d16d065c7c7501a1978665bccf08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/c5389729f458d16d065c7c7501a1978665bccf08"}],"sha":"71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/71ad837afe775b714528866427275377853be25d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/c5389729f458d16d065c7c7501a1978665bccf08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T10:47:48Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T10:47:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(splash): run the build instead of naming the hashes (#8410)\n\n* docs(splash): run the build instead of naming the hashes\n\nThe front page spent three output options on content hashes and then\nshowed their digits in the emitted page, which nothing on the page needs\nand which no reader can reproduce. Since 5.111 names a page''s entries\nafter the urls its tags carry, the config is down to the one option the\npage''s `type=\"module\"` tag asks for, and the emitted names are the ones\nwebpack gives them.\n\nThe room that frees goes to the two commands a first build is actually\nmade of, which the page never showed.\n\n* docs(splash): say what each mode does to the output\n\n* docs(optimization): point the bail link at the option''s own page\n\nThe link went to /api/cli/#advanced-options, an anchor the CLI page no\nlonger carries — it documents no bail flag at all — so the link check\nfailed on the fragment. bail is documented under other-options, which is\nwhere the sentence meant to send the reader.\n\n* docs(splash): give each mode its own command and description\n\nOne block with both commands made the reader hold two commands in mind\nbefore either was explained. Each command now stands next to what it\ndoes to the output.","tree":{"sha":"977e0ec04f2ffedc8aed783e638336d037b6c701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/977e0ec04f2ffedc8aed783e638336d037b6c701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/c5389729f458d16d065c7c7501a1978665bccf08","verification":{"payload":"tree 977e0ec04f2ffedc8aed783e638336d037b6c701\nparent 768172362939cac50bcb1cdeca946ef734fc3afc\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789382868 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789382868 +0300\n\ndocs(splash): run the build instead of naming the hashes (#8410)\n\n* docs(splash): run the build instead of naming the hashes\n\nThe front page spent three output options on content hashes and then\nshowed their digits in the emitted page, which nothing on the page needs\nand which no reader can reproduce. Since 5.111 names a page''s entries\nafter the urls its tags carry, the config is down to the one option the\npage''s `type=\"module\"` tag asks for, and the emitted names are the ones\nwebpack gives them.\n\nThe room that frees goes to the two commands a first build is actually\nmade of, which the page never showed.\n\n* docs(splash): say what each mode does to the output\n\n* docs(optimization): point the bail link at the option''s own page\n\nThe link went to /api/cli/#advanced-options, an anchor the CLI page no\nlonger carries — it documents no bail flag at all — so the link check\nfailed on the fragment. bail is documented under other-options, which is\nwhere the sentence meant to send the reader.\n\n* docs(splash): give each mode its own command and description\n\nOne block with both commands made the reader hold two commands in mind\nbefore either was explained. Each command now stands next to what it\ndoes to the output.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp9DUC