04e4dcf0d843ac139e"}],"sha":"ab7106e3e673e81668517dabe9338b79073d854e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/ab7106e3e673e81668517dabe9338b79073d854e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/0ba16baf78ac26561f84fe04e4dcf0d843ac139e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:01:39Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:01:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: catch typos with cspell, and fix the five it found (#8404)\n\nThe site had no spellchecker: vale runs proselint and Speciesism, neither of\nwhich checks spelling, so a misspelling only ever got caught by a reader. That\nis why refrence sat in the TypeScript guide for months while the PR fixing it\nwaited on a CLA.\n\nAdds cspell with a word list covering the site''s vocabulary, wires it into the\nlint script and the lint CI job, and fixes what it found: refrence, a\nConcatinating heading, nummber, testLolcalStorage and scollbar. The deliberate\nmisspellings that teach something -- cosnole in the development guide, prefx in\nthe loader options example, and webpack 1''s real OccurenceOrderPlugin -- get a\nfile-local cspell:ignore instead of a dictionary entry, so the same word\nelsewhere is still an error.","tree":{"sha":"4a188f3bc20d8592bd19f5770661d4461a9d4899","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/4a188f3bc20d8592bd19f5770661d4461a9d4899"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/0ba16baf78ac26561f84fe04e4dcf0d843ac139e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a188f3bc20d8592bd19f5770661d4461a9d4899\nparent ee1b9ec5b77a245cf49d3b33fe4b63ab14f68ca9\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789318899 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789318899 +0300\n\nci: catch typos with cspell, and fix the five it found (#8404)\n\nThe site had no spellchecker: vale runs proselint and Speciesism, neither of\nwhich checks spelling, so a misspelling only ever got caught by a reader. That\nis why refrence sat in the TypeScript guide for months while the PR fixing it\nwaited on a CLA.\n\nAdds cspell with a word list covering the site''s vocabulary, wires it into the\nlint script and the lint CI job, and fixes what it found: refrence, a\nConcatinating heading, nummber, testLolcalStorage and scollbar. The deliberate\nmisspellings that teach something -- cosnole in the development guide, prefx in\nthe loader options example, and webpack 1''s real OccurenceOrderPlugin -- get a\nfile-local cspell:ignore instead of a dictionary entry, so the same word\nelsewhere is still an error.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqptbzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcDEQAKmf4nlkzUFP6sewqGQ+Vtn7\n/k+IWBe3SIBBYsBepMZ7gA9cgRJC4JGWpvILeAXnnkgpGWbc5oUXQdoapUUc3Q6V\nHMxX9Iwk+wmuSTIT8O6n6