hub.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/305e4e3ac9a2c74d289a1d4980a55da1b1cedede/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:13:09Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:13:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(output): say where an ESM build names its chunks (#8387)\n\n* docs(output): say where an ESM build names its chunks\n\n`output.chunkFilename` still described the chunk id to filename map as the only\nway a chunk is named. Since 5.111.0 an `output.module` build loading through a\nnative `import()` holds a literal specifier per chunk in the chunk loader, so the\nname is in the runtime chunk rather than in every module importing it.\n\nDrops the analyzable-bailout row for a chunk the compilation emits no javascript\nfor, which is no longer reported: such a chunk is simply left out of that map.\n\n* docs(output): keep the chunk naming note under the line limit\n\nmarkdownlint caps a line at 600 characters and the note ran to 715.","tree":{"sha":"4441e05d6a95948580c1424e2d569f6b101fedf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/4441e05d6a95948580c1424e2d569f6b101fedf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/305e4e3ac9a2c74d289a1d4980a55da1b1cedede","verification":{"payload":"tree 4441e05d6a95948580c1424e2d569f6b101fedf6\nparent 9a547b6057a6d3d376a29b055b468729fc64f0bc\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789294389 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789294389 +0300\n\ndocs(output): say where an ESM build names its chunks (#8387)\n\n* docs(output): say where an ESM build names its chunks\n\n`output.chunkFilename` still described the chunk id to filename map as the only\nway a chunk is named. Since 5.111.0 an `output.module` build loading through a\nnative `import()` holds a literal specifier per chunk in the chunk loader, so the\nname is in the runtime chunk rather than in every module importing it.\n\nDrops the analyzable-bailout row for a chunk the compilation emits no javascript\nfor, which is no longer reported: such a chunk is simply left out of that map.\n\n* docs(output): keep the chunk naming note under the line limit\n\nmarkdownlint caps a line at 600 characters and the note ran to 715.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpnc1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIlIQAD/pD++oAnl5QFmWGN3dOjbt\nzWAocCmkCmQ9bF0aHAvJOKz9enRUo/rX4dT7QdyqZTYPSnCGQQGBEFbQKhi6cjQs\nf95KfV2dQRu72V5dk/SSA43g3EeR3RjLcoIb70351jQUkwbyyHe3lj+ObHw6jXsM\nUmSJb9dF0LBTGXRlz38AxAz0rD7mnj6ShN9R9X0DOQdo4kWDDsY7oeryQj3dk1oP\ny+EVRC5J/Xr9qUGOR6h5lOziljNGd4FLkuSl4iO2eoQbEvWzKxqJV6JSVQ7Dw53F\npZdULkCMARBXK+lCLTlhCt0UiaDBwFOGhT19AlWnAedSorxpLbuxIS50bBEg0eYf\nlyH7DITaB0iQofKg4bJ5ZjnsrSXE+UOON7Aw3P096CHAIOdj4UGrx2obauzmzu9y\nN31TWaCujNlugnSUn71Lnyy8JQl4WsXvye/3MzoM7zzPWtIa7iMj+EVQuAKGy6Fa\nVXUy8EskdtQy2yKHRmOfN0prTdAKP2LQxKnmQKZaqpOsOUkT6oAOUU4ONBGoGsZJ\n3Omhs