df97c64a57c757a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/41d557bbc3140016fda74105adf97c64a57c757a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/2630f1b0ac2d169b84dd19a93777d3420c6e3bc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:24:53Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T17:24:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): update dependencies (#8386)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies\n\nUpdates everything that can move without an upstream block or a code\nmigration: babel, react 19.3, eslint-config-webpack, autoprefixer,\nlint-staged, webpack-bundle-analyzer, react-refresh 0.19, cypress 16 and\n@docsearch/react 5.\n\nThree are left where they are, each for a reason outside this repo:\n\n- eslint 10 - eslint-plugin-react''s latest (7.37.5) peer-caps at eslint\n  ^9.7 and calls context.getFilename(), which eslint 10 removed.\n- eslint-plugin-cypress 7 - requires eslint >= 10, so it waits on the above.\n- react-router 8 - react-router-dom has no v8 and hard-pins react-router\n  7.18.3, so v8 means migrating every import off react-router-dom; v8 is\n  also ESM only and the jest suites cannot load it as CommonJS.\n\n* chore(deps): keep @docsearch/react on 4.x\n\nv5 replaces the single indexName prop with an indices array, so the\nNavigation component throws \"Must supply at least one `indices` entry for\nDocSearch\" on every page. That is an API migration rather than a version\nbump, so it goes with react-router 8 into a PR of its own.\n\n* chore(deps): keep cypress on 15.x\n\nCypress 16 runs Chrome on the native browser network instead of routing\nthrough Cypress, and 16.0.0 has two service-worker regressions fixed only\nin an unreleased 16.0.1. The site registers a Workbox service worker whose\ncatch handler falls back to the empty app shell, so scroll.cy.js loses the\npage content it asserts on.\n\n* chore(deps): drop autoprefixer\n\nwebpack''s CSS minifier maintains vendor prefixes from the same browserslist,\nadding what a target needs and stripping what none does. Feeding it the\nautoprefixed stylesheet and the unprefixed one emits byte-identical CSS, so\nautoprefixer never reached the bundle. Site CSS is 11 gzip bytes larger: three\ninert -webkit-backdrop-filter entries in transition-property lists that\nautoprefixer used to prune.\n\nThe native CSS guide already documents this.\n\n* chore(deps): drop lightningcss\n\nNothing imports it. It came in with css-loader, mini-css-extract-plugin and\ncss-minimizer-webpack-plugin, whose minifier it backed; those went when the\nsite moved to experiments.css and this stayed. @tailwindcss/postcss carries\nits own nested copy, so Tailwind is unaffected, and npm ci stops fetching a\nsecond set of native binaries.\n\nOn the site''s stylesheet webpack''s minifier emits 45923 raw / 9811 gzip\nagainst lightningcss''s 46880 / 9845.","tree":{"sha":"9949fc0be8cb79d89535c7d13ba8ddc3ad15f0c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/9949fc0be8cb79d89535c7d13ba8ddc3ad15f0c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/2630f1b0ac2d169b84dd19a93777d3420c6e3bc8","verification":{"payload":"tree 9949fc0be8cb79d89535c7d13ba8ddc3ad15f0c8\nparent 9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789233893 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789233893 +0300\n\nchore(deps): update dependencies (#8386)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies\n\nUpdates everything that can move without an upstream block or a code\nmigration: babel, react 19.3, eslint-config-webpack, autoprefixer,\nlint-staged, webpack-bundle-analyzer, react-refresh 0.19, cypress 16 and\n@docsearch/react 5.\n\nThree are left where they are, each for a reason outside this repo:\n\n- eslint 10 - eslint-plugin-react''s latest (7.37.5) peer-caps at eslint\n  ^9.7 and calls context.getFilename(), which eslint 10 removed.\n- eslint-plugin-cypress 7 - requires eslint >= 10, so it waits on the above.\n- react-router 8 - react-router-dom has no v8 and hard-pins react-router\n  7.18.3, so v8 means migrating every import off react-router-dom; v8 is\n  also ESM only and the jest suites cannot load it as CommonJS.\n\n* chore(deps): keep @docsearch/react on 4.x\n\nv5 replaces the single indexName prop with an indices array, so the\nNavigation component throws \"Must supply at least one `indices` entry for\nDocSearch\" on every page. That is an API migration rather than a version\nbump, so it goes with react-router 8 into a PR of its own.\n\n* chore(deps): keep cypress on 15.x\n\nCypress 16 runs Chrome on the native browser network instead of routing\nthrough Cypress, and 16.0.0 has two service-worker regressions fixed only\nin an unreleased 16.0.1. The site registers a Workbox service worker whose\ncatch handler falls back to the empty app shell, so scroll.cy.js loses the\npage content it asserts on.\n\n* chore(deps): drop autoprefixer\n\nwebpack''s CSS minifier maintains vendor prefixes from the same browserslist,\nadding what a target needs and stripping what none does. Feeding it the\nautoprefixed stylesheet and the unprefixed one emits byte-identical CSS, so\nautoprefixer never reached the bundle. Site CSS is 11 gzip bytes larger: three\ninert -webkit-backdrop-filter entries in transition-property lists that\nautoprefixer used to prune.\n\nThe native CSS guide already documents this.\n\n* chore(deps): drop lightningcss\n\nNothing imports it. It came in with css-loader, mini-css-extract-plugin and\ncss-minimizer-webpack-plugin, whose minifier it backed; those went when the\nsite moved to experiments.css and this stayed. @tailwindcss/postcss carries\nits own nested copy, so Tailwind is unaffected, and npm ci stops fetching a\nsecond set of native binaries.\n\nOn the site''s stylesheet webpack''s minifier emits 45923 raw / 9811 gzip\nagainst lightningcss''s 46880 / 9845.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpYrlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyGUQAKx46Hhjy/8BH9zGgkBffPAw\nm/hT+w4ZNj+UmnsG6pQ3ULLyDYAd1e/YkWKCrzVD4PzOZQ8XEWP52JgQkoBEPOiU\ncsr6qn7yiYwoxMtSA2ncak+yl1Jy08uTwBydR0WeGIx9PIfpDPfycLcoNYS6VlvZ\nKO0XJ3aHfEyvrTk1ClEveOzaot7ElEwazBCT6eunShFqrUpjBvLJoBFFL70E5aVw\nRuU30ce4kyMI2X1mC2VVjp/DZlezQOGVi62MSG8CFEKiws3maOU5NI/8nfeK54s8\n/h/pWJdIQpcOIBy8O3S0yACigwkQZchqz7vmqDwI5w+xQiGSWXjfqFGC2A6VuPPi\nnuuU5bVsqFQJ2EO1IfGjfxIIRluh3BRovFEATPoxJ4CmoCmN4JZlfdkF0L0ciL/i\n0ihgFHb1yGM+zvrsUh4Cy+EFJspkWUB3YavM+N9aepTp2dlH9ZRK2SehxHpwOvUX\nBfYOCrnW2cZCeRy2TO2M6ATo5MujaeRsB38y3fLDy9uiYXiHHZ4Ha9+BHuxq6qNf\nHFlZdNLd4JpmIw6d3Kx1x5/Q8RRUMF8/9cVSfjIpaZ5ZoLUUQmJtWo5Tb1JW9bwr\nXyQ2JdfBMEHaMPUj9i6uUp5+awj9jt+npCKpDWsY7WPo3b2TX7Gljt/vyh4/vgeM\nybcJT194BWszbbKE3vy3\n=gBVo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T17:24:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/2630f1b0ac2d169b84dd19a93777d3420c6e3bc8","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKDI2MzBmMWIwYWMyZDE2OWI4NGRkMTlhOTM3NzdkMzQyMGM2ZTNiYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c","sha":"9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c"}],"sha":"2630f1b0ac2d169b84dd19a93777d3420c6e3bc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/2630f1b0ac2d169b84dd19a93777d3420c6e3bc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T15:51:12Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T15:51:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: say which hook a plugin creates assets in (#8385)\n\nThe compiler''s emit hook runs after the compilation is sealed, so an asset\nadded there skips every processAssets stage and webpack reports the write as\ndeprecated. Nothing in the docs said so, and the plugins concept page had no\nguidance for plugin authors at all.\n\nCloses #2864","tree":{"sha":"7b4404b86381b052ff25ab2727d4c7f65cb1b259","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/7b4404b86381b052ff25ab2727d4c7f65cb1b259"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b4404b86381b052ff25ab2727d4c7f65cb1b259\nparent 083f982a51caa5bcec77a0d4f13d2c494d611dfc\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789228272 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789228272 +0300\n\ndocs: say which hook a plugin creates assets in (#8385)\n\nThe compiler''s emit hook runs after the compilation is sealed, so an asset\nadded there skips every processAssets stage and webpack reports the write as\ndeprecated. Nothing in the docs said so, and the plugins concept page had no\nguidance for plugin authors at all.\n\nCloses #2864","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpXTwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVvEQAGAXUPaqPbwe/GJ6yVV6Lf0A\naAFpphJJ6cb4nnKpsKQiocVO4vOUPfpXj7wLprXdEtn5Wg5Zc/dGIPlfAOwz2YBe\nd1PpbIlVa/OwkQCh2vr+9Bug+XLCawvsX3E7LSJacEbMdg9+c2vfG6eDVo1WAyqe\nK7Q0/ENnC8PQh/73fHZhmAWDcJ+YxZ7R14EJl9Am9WhzDJLctKnHwqJE5dt7zqwL\nN9G3H8DOJafpBlV80jKDxG4B1CXOVxN532lNYMDpg3dBdx/9yaE36vQpzbjShgrS\naXOwoOctybR/99y1yY6pF9Fg7YossS+SRLbFHnfznSVhE/DqdL4FNPqvr2XIC09h\njQdpr8u628Dy57vIjGDj11GHfeXWGYuqyCCZIZxLX4xry9Glf7NyhpkOEcyzKVHv\nIJFXcS2TSL2c/LUyCzAywrgJDUXnwqYaQtnlTTyIbjZX8U50m+E+xeoncKFrWb9D\nvTeOhc+5w6gSulB0l0/3ardXP6E/6RQD+vpS/TaSQRb/CJ+v1t07ryuKGnmJ1vtw\nbK4Zj/6NsAo5qaIoE9PTDQ8w1zon+3T3ptHslgbe9BwuqR/3r6V/1n4//wEWSWwb\n9tuSVYODfCL2PDE+YX4khI3vjbv5ZotPMKR1Rt5JpN88EBnFwcmcrgF75MUcAfTb\nAGQ3sTZ2W323IMDZPrGy\n=KTs4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T15:51:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKDk2ODhiYWNmZjQ5ZDQ0YTAyMTc5ZGI0Y2QwMWFkMmJmMTBjYTIxNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/083f982a51caa5bcec77a0d4f13d2c494d611dfc","sha":"083f982a51caa5bcec77a0d4f13d2c494d611dfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/083f982a51caa5bcec77a0d4f13d2c494d611dfc"}],"sha":"9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/9688bacff49d44a02179db4cd01ad2bf10ca216c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/083f982a51caa5bcec77a0d4f13d2c494d611dfc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T15:19:51Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T15:19:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: drop deprecated loaders and plugins from the sidebar (#8384)\n\n* docs: drop deprecated loaders and plugins from the sidebar\n\nEvery webpack-org loader and plugin page the site builds now comes from a\nrepository that is not archived. The eleven archived ones are excluded from\nthe fetch and their URLs redirect to what replaced them: native HTML, the\nbuilt-in CopyPlugin, MinimizerPlugin or DiagnosticsWebpackPlugin.\n\nAlso redirects /plugins/terser-webpack-plugin and /plugins/eslint-webpack-plugin,\nwhich 404 since those repositories were renamed.\n\n* docs: teach the shimming guide webpack''s own imports/exports recipe\n\nThe Granular Shimming and Global Exports sections taught imports-loader and\nexports-loader, both deprecated. They now use the plugin from webpack''s\nadd-imports and add-exports examples, so neither loader is mentioned anywhere\nin the docs.\n\nThe Granular Shimming example also never demonstrated the problem: it read\n`this` inside a function called bare, which is already the global object in a\nsloppy module. It now reads the module''s own `this`, which is what the wrapper\nchanges.\n\ncopy-webpack-plugin redirects to output.copy, and the two loader URLs to the\nsections that replace them.\n\n* docs: link webpack''s examples instead of inlining the shim plugin\n\nThe Granular Shimming and Global Exports sections point at the add-imports\nand add-exports examples rather than carrying a copy of the plugin, which\nwould go stale against the examples it was taken from.\n\n* docs: stop naming deprecated loaders and plugins outside the migration guides\n\nA developer reading the docs should meet the built-in feature, not the package\nit replaced. The remaining mentions in guides, configuration and API pages are\nreworded to describe the behaviour, and the three archived webpack packages are\ndropped from the awesome-webpack list.\n\nThe Native CSS and Native HTML guides keep theirs: naming what you are moving\noff is the point of a migration guide.","tree":{"sha":"ec0e91bfed5b3ca923d515631ce6ffb7cadbb020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/ec0e91bfed5b3ca923d515631ce6ffb7cadbb020"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/083f982a51caa5bcec77a0d4f13d2c494d611dfc","verification":{"payload":"tree ec0e91bfed5b3ca923d515631ce6ffb7cadbb020\nparent 3dcf6efe402f0653f747f64f0dee16472246d070\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1789226391 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789226391 +0300\n\ndocs: drop deprecated loaders and plugins from the sidebar (#8384)\n\n* docs: drop deprecated loaders and plugins from the sidebar\n\nEvery webpack-org loader and plugin page the site builds now comes from a\nrepository that is not archived. The eleven archived ones are excluded from\nthe fetch and their URLs redirect to what replaced them: native HTML, the\nbuilt-in CopyPlugin, MinimizerPlugin or DiagnosticsWebpackPlugin.\n\nAlso redirects /plugins/terser-webpack-plugin and /plugins/eslint-webpack-plugin,\nwhich 404 since those repositories were renamed.\n\n* docs: teach the shimming guide webpack''s own imports/exports recipe\n\nThe Granular Shimming and Global Exports sections taught imports-loader and\nexports-loader, both deprecated. They now use the plugin from webpack''s\nadd-imports and add-exports examples, so neither loader is mentioned anywhere\nin the docs.\n\nThe Granular Shimming example also never demonstrated the problem: it read\n`this` inside a function called bare, which is already the global object in a\nsloppy module. It now reads the module''s own `this`, which is what the wrapper\nchanges.\n\ncopy-webpack-plugin redirects to output.copy, and the two loader URLs to the\nsections that replace them.\n\n* docs: link webpack''s examples instead of inlining the shim plugin\n\nThe Granular Shimming and Global Exports sections point at the add-imports\nand add-exports examples rather than carrying a copy of the plugin, which\nwould go stale against the examples it was taken from.\n\n* docs: stop naming deprecated loaders and plugins outside the migration guides\n\nA developer reading the docs should meet the built-in feature, not the package\nit replaced. The remaining mentions in guides, configuration and API pages are\nreworded to describe the behaviour, and the three archived webpack packages are\ndropped from the awesome-webpack list.\n\nThe Native CSS and Native HTML guides keep theirs: naming what you are moving\noff is the point of a migration guide.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpW2XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwKYQABxwxK0URkQyhPbVNZqFUdt+\nT6gUeQJIIm/HJy4E4fFIru7fRuma8VE+IVBxhuW8mU3yk7WTW7JlKxtYWl4cGEiY\nBERWZVkp8iiY+vzdL4NI4UtjWcI14ijuegUXvbFLGZEQOmrOUofr0jB7V5Zxl66Y\nZ09OxYUFuuRMhfIqInMRA47felo3jf4sek41YuQC5uM7s/dD6HGFv9eNx7QQPoJr\n5YKLI83okjOk2NslSEiHNOZQ7s5wIK4HdYIhc0u3FivicVolQr9GDkr8AAanCCWC\nwwQa/92yX7+IdYSZFcnz4J0ZWPoHY1gyQxb2KJ6YmFqN3Os9miwCLnJRT7KbihHD\np2yPyGPLyX/CW+u8BSPKoAahvGFjsjM7Om+jtgoTKTuu10JNNsawHau5SB8nrfqo\n+VyTqU53T2nx1jqv6zp3+lWZc/N2p7wu0uOOKveZKzg2d9J/N509gGXVtiuznm5T\nLukbRaxZ6QLAxbwJFNaTK12rfxgm0Wkx68DtsH5zJEsZSslkL9FUt+7LnT1N+BXQ\n9f+7b09Aovt9HfFxf1pmixU6CfHSDYqAaCBi+CgKqQziYYZphxG7o0dVJPTi3WOE\nKFh7TXh0iUq6Ya1X6sKFkDj/qZ/9IjQmvTRuUWNuvDYKE6ilun7NoBtGZtNgmu3s\nml7BSVReImqq0HPy4Gec\n=oRjF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T15:19:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","i