api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/cf06dd3e64d97e1d19bc4a394cb54741d01009a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:26:15Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:26:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: give every page its own meta description (#8361)\n\n* docs: give every page its own meta description\n\nAll 136 non-blog pages shared one fallback meta description, so every page\nemitted an identical <meta name=\"description\"> and og:description. Duplicate\ndescriptions give search engines and retrieval pipelines no per-page signal,\nand Google discards them in favour of a synthesized snippet.\n\nAdd a description to each of the 132 pages that lacked one, and rewrite the\nfallback in Site.jsx. Both now reflect what webpack actually bundles and what\nit targets: JavaScript, CSS, HTML, WebAssembly and assets, for browsers,\nNode.js, Deno, Bun and other environments, rather than \"JavaScript files for\nusage in a browser\".\n\nDescriptions name the concrete options and superseded packages a reader\nsearches for, following the pattern already used by the native CSS and HTML\nguides.\n\nAlso list CSS and HTML in the native module types on concepts/modules, which\nstill enumerated only ECMAScript, CommonJS, AMD, assets and WebAssembly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDxiMfJ9FnjuLdeRkwdWPa\n\n* test: assert the home page''s own meta description\n\ncheck-server-side-rendering pinned the old fallback string and visited \"/\"\nto read it. The home page now carries its own description, so \"/\" no longer\nrenders the fallback at all and the assertion was stale twice over.\n\nPoint the assertion at the home page''s actual description and rename the\ncase to match what it covers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDxiMfJ9FnjuLdeRkwdWPa\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa285e2dc20fbfc64bb220421507bea33377cd52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/aa285e2dc20fbfc64bb220421507bea33377cd52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/cf06dd3e64d97e1d19bc4a394cb54741d01009a9","verification":{"payload":"tree aa285e2dc20fbfc64bb220421507bea33377cd52\nparent ea1c0cb1b44f43bdcfaf4e0e064167619b29e882\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788881175 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788881175 +0300\n\ndocs: give every page its own meta description (#8361)\n\n* docs: give every page its own meta description\n\nAll 136 non-blog pages shared one fallback meta description, so every page\nemitted an identical <meta name=\"description\"> and og:description. Duplicate\ndescriptions give search engines and retrieval pipelines no per-page signal,\nand Google discards them in favour of a synthesized snippet.\n\nAdd a description to each of the 132 pages that lacked one, and rewrite the\nfallback in Site.jsx. Both now reflect what webpack actually bundles and what\nit targets: JavaScript, CSS, HTML, WebAssembly and assets, for browsers,\nNode.js, Deno, Bun and other environments, rather than \"JavaScript files for\nusage in a browser\".\n\nDescriptions name the concrete options and superseded packages a reader\nsearches for, following the pattern already used by the native CSS and HTML\nguides.\n\nAlso list CSS and HTML in the native module types on concepts/modules, which\nstill enumerated only ECMAScript, CommonJS, AMD, assets and WebAssembly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDxiMfJ9FnjuLdeRkwdWPa\n\n* test: assert the home page''s own meta description\n\ncheck-server-side-rendering pinned the old fallback string and visited \"/\"\nto read it. The home page now carries its own description, so \"/\" no longer\nrenders the fallback at all and the assertion was stale twice over.\n\nPoint the assertion at the home page''s actual description and rename the\ncase to match what it covers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDxiMfJ9FnjuLdeRkwdWPa\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoCkXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd1gQAHd/Pc4T3Z/IfmEOG5ymydYL\nD8iocC2QP0g0iCS49jSYO8geklCnXa5K6A3bzQTZYYRrAzu7YyKsfz3U1w1mq9N5\nU5qcgNsl1Q4MXp9eX+OHH4MJkAb34Z2M5yk3BenG+z5J/tVX2SFi4fLhUF8xXRuG\nxWIc3jcUiV5QrYtCbOcsaW2YP/HcQRJZPIubR4yHH8+r+IWR9pW35oZJTve5LAG+\nkRgv+0KIc8EVeJum+6OMTZhMC1zIoJTUotxEd3Zt2F01wLom8XEwSbFviQvqDIGX\nHgUt32aS/URqvzxYN7I2ptuBdb0DfN1s2sVblUjORlq+w5lqZzr9Hxk2XDnbPvOH\nzl98jVMbrN46iv5RI7naArKfE/XHWFFrBVxyXuObd20iGtu1MClmXTpSByMf3aiY\n+CCUoJ1LMDr0/yNVSlLbQmF2SEqydbW1eVW18XrTJkf6aVb8n9IqFyHhTHNCKY70\nQFm2q5rlx1wQia8DqprSAUaVEC3tsDWDRdg8RqIH+tXVVy1mZVhITzeD5KamcgHE\nF6V0fGbQdR7UYOZrZqQbfves/ADYiT3TR10IKsPhsFRAFIyLTrf/t9IYhEj8nb2h\nTPm5Ex1ExeH7A0zCDoM27NMWynY1Ip9lnYCX9WS1tESs77r7XjDoWR+zJ8hdoUBD\n++OB5EJQSzjEAWEm45Ho\n=RDrI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T15:26:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/cf06dd3e64d97e1d19bc4a394cb54741d01009a9","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKGNmMDZkZDNlNjRkOTdlMWQxOWJjNGEzOTRjYjU0NzQxZDAxMDA5YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/ea1c0cb1b44f43bdcfaf4e0e064167619b29e882","sha":"ea1c0cb1b44f43bdcfaf4e0e064167619b29e882","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/ea1c0cb1b44f43bdcfaf4e0e064167619b29e882"}],"sha":"cf06dd3e64d97e1d19bc4a394cb54741d01009a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/cf06dd3e64d97e1d19bc4a394cb54741d01009a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/ea1c0cb1b44f43bdcfaf4e0e064167619b29e882/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:49:37Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:49:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: teach the docs native HTML and CSS, drop html-webpack-plugin and the CSS loaders (#8355)\n\n* docs: drop html-webpack-plugin from the guides and reference\n\nThe guide series taught HtmlWebpackPlugin and each page carried a note\nexplaining why it had not moved to the built-in HTML support yet. Webpack\nbuilds pages itself, so the guides now use it and the plugin is no longer\nnamed anywhere outside the migration guide.\n\noutput-management makes src/index.html the entry point: the page lists the\nscripts it needs, webpack rewrites their URLs to the emitted bundles, and\nthere is no second list of entry points to keep in sync. development, HMR\nand PWA follow that config through, and caching uses output.html since it\nkeeps a single JavaScript entry. Every build listing in those guides was\nregenerated against webpack 5.110.3.\n\nScripts a page references become chunks of that page, so their names are\ngenerated (__html_<hash>_<n>) rather than taken from entry. That is what\nthe listings show now, with a note in output-management and caching saying\nwhere the names come from.\n\n/plugins/html-webpack-plugin is removed and redirects to the Native HTML\nguide, which documents the plugin''s options and their built-in equivalents.\nThe plugins index links there instead of to the deleted page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: build the front page example with native HTML and CSS\n\nThe splash example bundled one JavaScript file and asked the reader to\nwrite the page by hand, pointing a <script> tag at dist/bundle.js. Webpack\nhandles all three now, so the example starts from src/index.html: the page\nlinks a stylesheet and a script, entry points at the page, and the emitted\ndocument is shown next to the config with its URLs rewritten to the hashed\nassets. Verified against webpack 5.110.3 — an HTML entry turns on the html\nand css support on its own, and htmlFilename keeps the page''s name out of\nthe contenthash pattern.\n\nThe migration guide''s companion-plugin table now covers the popular\nhtml-webpack-plugin ecosystem rather than five entries, and a new section\nmaps its six hooks onto HtmlModulesPlugin''s, with a plugin rewritten\nthrough transformTags and injectTags as the worked example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: drop css-loader, style-loader and MiniCssExtractPlugin from the docs\n\nWebpack handles CSS itself, so the three packages are no longer named\noutside the migration guide, and their pages are gone: css-loader and\nstyle-loader join the excluded loaders, MiniCssExtractPlugin the excluded\nplugins, and /loaders/css-loader, /loaders/style-loader and\n/plugins/mini-css-extract-plugin redirect to the Native CSS guide. The\nexclusion entries carry the webpack/ prefix the repositories actually\nhave; the older webpack-contrib/ spellings around them no longer match\nanything the fetcher lists.\n\nThe HMR guide stops installing style-loader and css-loader for its\nstylesheet section: experiments.css defaults to ''auto'', so importing a\nstylesheet needs no rule at all — webpack bundles it and links it into the\npage, verified against webpack 5.110.3. The remaining mentions were\nreference asides (a filter option, an ident-hash comment, an exports\nconvention, the CSS extraction bullet) and now describe the behavior\nwithout naming a package, linking the guide where a reader needs more.\n\nLeft alone: the Native CSS migration guide, which has to name what it\nmigrates from, and the release posts and the v1-to-v2 migration guide,\nwhere the loaders are part of the record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: name a page''s bundles after its entry in the build listings\n\nwebpack/webpack#22008 gives a page''s extracted scripts the entry''s\nfilename now that the page emits no JavaScript of its own, so the guides\nstop showing generated identifiers. output-management and development list\nmain.bundle.js and main1.bundle.js for the two scripts the page pulls in,\nthe PWA listing follows in the same format, and caching is back to\nmain.<contenthash>.js beside runtime and vendors — its note about generated\nchunk names is gone and the prose names the main bundle again.\n\nEvery listing was regenerated against that branch (84c1155): a page with\ntwo scripts emits main.bundle.js and main1.bundle.js, and the caching setup\nemits main.<hash>.js, vendors.<hash>.js and runtime.<hash>.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* test: use postcss-loader as the package the site has a page for\n\nThe two owner-rename tests used css-loader as their example, and this\nbranch stops building a css-loader page, so the \"has a page\" assertion\nno longer holds. postcss-loader is the same shape — a webpack-owned\nloader the site still builds a page for — and keeps both tests testing\nwhat they were written for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs(config): document the validate option\n\ndiagnostics-webpack-plugin''s README links to\n/configuration/other-options/#validate, and the anchor did not exist:\nwebpack has had a top-level `validate` option since 5.106.0, and this\npage never covered it. That dead fragment fails the link check on any\nbuild, this branch included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7d439818ac948c38c0298e6d4089c43255d23b92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/7d439818ac948c38c0298e6d4089c43255d23b92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/ea1c0cb1b44f43bdcfaf4e0e064167619b29e882","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d439818ac948c38c0298e6d4089c43255d23b92\nparent f2b7266dcba16c1be29d4d3c01d6f89d3930bcd3\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788860977 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788860977 +0300\n\ndocs: teach the docs native HTML and CSS, drop html-webpack-plugin and the CSS loaders (#8355)\n\n* docs: drop html-webpack-plugin from the guides and reference\n\nThe guide series taught HtmlWebpackPlugin and each page carried a note\nexplaining why it had not moved to the built-in HTML support yet. Webpack\nbuilds pages itself, so the guides now use it and the plugin is no longer\nnamed anywhere outside the migration guide.\n\noutput-management makes src/index.html the entry point: the page lists the\nscripts it needs, webpack rewrites their URLs to the emitted bundles, and\nthere is no second list of entry points to keep in sync. development, HMR\nand PWA follow that config through, and caching uses output.html since it\nkeeps a single JavaScript entry. Every build listing in those guides was\nregenerated against webpack 5.110.3.\n\nScripts a page references become chunks of that page, so their names are\ngenerated (__html_<hash>_<n>) rather than taken from entry. That is what\nthe listings show now, with a note in output-management and caching saying\nwhere the names come from.\n\n/plugins/html-webpack-plugin is removed and redirects to the Native HTML\nguide, which documents the plugin''s options and their built-in equivalents.\nThe plugins index links there instead of to the deleted page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: build the front page example with native HTML and CSS\n\nThe splash example bundled one JavaScript file and asked the reader to\nwrite the page by hand, pointing a <script> tag at dist/bundle.js. Webpack\nhandles all three now, so the example starts from src/index.html: the page\nlinks a stylesheet and a script, entry points at the page, and the emitted\ndocument is shown next to the config with its URLs rewritten to the hashed\nassets. Verified against webpack 5.110.3 — an HTML entry turns on the html\nand css support on its own, and htmlFilename keeps the page''s name out of\nthe contenthash pattern.\n\nThe migration guide''s companion-plugin table now covers the popular\nhtml-webpack-plugin ecosystem rather than five entries, and a new section\nmaps its six hooks onto HtmlModulesPlugin''s, with a plugin rewritten\nthrough transformTags and injectTags as the worked example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: drop css-loader, style-loader and MiniCssExtractPlugin from the docs\n\nWebpack handles CSS itself, so the three packages are no longer named\noutside the migration guide, and their pages are gone: css-loader and\nstyle-loader join the excluded loaders, MiniCssExtractPlugin the excluded\nplugins, and /loaders/css-loader, /loaders/style-loader and\n/plugins/mini-css-extract-plugin redirect to the Native CSS guide. The\nexclusion entries carry the webpack/ prefix the repositories actually\nhave; the older webpack-contrib/ spellings around them no longer match\nanything the fetcher lists.\n\nThe HMR guide stops installing style-loader and css-loader for its\nstylesheet section: experiments.css defaults to ''auto'', so importing a\nstylesheet needs no rule at all — webpack bundles it and links it into the\npage, verified against webpack 5.110.3. The remaining mentions were\nreference asides (a filter option, an ident-hash comment, an exports\nconvention, the CSS extraction bullet) and now describe the behavior\nwithout naming a package, linking the guide where a reader needs more.\n\nLeft alone: the Native CSS migration guide, which has to name what it\nmigrates from, and the release posts and the v1-to-v2 migration guide,\nwhere the loaders are part of the record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: name a page''s bundles after its entry in the build listings\n\nwebpack/webpack#22008 gives a page''s extracted scripts the entry''s\nfilename now that the page emits no JavaScript of its own, so the guides\nstop showing generated identifiers. output-management and development list\nmain.bundle.js and main1.bundle.js for the two scripts the page pulls in,\nthe PWA listing follows in the same format, and caching is back to\nmain.<contenthash>.js beside runtime and vendors — its note about generated\nchunk names is gone and the prose names the main bundle again.\n\nEvery listing was regenerated against that branch (84c1155): a page with\ntwo scripts emits main.bundle.js and main1.bundle.js, and the caching setup\nemits main.<hash>.js, vendors.<hash>.js and runtime.<hash>.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* test: use postcss-loader as the package the site has a page for\n\nThe two owner-rename tests used css-loader as their example, and this\nbranch stops building a css-loader page, so the \"has a page\" assertion\nno longer holds. postcss-loader is the same shape — a webpack-owned\nloader the site still builds a page for — and keeps both tests testing\nwhat they were written for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs(config): document the validate option\n\ndiagnostics-webpack-plugin''s README links to\n/configuration/other-options/#validate, and the anchor did not exist:\nwebpack has had a top-level `validate` option since 5.106.0, and this\npage never covered it. That dead fragment fails the link check on any\nbuild, this branch included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn9oxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQjsQAAH4YREbqVV+GUroAYc15XFU\nneLU0NYUhPWRuLFKEMTlddUc8iSDqOUb8QXGb8HOfUF2qyB4z9n7ldy6ar2Is7EY\n2Jsc0QLdtg/lZeAMI2NYY95XM2vMaH0wMVVcra3SHuBKVkh/lx9XCaOlPiS75reK\nxZ0IMLdeZGRLIW1Suzm3BFz3wxbvmWmjxtwY1RQELNvVRrT+nz74yPyRLLJfFF5l\nBv+28QSbP/vMfYv/ER3FegKv3tQSHZmPp1pejKSMpzJNn5JZfn35vijmlJWxrcAO\nkbiUXtNfmhhTJ1fK9hWS2xD1YPMePp162WCIAzofL/2B8vhGDfDthW7hTF2biRUb\ncmFH88sj3g53bM/AmVR+tfUeVwcj