.org/commits/c8c2c04485cd45d15d057a87301fbd3065e56832"}],"sha":"e12940fc960e5758023bb5b729082aa8d02cec41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/e12940fc960e5758023bb5b729082aa8d02cec41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/c8c2c04485cd45d15d057a87301fbd3065e56832/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:18:48Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T16:18:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(config): document output.copy and the CopyPlugin behind it (#8353)\n\n* docs(config): document output.copy and the CopyPlugin behind it\n\nwebpack copies files itself since 5.111.0. Adds the output.copy reference\nwith its pattern, glob and transform options, a CopyPlugin page for the\nconcurrency and stage options output.copy does not carry, and lists the\nplugin in the index, marking copy-webpack-plugin as superseded.\n\n* fix(ci): satisfy the sort lint rule and point the index at lint-webpack-plugin\n\nThe CopyPlugin merge example sorted with Array#sort, which unicorn/no-array-sort\nrejects; toSorted does the same on the array filter already returned.\n\nThe link check was failing on /plugins/eslint-webpack-plugin, which the plugins\nindex still lists. webpack/eslint-webpack-plugin was renamed to\nwebpack/lint-webpack-plugin (it now runs ESLint and Stylelint and replaces\nstylelint-webpack-plugin too), so the org listing the page generator walks no\nlonger carries the old name and no page is built for it. The entry now names the\nrenamed plugin. This failure predates the branch — it reproduces on unrelated\nPRs — but it blocks this one, so it is fixed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n* fix(plugins): follow the rename to diagnostics-webpack-plugin\n\nThe plugin that replaced eslint-webpack-plugin and stylelint-webpack-plugin was\nrenamed again, from lint-webpack-plugin to diagnostics-webpack-plugin, since it\nnow covers type checkers and other diagnostic tools rather than linters alone.\nThe org listing the plugin pages are generated from carries only the new name,\nso the index entry follows it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n* fix(build): only link a README''s package when the site builds its page\n\nprocess-readme rewrote every github.com/webpack{,-contrib}/*-loader and\n*-plugin URL into an internal docs link, whether or not a page for that\npackage exists. stylelint-webpack-plugin''s README points at\nwebpack/lint-webpack-plugin, which has since been renamed again, so the\ngenerated page carried a link to /plugins/lint-webpack-plugin/ and the link\ncheck failed on it.\n\nThe rewrite is now gated on the repository lists the pages are generated\nfrom, which fetch-package-readmes passes in: a package missing from them\nkeeps its GitHub link, which redirects to wherever the repository moved,\ninstead of pointing at a page that was never built. Without the lists the\nbehaviour is unchanged, so processReadme keeps working on its own.\n\nAlso strips the trailing slash a matched URL may carry before building the\ninternal path and comparing against the exclusion lists, which those two\ncomparisons already assumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"408bd9bfa8504fb1d057ea851fe51e58b30451e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/408bd9bfa8504fb1d057ea851fe51e58b30451e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/c8c2c04485cd45d15d057a87301fbd3065e56832","verification":{"payload":"tree 408bd9bfa8504fb1d057ea851fe51e58b30451e0\nparent 3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788797928 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788797928 +0300\n\ndocs(config): document output.copy and the CopyPlugin behind it (#8353)\n\n* docs(config): document output.copy and the CopyPlugin behind it\n\nwebpack copies files itself since 5.111.0. Adds the output.copy reference\nwith its pattern, glob and transform options, a CopyPlugin page for the\nconcurrency and stage options output.copy does not carry, and lists the\nplugin in the index, marking copy-webpack-plugin as superseded.\n\n* fix(ci): satisfy the sort lint rule and point the index at lint-webpack-plugin\n\nThe CopyPlugin merge example sorted with Array#sort, which unicorn/no-array-sort\nrejects; toSorted does the same on the array filter already returned.\n\nThe link check was failing on /plugins/eslint-webpack-plugin, which the plugins\nindex still lists. webpack/eslint-webpack-plugin was renamed to\nwebpack/lint-webpack-plugin (it now runs ESLint and Stylelint and replaces\nstylelint-webpack-plugin too), so the org listing the page generator walks no\nlonger carries the old name and no page is built for it. The entry now names the\nrenamed plugin. This failure predates the branch — it reproduces on unrelated\nPRs — but it blocks this one, so it is fixed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n* fix(plugins): follow the rename to diagnostics-webpack-plugin\n\nThe plugin that replaced eslint-webpack-plugin and stylelint-webpack-plugin was\nrenamed again, from lint-webpack-plugin to diagnostics-webpack-plugin, since it\nnow covers type checkers and other diagnostic tools rather than linters alone.\nThe org listing the plugin pages are generated from carries only the new name,\nso the index entry follows it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n* fix(build): only link a README''s package when the site builds its page\n\nprocess-readme rewrote every github.com/webpack{,-contrib}/*-loader and\n*-plugin URL into an internal docs link, whether or not a page for that\npackage exists. stylelint-webpack-plugin''s README points at\nwebpack/lint-webpack-plugin, which has since been renamed again, so the\ngenerated page carried a link to /plugins/lint-webpack-plugin/ and the link\ncheck failed on it.\n\nThe rewrite is now gated on the repository lists the pages are generated\nfrom, which fetch-package-readmes passes in: a package missing from them\nkeeps its GitHub link, which redirects to wherever the repository moved,\ninstead of pointing at a page that was never built. Without the lists the\nbehaviour is unchanged, so processReadme keeps working on its own.\n\nAlso strips the trailing slash a matched URL may carry before building the\ninternal path and comparing against the exclusion lists, which those two\ncomparisons already assumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnuPoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtRcQAEs62+hbjIYEO7ocEOWnghHD\ndsj8iHI0j8/2qNwNqy7I9uB/TaWtpDrni0JvFIJurfTbVK7WRM7+oEi+dNWMCBuk\n5EtEunl//2TyJnaEqL6mS4wtwCjklZTi8mnLd+Wf2KgA32GyVrTGeoRxsIpZjm0u\ni4qlYhpWmOs0m+mbp5+1wFsVG3/f7KbMDo8V6K4gX/gNQYjaskCr9iW2tjUpt8Hd\nFrzXs8hAXelELlUvtqb5x/zm0UwKBxPtz0kiHTC3pzZFI+0OG+CetNJmc6YgKPCK\np8SVR2W1ruTWVjX2Fl5H24UKeDt4veCOQSSLwFdWmzsT26xuVAikwa/IaayNS5Fy\nwjFG5I1I/sj+jM0TM2lbhtOyqOfrTt1h/P9I3DpAhRJdOt4vZ0Qc8nN1hiopKpvb\n/4K5mv12FucvuCy3i122d6JXdobUjZBBQt5S/iNNGwqy5vlqEj25deKnw+aMLLcm\nDSgvPJfzXUOvdCiw99wPaiMR+Y4r/fe/+hVFluKSBQop1CcJiRV0xrJ4yYEUrZZF\n0FCIMZRATm6gXzS5UpA3pa7IlBKsy5Cz5WUh+spq1jB5joIKHq5uBjlWJxaH/Zwr\nC90LWy53PD+AppbmsLCGV2jyrfezctyUNhMlqqZaUzPIZxZ7M68H4lvkUFIYouq/\nKC0JJ3vQR4uBIFcKYxiU\n=yYwp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T16:18:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/c8c2c04485cd45d15d057a87301fbd3065e56832","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKGM4YzJjMDQ0ODVjZDQ1ZDE1ZDA1N2E4NzMwMWZiZDMwNjVlNTY4MzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342","sha":"3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342"}],"sha":"c8c2c04485cd45d15d057a87301fbd3065e56832","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/c8c2c04485cd45d15d057a87301fbd3065e56832"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T21:03:51Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T21:03:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(performance): document the grouped hint options (#8350)\n\n* docs(performance): document the grouped hint options\n\n* docs(performance): name the renamed checks and the federation ones\n\nThe seven names 5.110.0 shipped were removed when the checks were grouped,\nand webpack rejects an unknown property, so a config still using one fails\nvalidation rather than being ignored. Give them a table pointing at what\nreplaced each.\n\nAlso record that `unusedConfig` now covers Module Federation, including the\ncase that stays silent today: an exact `shared` key matches only the exact\nrequest, so it shares nothing next to a deep import.","tree":{"sha":"30769792b35f409c05d3a1a4daebd73173b40be7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/30769792b35f409c05d3a1a4daebd73173b40be7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342","verification":{"payload":"tree 30769792b35f409c05d3a1a4daebd73173b40be7\nparent e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788728631 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788728631 +0300\n\ndocs(performance): document the grouped hint options (#8350)\n\n* docs(performance): document the grouped hint options\n\n* docs(performance): name the renamed checks and the federation ones\n\nThe seven names 5.110.0 shipped were removed when the checks were grouped,\nand webpack rejects an unknown property, so a config still using one fails\nvalidation rather than being ignored. Give them a table pointing at what\nreplaced each.\n\nAlso record that `unusedConfig` now covers Module Federation, including the\ncase that stays silent today: an exact `shared` key matches only the exact\nrequest, so it shares nothing next to a deep import.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqndU3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmEcQAKRw5MzErJJBPkOVZsH3ecsQ\n1wZf55eokPm+PfMyKws3tbYB2quv+/wef+q4xIj5IzM3D/YGqseBB1KSMxkGIcQ3\nAs1cRXDjBhwUK77eW8zuPfxtyMchr/ODKgXjrhk/Rv9cg+506vLvvAYmLIOMPVC4\nh6a9F3FX16uarAZg0m5THO45DNC0qpSafeG6O+nllxpY7Ejfc+xXGgCHcJEIdETX\nsVB4KjBhI9zZHd7yJlX+IEUmTWrQbUK7PUTNDfSt6ByUEkfG8DqYPuR46XSS/fNC\nKvcKqo5KXsVUG4u3lCuBr5lCxDYuYmmCcTec/hUfRTff8Ir4D7NEUS/iy00I0YEw\nuL3iaGk/JTIhoYl8gP62X/0tKucxqi0V9AUszGuWlOoHj628aMm/sQt71WuQrm0r\nH4zn0biKfshsx8hkB5QNlipUj2cDIt3rBpesM82LJTYNeHWSMpls5FXQ6gB5gy04\njdPyt5OlGBtnUYkX6SvGF7SmPLZWtf/WXIKgPCxS/DBonqcP2bbUQPb9J5QQUUi6\nNaL8RsfgCQ11uOh11VE1+MbRvieA/IEfqz5pwHigshEBsDXyC2Er/MhAqn+CqcgO\nPhNJ0E6hViownj4lzRdpg55RqjyCc1u/gdEhwmg4I4UnPAXmzlk5tDn8acouWT7B\nLBLHwLO+V/uAnpbtIIzB\n=ads4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T21:03:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKDNlOTFjMzE4MjU2Zjc4MzJkMTUyMDMwYjhmMmQ3NzNmZjdkZGUzNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63","sha":"e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63"}],"sha":"3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/3e91c318256f7832d152030b8f2d773ff7dde342"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:26:46Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:26:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: drop the built-in-superseded loaders and plugins from the indexes (#8344)\n\n* docs: drop the built-in-superseded loaders and plugins from the indexes\n\ncss-loader, style-loader, html-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and\nHtmlWebpackPlugin are no longer listed on /loaders/ and /plugins/, the\nsame treatment file-loader, url-loader and raw-loader got when asset\nmodules replaced them. Each page stays reachable and is linked from the\nnote that replaces its entry, so the options with no built-in equivalent\nare still documented.\n\n* docs: stop pointing readers at the superseded loaders and plugins\n\nThe guide series builds its CSS with the built-in support, so production''s\ndevDependencies listed css-loader and style-loader that nothing installs.\noutput.mdx sent readers to css-loader''s docs for localIdentName, which\nwebpack has as a generator option. The UseEntry and kebab-case examples\nand the awesome-webpack ecosystem list named them where any loader would\ndo.\n\n* build: use webpack''s built-in CSS instead of css-loader and MiniCssExtractPlugin\n\nThe site documents native CSS but did not use it. The rule keeps\npostcss-loader for Tailwind and hands the result to webpack via\ntype: css/auto; output.cssFilename reproduces the plugin''s names.\n\nVerified against the previous config: 382 emitted files and 188 pages\nboth ways, the vendor stylesheet byte-identical (97fc31c3662cb803), and\nindex.css differing by two bytes because webpack quotes the @import url.\nThe stray stylesheet the SSG pass emits drops from 48.6 KB to 177 B.\n\n* build: minify CSS with webpack instead of css-minimizer-webpack-plugin\n\nwebpack minifies CSS itself and deliberately steps aside when another\nminimizer claims those assets, so the plugin was displacing it. Dropping\nit is a gzip win on both stylesheets: vendor 5939 -> 5884 B and the main\nsheet 13181 -> 13130 B, 106 B less over the wire.\n\nThe ssg pass replaced the default minimizers rather than extending them,\nso its server bundle was never minified and the stylesheet it emits is\nunreferenced; it now says minimize: false instead.\n\nAll 188 pages stay byte-identical and the emitted file list is unchanged.\n\n* build: update webpack to 5.110.2","tree":{"sha":"fb5e115596b6cb2b2da9264969271455d8cb1ec0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/fb5e115596b6cb2b2da9264969271455d8cb1ec0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63","verification":{"payload":"tree fb5e115596b6cb2b2da9264969271455d8cb1ec0\nparent 24dc0b575d829f54f6caa37f465fc7af4b58de69\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1788107206 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788107206 +0300\n\ndocs: drop the built-in-superseded loaders and plugins from the indexes (#8344)\n\n* docs: drop the built-in-superseded loaders and plugins from the indexes\n\ncss-loader, style-loader, html-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and\nHtmlWebpackPlugin are no longer listed on /loaders/ and /plugins/, the\nsame treatment file-loader, url-loader and raw-loader got when asset\nmodules replaced them. Each page stays reachable and is linked from the\nnote that replaces its entry, so the options with no built-in equivalent\nare still documented.\n\n* docs: stop pointing readers at the superseded loaders and plugins\n\nThe guide series builds its CSS with the built-in support, so production''s\ndevDependencies listed css-loader and style-loader that nothing installs.\noutput.mdx sent readers to css-loader''s docs for localIdentName, which\nwebpack has as a generator option. The UseEntry and kebab-case examples\nand the awesome-webpack ecosystem list named them where any loader would\ndo.\n\n* build: use webpack''s built-in CSS instead of css-loader and MiniCssExtractPlugin\n\nThe site documents native CSS but did not use it. The rule keeps\npostcss-loader for Tailwind and hands the result to webpack via\ntype: css/auto; output.cssFilename reproduces the plugin''s names.\n\nVerified against the previous config: 382 emitted files and 188 pages\nboth ways, the vendor stylesheet byte-identical (97fc31c3662cb803), and\nindex.css differing by two bytes because webpack quotes the @import url.\nThe stray stylesheet the SSG pass emits drops from 48.6 KB to 177 B.\n\n* build: minify CSS with webpack instead of css-minimizer-webpack-plugin\n\nwebpack minifies CSS itself and deliberately steps aside when another\nminimizer claims those assets, so the plugin was displacing it. Dropping\nit is a gzip win on both stylesheets: vendor 5939 -> 5884 B and the main\nsheet 13181 -> 13130 B, 106 B less over the wire.\n\nThe ssg pass replaced the default minimizers rather than extending them,\nso its server bundle was never minified and the stylesheet it emits is\nunreferenced; it now says minimize: false instead.\n\nAll 188 pages stay byte-identical and the emitted file list is unchanged.\n\n* build: update webpack to 5.110.2","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlFnGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC8wQAFj+yxyeJrnLHchSGVews6K9\nQQYY9DKOfVIBmpDkIq6RqNKtHQzhAf4Vwp/eVwO8dnkzbwWkDTL2fUhFXoEQL1oS\nbeg52JE53HbuFhnlKVFbDGK2pBqSdYeBkb2MBfNU3u+uFczlV/WLVAFnxBeX3AAb\nO1bWUGmsxIaaXmzYABctIzYazYBsXi7Y2EvCSf3UwYLyC5LLlQ1zDZ7CCsrUGSQx\nVixMDV4P0n/6Tv5QeIRVOicF9Yec5sD1qbcnS05ehPyf9YdCNIXa7DxA7GE7L0Eq\n1QqrqdRtYttaihM0Lv0kmY/Nj+o38/6B9ButMVdrYIJh4SrRoQ+8NT7Ug2d7d/NV\n42H0uN3x0ZUJDdcjcTOSl9TL7sswaq3gIGpi7irVpqBAuYdff5xCt9hKu/8N9jhf\nBcSgKqGQtnIRquMkmaE7K5noqbQlO6uisFwANDa8wAi6Mz6QKGaqXGVFvYUR4h2E\nAiOiSyw7oDrT7+XN4upQA/F2ZXVEH/usGRAmqkcD8J6ikj6oZVaD6Y4Iuc+4oi14\n6I7Nd5bE9eMcufjlS3bRE3dTGNsdAbX9LAUPEy1E9y9CAKO3Y7Nv1S5QofCmfIEN\n6x2s4izLTj41nYmJfEgF/v/v/1xeAIo/lkvDYzJHgcNfihQ5geJZNYky1J9xeDeY\ncXZhzyXCxEBaqgTlJMs1\n=Z+dW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T16:26:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKGU2ZmIwYjViYjc0N2ZhZDQxMTg2YzljNWMyYjc3MTUyYTliNmVhNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/24dc0b575d829f54f6caa37f465fc7af4b58de69","sha":"24dc0b575d829f54f6caa37f465fc7af4b58de69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/24dc0b575d829f54f6caa37f465fc7af4b58de69"}],"sha":"e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/e6fb0b5bb747fad41186c9c5c2b77152a9b6ea63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103585995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjohansebas","id":103585995,"login":"bjohansebas","node_id":"U_kgDOBiyYyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/24dc0b575d829f54f6caa37f465fc7af4b58de69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:28:31Z","email":"bjohansebas@gmail.com","name":"Sebastian Beltran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:28:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(blog): add the webpack 5.110 release post (#8338)\n\n* docs(blog): add the webpack 5.110 release post\n\nCovers the performance hint suite, built-in CSS and HTML minification,\nthe native CSS story, the nodeModules externals preset, the glob rule\ncondition and the rest of the release.\n\nThe benchmark table comparing the native pipeline with the loader one is\na placeholder pending real measurements, and the banner image still has\nto be added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): point the CSS migration at the new codemod\n\nwebpack/codemods ships @webpack/css-plugins-to-native-css, which does\nthe mini-css-extract-plugin and style-loader/css-loader migration the\npost describes by hand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): drop the empty benchmark table\n\nThe Benchmarks section keeps its placeholder note until the real\nmeasurements are in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): replace the benchmark section with the performance claim\n\nDrops the empty Benchmarks section and its table of contents entry, and\nsays instead where the win comes from: the built-in support parses each\nstylesheet once as CSS instead of once per loader plus once as a\nJavaScript module, so a build whose work is mostly CSS gains the most.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): mention the devtool default change for library builds\n\nA module or modern-module library, and any library under\nfutureDefaults, no longer gets the default eval source map in\ndevelopment, since the eval wrapper hides import.meta from the bundler\nreading the library.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): add the release banner and move the post to today\n\nBuilds the banner in the style of the 5.108 and 5.109 ones: the webpack\nlockup from src/assets/logo-on-dark-bg.svg, Geomanist for the type, and\nthe same palette, sizes and layout measured off webpack-5-109.png.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): fix the codemod command\n\nThe Codemod CLI takes the package directly; ''run'' is not part of it.\nMatches the command the Native CSS guide already documents, which the\npost now links to for the full option mapping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c93082e0e473378b2d8af818d859d0231c8b0cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/7c93082e0e473378b2d8af818d859d0231c8b0cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/24dc0b575d829f54f6caa37f465fc7af4b58de69","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c93082e0e473378b2d8af818d859d0231c8b0cf\nparent 68024c8f0f33629b971d9f80137359cff4337366\nauthor Sebastian Beltran <bjohansebas@gmail.com> 1788042511 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788042511 -0500\n\ndocs(blog): add the webpack 5.110 release post (#8338)\n\n* docs(blog): add the webpack 5.110 release post\n\nCovers the performance hint suite, built-in CSS and HTML minification,\nthe native CSS story, the nodeModules externals preset, the glob rule\ncondition and the rest of the release.\n\nThe benchmark table comparing the native pipeline with the loader one is\na placeholder pending real measurements, and the banner image still has\nto be added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): point the CSS migration at the new codemod\n\nwebpack/codemods ships @webpack/css-plugins-to-native-css, which does\nthe mini-css-extract-plugin and style-loader/css-loader migration the\npost describes by hand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): drop the empty benchmark table\n\nThe Benchmarks section keeps its placeholder note until the real\nmeasurements are in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): replace the benchmark section with the performance claim\n\nDrops the empty Benchmarks section and its table of contents entry, and\nsays instead where the win comes from: the built-in support parses each\nstylesheet once as CSS instead of once per loader plus once as a\nJavaScript module, so a build whose work is mostly CSS gains the most.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): mention the devtool default change for library builds\n\nA module or modern-module library, and any library under\nfutureDefaults, no longer gets the default eval source map in\ndevelopment, since the eval wrapper hides import.meta from the bundler\nreading the library.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): add the release banner and move the post to today\n\nBuilds the banner in the style of the 5.108 and 5.109 ones: the webpack\nlockup from src/assets/logo-on-dark-bg.svg, Geomanist for the type, and\nthe same palette, sizes and layout measured off webpack-5-109.png.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): fix the codemod command\n\nThe Codemod CLI takes the package directly; ''run'' is not part of it.\nMatches the command the Native CSS guide already documents, which the\npost now links to for the full option mapping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqk10PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4YoQAFWlcVWuTq6TNMAL128unDgD\nzLZIOcFIVzGB/JuKtLvKuvCt3oXUzggwd/GOTK8SOJ1SYwnwd7fI88hQhI4t64SP\nXS34zEj9s2SofuTrckFsydZUUklu6EJXSJZlqTtyqMyt6f+QUvCX5SxjP2h4n7F7\nO83LYudz/5m76KFfPg3t9XZgtdaEkUY8VrcsM4FmB/ZdwG/UyYinAyxwMOtBxrw+\nkH3hzRxdydI2zrpMkQbA9y4gk0CwscmAuvUddsUISR1u32uXKLURzFFvAB5l446J\npeGqfR0HBwPBE6OnxQc4LxOOkcCehZsZo9dDgQrp/uTYCES/VC8w4NVGssFw+cgl\nFz7gaDo3Lfva48JMkk/4UN6r8TMIqWETrKzgcuTSG6JthQYjPAwqvnhzwI0jSVN8\nhbFk6W7gkSPyG9A9g7qZaoiG/Oj815tVEdYqsLyp4D25wYaYIH/MPQ9eWo1g52Ig\nZaeM461sSUsUfW7LMdZySFg8//aM61YkuA/HED9nUYT6NEcxf89oqztQbMeF1DHN\nCHFaHmGAnymfux1bFDqao6SgP1MGOxIW+9RjvVi9oOvtnfJEyOP1M+krLHMJksiN\n05eP1TATMa9lSZtUGPLFOYWo+zUkYd0QJhSPBhMIoznv/zkcpuGmGYCPmwpb5KfU\nb+WXN5lDmWAU7/dYIPsj\n=GFRJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T22:28:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"star