"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/c2237b95e4ecebb8ee2348dadde5fbd1cc603520"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103585995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bjohansebas","id":103585995,"login":"bjohansebas","node_id":"U_kgDOBiyYyw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjohansebas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/1a83fe2cb97e29f9b45bb04d27e5c3dc2849a80f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T04:06:24Z","email":"bjohansebas@gmail.com","name":"Sebastian Beltran"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T04:06:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: document the webpack 5.110.0 configuration and API surface (#8337)\n\n* docs(performance): document the 5.110 performance checks\n\nAdds performance.all, hints: \"stats\" and the opt-in checks introduced in\nwebpack 5.110.0, plus an overview table grouping them by what they\ninspect and a note on which ones are not gated on hints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(module): document Rule.glob and Rule.descriptionRelativePath\n\nBoth conditions land in webpack 5.110.0: glob matches the resource\nOS-independently and is also accepted inside a Condition object, and\ndescriptionRelativePath matches a module by its path inside its own\npackage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(externals): document nodeModules preset and external sideEffects\n\nCovers externalsPresets.nodeModules and its allowlist, which replace the\nwebpack-node-externals plugin, plus the { external, sideEffects } value\nform, both added in webpack 5.110.0. Also fills in the bun and deno\npreset rows, which the table was missing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(output): document contained path placeholders, umdAmdContainer, resourceHints.dedupe and per-entry html\n\nAdds the [containedfile]/[containedpath] template placeholders,\noutput.library.umdAmdContainer and output.resourceHints.dedupe from\nwebpack 5.110.0, plus the entry descriptor''s html option, which now\naccepts an object overriding output.html per entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(optimization): document minimize per asset type\n\nwebpack 5.110.0 makes optimization.minimize accept an object that\nconfigures the built-in minimizer per asset type, and the default\nminimizer now handles CSS and HTML too. Documents the javascript, css\nand html option sets and when each minifier runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(stats): document stats.hints and stats.hintsCount\n\nAlso adds the deferImport and sourceImport environment flags to the\noutput.environment listing, both added in webpack 5.110.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(api): document __webpack_css_server_styles__ and MultiCompiler hooks\n\nThe module variable reads back the CSS collected while rendering without\na DOM, and MultiCompiler gained an aggregated shutdown hook plus a done\nhook that reports which compilers actually rebuilt. Both in 5.110.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: document renderEmbeddedSource and HTML head hot patching\n\nAdds the renderEmbeddedSource and embeddedSourceHash compilation hooks,\nand updates the HTML HMR note: 5.110.0 patches the head in place instead\nof falling back to a full page reload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(performance): fix dataUrlCondition link target\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(optimization): keep main''s inline comment formatting\n\nThe local prettier (3.8.3) reformatted two of main''s inline block\ncomments onto their own lines; the declared version (3.9.6), which CI\ninstalls, wants them inline, which is how they are committed on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b677e178da4b55f3b63191ddcf9a5a015d5c4ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/2b677e178da4b55f3b63191ddcf9a5a015d5c4ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/1a83fe2cb97e29f9b45bb04d27e5c3dc2849a80f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b677e178da4b55f3b63191ddcf9a5a015d5c4ea\nparent d688d3616c0f9ae05fd5e6e2b33dbf81d8d2899a\nauthor Sebastian Beltran <bjohansebas@gmail.com> 1787889984 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787889984 -0500\n\ndocs: document the webpack 5.110.0 configuration and API surface (#8337)\n\n* docs(performance): document the 5.110 performance checks\n\nAdds performance.all, hints: \"stats\" and the opt-in checks introduced in\nwebpack 5.110.0, plus an overview table grouping them by what they\ninspect and a note on which ones are not gated on hints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(module): document Rule.glob and Rule.descriptionRelativePath\n\nBoth conditions land in webpack 5.110.0: glob matches the resource\nOS-independently and is also accepted inside a Condition object, and\ndescriptionRelativePath matches a module by its path inside its own\npackage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(externals): document nodeModules preset and external sideEffects\n\nCovers externalsPresets.nodeModules and its allowlist, which replace the\nwebpack-node-externals plugin, plus the { external, sideEffects } value\nform, both added in webpack 5.110.0. Also fills in the bun and deno\npreset rows, which the table was missing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(output): document contained path placeholders, umdAmdContainer, resourceHints.dedupe and per-entry html\n\nAdds the [containedfile]/[containedpath] template placeholders,\noutput.library.umdAmdContainer and output.resourceHints.dedupe from\nwebpack 5.110.0, plus the entry descriptor''s html option, which now\naccepts an object overriding output.html per entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(optimization): document minimize per asset type\n\nwebpack 5.110.0 makes optimization.minimize accept an object that\nconfigures the built-in minimizer per asset type, and the default\nminimizer now handles CSS and HTML too. Documents the javascript, css\nand html option sets and when each minifier runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(stats): document stats.hints and stats.hintsCount\n\nAlso adds the deferImport and sourceImport environment flags to the\noutput.environment listing, both added in webpack 5.110.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(api): document __webpack_css_server_styles__ and MultiCompiler hooks\n\nThe module variable reads back the CSS collected while rendering without\na DOM, and MultiCompiler gained an aggregated shutdown hook plus a done\nhook that reports which compilers actually rebuilt. Both in 5.110.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: document renderEmbeddedSource and HTML head hot patching\n\nAdds the renderEmbeddedSource and embeddedSourceHash compilation hooks,\nand updates the HTML HMR note: 5.110.0 patches the head in place instead\nof falling back to a full page reload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(performance): fix dataUrlCondition link target\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(optimization): keep main''s inline comment formatting\n\nThe local prettier (3.8.3) reformatted two of main''s inline block\ncomments onto their own lines; the declared version (3.9.6), which CI\ninstalls, wants them inline, which is how they are committed on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkQlACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI3AQAKzwjOL1sfXbU3n1+A1vy+lo\n9cs/0HrllDAxaNVSJtoP2hkvGZs6IwXsJVjx/rxlkwNVcye4S2hS0iQ5GQbTPetf\nGaLwuzTbT5kPMSRk+HsoIPsJpocFxADuPjmARwn9SKzI3Ylc9W9szBs2YUCKzEEz\nbdBMuLL1sZrKhQfoU5U2TOO/YqlCxKItPW9j5hL2LF0a4RQOFncwYRxTi4TUcON8\namIExcAdWBe3xKMx9XPLbEi9+3O40cMIRMlyPmQCCx1eA+kIQd1s5stHzNBf0V91\nQo/jFjGhiaUsZoAbtHc7M3WNP72Omvpt2rDZSKhodZitoIvVGIoPM1AQobsPUZ7l\nd5Y08PGllVi4bXriSmmcrulbQvP7gKovrnuHW3irYGzOgvFRSdQhlacDZ1vmR2h7\nuLHeSRJT7rBJ+nXA+Dj0BMNrK/ZOvDzqebmGiUpm9yis5GS4W+9hjkDZyAkHP8A3\n7ao43QNv3z68gb+fXOsHvyRvNu7qmMjeTZKeWaO4F2ct4S5kT2u0C2wa2ZUpdEbP\nJ1KKA5uw8OZIaG1G8258t5oWDW0IL3iUqCy/aKd6ewQ45IwB5ysRCppRdeVGK7Tt\nx4jMZ1mj2Uaiu2n2UgMoed3LjxpCTp9D7Jm5KcLD9ThQEW4TUpE+yuQR8wMWRIj6\ncGmMa5TbDQci8ZJOV1CV\n=JlrC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T04:06:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/1a83fe2cb97e29f9b45bb04d27e5c3dc2849a80f","node_id":"C_kwDOA7BOndoAKDFhODNmZTJjYjk3ZTI5ZjliNDViYjA0ZDI3ZTVjM2RjMjg0OWE4MGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.js.org/commit/d688d3616c0f9ae05fd5e6e2b33dbf81d8d2899a","sha":"d688d3616c0f9ae05fd5e6e2b33dbf81d8d2899a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/d688d3616c0f9ae05fd5e6e2b33dbf81d8d2899a"}],"sha":"1a83fe2cb97e29f9b45bb04d27e5c3dc2849a80f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/1a83fe2cb97e29f9b45bb04d27e5c3dc2849a80f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4567934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alexander-akait","id":4567934,"login":"alexander-akait","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1Njc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/d688d3616c0f9ae05fd5e6e2b33dbf81d8d2899a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T17:28:27Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T17:28:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): update dependencies (#8340)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies within their semver ranges\n\nIncludes webpack 5.107 -> 5.110, prettier 3.8 -> 3.9, cypress 15.12 ->\n15.21, react-router-dom 7.13 -> 7.18 and the rest of the in-range\nupdates. Prettier 3.9 prints a block whose only content is a comment on\none line, which reformats four documentation code samples.\n\n* chore(deps): update feed, webpack-dev-server and @docsearch/react to v6, v6 and v5\n\nDocSearch v5 replaces the `indexName` prop with an `indices` array, so\nNavigation passes the configured index as a single-element array. The\noverridden button class names and the primary-color variable are\nunchanged in v5, and the entry bundle drops from 1.06 MiB to 901 KiB.\n\n* chore(deps): update Babel to v8\n\nBabel 8 drops @babel/plugin-proposal-class-properties, whose transform\npreset-env now applies on its own, so the plugin goes with it.\n\n* chore(deps): match the react-router range to react-router-dom\n\nreact-router-dom 7.18.2 depends on exactly react-router 7.18.2, so the\ndeclared range now says so.\n\n* chore(deps): raise the Node requirement to match the updated toolchain\n\nBabel 8 requires Node ^22.18.0 || >=24.11.0 and webpack-dev-server 6\nrequires >=22.15.0, so the declared range no longer described what the\ndependencies install on.\n\n* chore(deps): hold @docsearch/react at v4\n\nv5 ships an Ask AI feature whose dependency chain (ai, @ai-sdk/*) brings\nin undici, which carries a high-severity advisory, so dependency-review\nrejects it. Holding the upgrade drops the chain, takes the audit from 26\nvulnerabilities on main to 12, and leaves the production build without\nthe warning @ai-sdk/provider-utils was emitting.","tree":{"sha":"8fe503a7001f67dc6d86e8581d8784e307c2ce0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/8fe503a7001f67dc6d86e8581d8784e307c2ce0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/d688d3616c0f9ae05fd5e6e2b33dbf81d8d2899a","verification":{"payload":"tree 8fe503a7001f67dc6d86e8581d8784e307c2ce0f\nparent e3fd8f536cc3fb20856f9ace63bd7507501aa0ba\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1787851707 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787851707 +0300\n\nchore(deps): update dependencies (#8340)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies within their semver ranges\n\nIncludes webpack 5.107 -> 5.110, prettier 3.8 -> 3.9, cypress 15.12 ->\n15.21, react-router-dom 7.13 -> 7.18 and the rest of the in-range\nupdates. Prettier 3.9 prints a block whose only content is a comment on\none line, which reformats four documentation code samples.\n\n* chore(deps): update feed, webpack-dev-server and @docsearch/react to v6, v6 and v5\n\nDocSearch v5 replaces the `indexName` prop with an `indices` array, so\nNavigation passes the configured index as a single-element array. The\noverridden button class names and the primary-color variable are\nunchanged in v5, and the entry bundle drops from 1.06 MiB to 901 KiB.\n\n* chore(deps): update Babel to v8\n\nBabel 8 drops @babel/plugin-proposal-class-properties, whose transform\npreset-env now applies on its own, so the plugin goes with it.\n\n* chore(deps): match the react-router range to react-router-dom\n\nreact-router-dom 7.18.2 depends on exactly react-router 7.18.2, so the\ndeclared range now says so.\n\n* chore(deps): raise the Node requirement to match the updated toolchain\n\nBabel 8 requires Node ^22.18.0 || >=24.11.0 and webpack-dev-server 6\nrequires >=22.15.0, so the declared range no longer described what the\ndependencies install on.\n\n* chore(deps): hold @docsearch/react at v4\n\nv5 ships an Ask AI feature whose dependency chain (ai, @ai-sdk/*) brings\nin undici, which carries a high-severity advisory, so dependency-review\nrejects it. Holding the upgrade drops the chain, takes the audit from 26\nvulnerabilities on main to 12, and leaves the production build without\nthe warning @ai-sdk/provider-utils was emitting.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkHO7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJX4QAHvse7rR6jUNnISAPc352QaJ\nvsM2JuxztdO7KoKK12jPTTmWLQog9v0TJvm/0+Oy18nHorqakl0XgISrd1M4KBpz\n9RDRhAjMCMej3OP5kfOiKqK7sNZbS7PA7n81sQzp2KRRhFyubbH1C49ZP/WThfkB\nh71qvuXVfJ05vdu+ChV6I8nGYqa0p0aXevMCLVs+resDmLgIhOFA2j7bkShNWuJ5\nM8Fn5XgyNB40Vtsyz8hVq7G8r5yToWPcUpPBqmzfDAilR6pRGucLU2Ni+6YF0Dd3\ncSotBzA/VpBZT0b4EMS86tZuQePIbqfb+EoR39ymfZir5eHMDrmD87GF0xTYz5e6\njQV2o2B9N9li5quFtGY37qMGbKnO0nb8iTeVsLIVYvCn1j2yET0IB68Wtq1TzRlZ\n2Q86e4oapJtrfz1grp6ECt53zH+zo4qNkkUOGjwdPSCk74WuqsKh+FnxsIRh8yOv\nkDO4KIqTNCUnK89aJ6j3aUzmR3vjlflEb+B7OFUlqNk/u4hZ69qL3MD9LV/b5/Wv\n/6YXRosTA3YCAAYL66EtRTVIdkJ/1pv108KX48OvycWM1WGnAc2oZ3pZCx6ZFdMx\nRPJn0+yba0Fxh9GL38JH7NQi7lapmU/sJXwJJSALLdsSplHwmlyRzT39hSPUY55o\nRvgAPDDXkC57uzYX5gyl\n=QU61\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T17:28:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/