.github.com/users/alexander-akait/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexander-akait","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/commits/e3fd8f536cc3fb20856f9ace63bd7507501aa0ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:27:22Z","email":"4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Akait"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:27:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: native HTML guide and expanded native CSS coverage (#8339)\n\n* docs: native HTML guide and expanded native CSS coverage\n\nAdd a Native HTML guide covering the built-in HTML support: HTML entry\npoints, generated pages, HTML imported from JS, the parser''s source list,\ntemplating, minification, resource hints, HMR and plugin hooks, plus\nmigration paths off html-loader and html-webpack-plugin.\n\nExpand the Native CSS guide with @custom-media / @custom-selector, the\nbuilt-in CSS minimizer (including browserslist vendor prefixing), font\npreloading and url hints, CSS referenced from HTML, and more examples.\n\nDocument optimization.minimize''s per-asset-type object form and the entry\ndescriptor html option, which both guides reference.\n\n* docs: complete HTML parser, generator and output option reference\n\nAdd an \"All options with examples\" section to the Native HTML guide\ncovering every option: the html parser (sources with all source types,\nas, urlHints, template), the generator (extract), output.html and the\nhtml filename templates, output.resourceHints with its hint and url-rule\ndescriptors, every optimization.minimize.html transform, and the HTML\nmagic comments.\n\n* docs: use built-in CSS in examples, deprecate the superseded loaders/plugins\n\nMark style-loader, css-loader, html-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and\nHtmlWebpackPlugin as deprecated on the loaders and plugins index pages,\neach pointing at the native support guide.\n\nReplace the CSS-loader examples with the built-in support: asset\nmanagement (no install, no rule, extracted stylesheet — transcripts\nregenerated from real builds), advanced entry, concepts/loaders,\nextending configurations, module.use, code splitting, tree shaking,\nauthor libraries, production, HMR concepts and the glossary.","tree":{"sha":"dd9c8dd90ad1e9ad2f214db4443b5a21a98b8108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/trees/dd9c8dd90ad1e9ad2f214db4443b5a21a98b8108"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack.js.org/git/commits/e3fd8f536cc3fb20856f9ace63bd7507501aa0ba","verification":{"payload":"tree dd9c8dd90ad1e9ad2f214db4443b5a21a98b8108\nparent e919bc0bddf170b1cb2a79252fe252965c5c7461\nauthor Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com> 1787840842 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787840842 +0300\n\ndocs: native HTML guide and expanded native CSS coverage (#8339)\n\n* docs: native HTML guide and expanded native CSS coverage\n\nAdd a Native HTML guide covering the built-in HTML support: HTML entry\npoints, generated pages, HTML imported from JS, the parser''s source list,\ntemplating, minification, resource hints, HMR and plugin hooks, plus\nmigration paths off html-loader and html-webpack-plugin.\n\nExpand the Native CSS guide with @custom-media / @custom-selector, the\nbuilt-in CSS minimizer (including browserslist vendor prefixing), font\npreloading and url hints, CSS referenced from HTML, and more examples.\n\nDocument optimization.minimize''s per-asset-type object form and the entry\ndescriptor html option, which both guides reference.\n\n* docs: complete HTML parser, generator and output option reference\n\nAdd an \"All options with examples\" section to the Native HTML guide\ncovering every option: the html parser (sources with all source types,\nas, urlHints, template), the generator (extract), output.html and the\nhtml filename templates, output.resourceHints with its hint and url-rule\ndescriptors, every optimization.minimize.html transform, and the HTML\nmagic comments.\n\n* docs: use built-in CSS in examples, deprecate the superseded loaders/plugins\n\nMark style-loader, css-loader, html-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and\nHtmlWebpackPlugin as deprecated on the loaders and plugins index pages,\neach pointing at the native support guide.\n\nReplace the CSS-loader examples with the built-in support: asset\nmanagement (no install, no rule, extracted stylesheet — transcripts\nregenerated from real builds), advanced entry, concepts/loaders,\nextending configurations, module.use, code splitting, tree shaking,\nauthor libraries, production, HMR concepts and the glossary.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkElKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJyEQAAJnMiwd+kqoWQ1hRWdv2hn6\nd38gADPdUyhl/dI7uf9H916H4Y8cEaV+w8kLROUzvhVIwebl0V1f1KRhKMuFmQLm\n8kAVibHt7DK+OztZnWz05bMgNTPLcz8uZKnH29cMGGiczyZfqSaOBu7xJfgx7Nt5\ncitEQGtwzW6QRKWFy1IBhdGMRls3DbEUlEaPRvUXzRI4fsrSfP+7X5Ks5ZMz1WC5\nfvFe6uT4l05gyepPIyIFm1gJZfeyPHu0X21RNhMDyaBMg8AVKgIlwgV8m9YnKYRy\nUoq7Rqz4Hm3PY5itexKBzMSWLCkQvulcqMAgFZJfty89zz7djCvjpfxrJh4LnO2U\nk0I9o7Xicgwg7+JgEOz+pqZm0UscNt4Vd8ouH+cDQotkCA4Ki2Es3AvIs+U/rYmB\nth7KQJ/ZgOqLpUlXMH2tWYadtpE8+OlFkjVd8Yw5Z/7BRQQTSKdenkZrqrPoNm4z\nqCEtPTALaJK5qv4Y0jqMpc7KLn/efXok2A1F4n+siK/450xh9PF6eBMZvWXxL3Jd\nctvOjpIok04ro5goMuAOWloLmyA68Xbvc6ACm/IJtH/StzFv0B5xzogz5ubenYAa\nXHCJfV43jNaftVRIlaJKBTvHt3V8vXNGky/QgaewsqLih4SDOVjrtPbMYGq7VUnp\n+jiqY66K9HtUY+1JT15Z\n=Xi3D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T14:27:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privac