ations as fallback (#1762)\n\nAlways load en-US translations, allowing them to serve as a fallback\nwhen those entries are missing from another locale.\n\nRefs STCOR-1024","tree":{"sha":"0cd7d133a8c8563b6076c695507094aca071afd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/0cd7d133a8c8563b6076c695507094aca071afd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/124fedb3a489f9d9236d4828b1129a09cbbf97d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 0cd7d133a8c8563b6076c695507094aca071afd6\nparent 02f7843458a473f1c0db1fba2f17cbebfccb41a7\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1790607522 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790607522 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1024 load en-US translations as fallback (#1762)\n\nAlways load en-US translations, allowing them to serve as a fallback\nwhen those entries are missing from another locale.\n\nRefs STCOR-1024","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquoCiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAufkQAENvwDMN1HQ3tJ40MgYjiasb\nE6Z7MZP/udl5nu5FK5XzOeAbjviEiLYArbzFSjBLf8BkFlgRTN+Er6aUkCdpEg6/\nRZGlmmrjXQosJ6kHKrTDGN6ZHsQeiOxIDj404C9Hye7ux8U0PRcWc7fDYrqlx8R9\nFr6fn0vJAjRo6cT7BMiuYnykntU2uHbSnlOGGu+FrgJMy8R9pzI8iZp7fKYI44FT\nPTHa+BDEs1AiKVhTHzws9GMFHoMZNNmdu3SLds3ZMXgvqJDiUcevOS4uvaDmAaxr\nOA5QyUqnZIetnJmEMBi/csqf8FnpO/DVIzNuhnLM6RwbLMDQZzhkRTSblTbUZsLE\n1El+6LckB1es7/kS+M9gdAxPFymbzvC2eoO7Xq12vSJYS1Bus4fy9D57ZChloWBp\nTLpfwyVqMZLxQm3SJAV7drvrjzasa9miYHsnoLn1NXOdohfCOAAe/2bxnQ1nOK8T\nUFVZuD5Ldd42EVzO/fFBiAmfmFyMyt7BHxYp0b6Lzc8tr+hK8Xfk/Nu6nekD2Wrq\npr1DjG7/pe2Pydi/4enqhmbcKyPZFnzMzh4R5lSF/brmNaZbhVDe82zIpH2N9rSB\nABcy4NDDh9lUJLMxpnvpu9hWpmil+2pjM+uOmyvoOXWizb6XRxmihcz22S0A9knf\nu3QuUKAFmvYzguR6yvGj\n=Q2j1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T14:58:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/124fedb3a489f9d9236d4828b1129a09cbbf97d0","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDEyNGZlZGIzYTQ4OWY5ZDkyMzZkNDgyOGIxMTI5YTA5Y2JiZjk3ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/02f7843458a473f1c0db1fba2f17cbebfccb41a7","sha":"02f7843458a473f1c0db1fba2f17cbebfccb41a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/02f7843458a473f1c0db1fba2f17cbebfccb41a7"}],"sha":"124fedb3a489f9d9236d4828b1129a09cbbf97d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/124fedb3a489f9d9236d4828b1129a09cbbf97d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/02f7843458a473f1c0db1fba2f17cbebfccb41a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:29:00Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:29:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1102 default to en-US given an invalid locale (#1760)\n\nGiven an invalid locale, recover and default to `en-US`. Previously, an\ninvalid locale string such as `en-US-u-nu-latn-u-nu-latn` would cause\nstripes to halt midway through initialization, showing a flash of\navailable applications followed by a blank screen when IntlProvider\ninit failed.\n\nThe built-in Intl APIs have come a long way since i18n as first\nintroduced to stripes in 7d8f0fc74 in 2017. This makes processing locale\ndata both simpler and more robust, allowing us to use the `Intl.Locale`\nconstructor to validate the input, and to use its return value to\nprovide the `language` and `region` values we previously parsed out\nmanually.\n\nBad locale values may come from improperly stored data, e.g. if a locale\nis stored with a duplicate numbering-system attribute like\n```\n{ locale: \"en-US-u-nu-latn\", numberingSystem: \"latn\" }\n```\nthen numbering-system will be applied twice.\n\nRefs STCOR-1102, STCOR-1101","tree":{"sha":"ec4d40f2cdbdc9ad302b36ae28af88200a0ae515","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/ec4d40f2cdbdc9ad302b36ae28af88200a0ae515"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/02f7843458a473f1c0db1fba2f17cbebfccb41a7","verification":{"payload":"tree ec4d40f2cdbdc9ad302b36ae28af88200a0ae515\nparent e888fa16b87a5a19bc019976d65d613873b431f7\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1790101740 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790101740 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1102 default to en-US given an invalid locale (#1760)\n\nGiven an invalid locale, recover and default to `en-US`. Previously, an\ninvalid locale string such as `en-US-u-nu-latn-u-nu-latn` would cause\nstripes to halt midway through initialization, showing a flash of\navailable applications followed by a blank screen when IntlProvider\ninit failed.\n\nThe built-in Intl APIs have come a long way since i18n as first\nintroduced to stripes in 7d8f0fc74 in 2017. This makes processing locale\ndata both simpler and more robust, allowing us to use the `Intl.Locale`\nconstructor to validate the input, and to use its return value to\nprovide the `language` and `region` values we previously parsed out\nmanually.\n\nBad locale values may come from improperly stored data, e.g. if a locale\nis stored with a duplicate numbering-system attribute like\n```\n{ locale: \"en-US-u-nu-latn\", numberingSystem: \"latn\" }\n```\nthen numbering-system will be applied twice.\n\nRefs STCOR-1102, STCOR-1101","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqssjsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAevoQAI9SIgtX7h7By3mwKgF90lyo\nYEFnJbpRVF/XesZKlTONIXhmlWcHpZb8ClGuJQUYLxk0KPDASLyVfHxnekMe2owx\nkgplPYZxyJ0OuC8pdCscYTcd7J2NOawF9ynGvioxholOqwRh4VpLyf8pUlwBIa1n\nNpAJUhhY+hYcFFdIrav6v/45FXsUFe3wIcFz6iGRLdtefqw62w3gvN1ROjcMFFRZ\nZ1nq+yUwkbRMwF72s8nVUMPPDFz60xJa2VCljdwm9nQUkk7bacuaOIBXAam7DusK\nKK3B1DVEY75mN8etk+FasaYSEOS30BF5jibR4BNDlslHBurrAHoOkCw5/6BNQCnL\nN1OqUlpPFpvEDQMFudGgiK6yblaGaOK/fZH0h4qKR7VDNw0fRaWBGrhqZdIYIEnr\nS9SO5mUNY+qkgGeApFIv3Kg4PzMm9lmL74c7+ehhr/IMUmgODndmRlPzatKHz0pq\neSxlXt8jvcvS7AAeVctdZbDggMkWV5SWtFpuuIVhwgtc2j/z6ru4Ou8lH5zEoVr+\n/w8mLaGDTyqr2HCjguiPWTN4N5b1ht3AwLxy2g/yC0xij/idN9Zm/bwyLa1WqV1A\nVFj6KVjgW9twrJsZi8ZT5GAootMvY0Yx6mfc/jjcTmPbdfqAHTazqmsv/gKR9f1e\nvO5xMsPdL0TPm91gXbYR\n=5Evc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,