nassertion as an unnecessary wrapper around `screen.getBy...()` calls.\n\nRefs STCOR-993","tree":{"sha":"416b32184bf8714d8f092b4bb56d46daded809cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/416b32184bf8714d8f092b4bb56d46daded809cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/53e05dffd9c9a09a6da0a64538434dcd4a3b0512","verification":{"payload":"tree 416b32184bf8714d8f092b4bb56d46daded809cc\nparent 75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1788469624 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788469624 -0400\n\nSTCOR-993 codesmell cleanup for ForgotUserName, ForgotPassword (#1755)\n\nGiven we can call `history.push()` in the event handler, there is zero\nvalue in copying values into state and then rendering a `<Redirect>`\nafter the state change.\n\nMinor cleanup of existing tests where `expect()` was called without an\nassertion as an unnecessary wrapper around `screen.getBy...()` calls.\n\nRefs STCOR-993","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmeF4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEskQAGvK2EVGLsHw3k6yWhlkeeRG\na4YqFpmks+iKErS6J9QX2Xb8xlhgRpIVUOMYeI6Lrb23LTSLoHNckfYQ/XSkTCPu\n7xFnUsB4zQA3JSXqKiRCmwnZvmeUqstomLSAZhuih0Iqiova8ZM9krC5taigltlk\nnbkDtUChirKeBtO5uklV5T4j2kH4rGckAnZiQSwXHh75FdL1Qiae9ahBc/tiLa0V\nCEbPEL+zx47ICWs3+a9GRKvszZkLSa6Ury/6oGEOohWOhpDveW6lO+1LLJpTfygd\nGx92o/mvJzTclqTnmKgqeg3Kihc8YaYXvENcHI3RcthGfphuXKZ/cg7mqKAMBMDh\nEgc10BOmsvIs763LC65XXhT1ndTqF7eGCyQfCfLi4HH7EuWlKgvEzc6x72GPj+MV\nvT3jQODf4eMVBsT62d5mGWubFFki52+E5mCOy/ZP2C4U8wXBgGAeExwuG6lbmbsR\nIfeaqS/etme0mToAgC+zQGaRD1obJCqQvhHQQev4bXfwrIzKINRvmnV8Jh3s79ch\nOAMxUDcyLg1FRPmeGZ7GPfEd+hUpyUXD28WdPXy6wW1wPYIJOHHTpF/4eGDE/x7J\nkZpSkWRUSO1M4w/BTZDuDhDOHGhkW2p4PmojZ5G4uoeKOlxGD8z7vJNS+yj+nPup\nvJImGO7NWtb4GcimJMi/\n=HbhF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T21:07:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/53e05dffd9c9a09a6da0a64538434dcd4a3b0512","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDUzZTA1ZGZmZDljOWEwOWE2ZGEwYTY0NTM4NDM0ZGNkNGEzYjA1MTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022","sha":"75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022"}],"sha":"53e05dffd9c9a09a6da0a64538434dcd4a3b0512","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/53e05dffd9c9a09a6da0a64538434dcd4a3b0512"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:46:17Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:46:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1099 supply rtrIgnore to forgot-* API requests (#1756)\n\nSupply `rtrIgnore: true` on the forgot-password and forgot-username API\nrequests, allowing them to avoid invoking RTR when credentials are not\npresent, which of course they **won''t be because the whole reason for\naccessing these routes is that an end-user cannot remember their\ncredentials.\n\nThis bug has been lurking for a while but was masked by the initial RTR\nimplementation that amounted to \"play a request; on failure, if\ncredentials are required-but-missing, rotate; replay the request\". The\nloophole is that all requests would be played once prior to invoking\nRTR. This meant requests that require credentials (as most do) would\nfail, polluting the console, but it also meant the requests that do NOT\nrequire credentials (and these two do NOT) would succeed, even though\nthey do not specify `rtrIgnore: true` to indicate that they should\nbypass rotation.\n\nThe loophole was closed in STCOR-1069 in PRs #1732 and #1737 and was\nrevealed by testing for STCOR-993 in PR #1755.\n\nNew unit tests courtesy Codex GPT 5.6 Luna\n\nRefs STCOR-1099","tree":{"sha":"9bc288f28c936f3c253c71eeaae199f4e170b03c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/9bc288f28c936f3c253c71eeaae199f4e170b03c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bc288f28c936f3c253c71eeaae199f4e170b03c\nparent 53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1787233577 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787233577 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1099 supply rtrIgnore to forgot-* API requests (#1756)\n\nSupply `rtrIgnore: true` on the forgot-password and forgot-username API\nrequests, allowing them to avoid invoking RTR when credentials are not\npresent, which of course they **won''t be because the whole reason for\naccessing these routes is that an end-user cannot remember their\ncredentials.\n\nThis bug has been lurking for a while but was masked by the initial RTR\nimplementation that amounted to \"play a request; on failure, if\ncredentials are required-but-missing, rotate; replay the request\". The\nloophole is that all requests would be played once prior to invoking\nRTR. This meant requests that require credentials (as most do) would\nfail, polluting the console, but it also meant the requests that do NOT\nrequire credentials (and these two do NOT) would succeed, even though\nthey do not specify `rtrIgnore: true` to indicate that they should\nbypass rotation.\n\nThe loophole was closed in STCOR-1069 in PRs #1732 and #1737 and was\nrevealed by testing for STCOR-993 in PR #1755.\n\nNew unit tests courtesy Codex GPT 5.6 Luna\n\nRefs STCOR-1099","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhwUpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXFkQAAQnGnjWIbf5qwSav78sLjdm\n9cn9vRgpTRx7jyDGfVplraq90sPvNppZGE4ACQyfcy//K7y811uvf3eOt3cg+YK/\nrZxc88ZwkvH+aazJEiIHPd9yHwGjryVV46qQs7IvySMp8TGtUaurAddsRDny3k1/\nOcou3pKz7fzBMPCQW8zgfOoJzGEXI0eOhXj7u829lARGm/6agMrF5QcrOsvOmnuD\ns9qERscG64+XYgzAZ9gsHc83JXPgA3Wbe80FHJcD78TtbMZMCt4yMRY4zpTEEXsC\nHDxKtLiFmWkdVQ5MDwaHkkHX4+Gph2mj6fbeQo1Hg71APLfWm+AzH7H7/ftP7y1U\nZg0TYu65f8Rh2tf8FG7eeTrHpiEsuf95igRLV1gv1ErD3q3lmPDDE7CmtTWuU5sQ\nlLxoimnSY6lWhJYQiZfzFuKND8e/8LCoQ4vt+dYs5ZaW5qQzT4pDILqmml13tiHy\nXSTmFF2asL/FeZyq0ZREypG/XTzC4AnUu+d5M/YNHI2o+TPtLWG0WxdJx7iG1WfS\n0td6GMI4Wp2w1gseN+1dv71G1d5uEnSInod5Hld9qThyRVHOXxHXMXErzhDEUjeM\nL9nwoLnYyp5iSiMMgy1gZ/2THQUtZ4HwZJhUmWiItJXPLdEGQ7/XN0Gi75u9iz55\naxlwAuX//hqPeflCvVfL\n=hbcF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T13:46:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDc1YzUzMTg3ZjdjN2UzMmZiYmZjZDIwYzU1M2UzNWNkMGQ2NjMwMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec","sha":"53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec"}],"sha":"75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/75c53187f7c7e32fbbfcd20c553e35cd0d663022"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77053927?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","id":77053927,"login":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDUzOTI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T13:19:17Z","email":"77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T13:19:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1093: Rename `button.new` from `+ New` to `New`. (#1752)\n\n## Purpose\nRename `button.new` from `+ New` to `New`.\n\n## Issues\nIt is required in the first scenario of\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1093 and in\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOM-1505","tree":{"sha":"a8941197483657aaefa2163c12a4c5b48e21e627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/a8941197483657aaefa2163c12a4c5b48e21e627"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec","verification":{"payload":"tree a8941197483657aaefa2163c12a4c5b48e21e627\nparent 21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750\nauthor Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com> 1785763157 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785763157 +0300\n\nSTCOR-1093: Rename `button.new` from `+ New` to `New`. (#1752)\n\n## Purpose\nRename `button.new` from `+ New` to `New`.\n\n## Issues\nIt is required in the first scenario of\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1093 and in\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOM-1505","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcJVVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATkEQAJShvmR38ytF6Pfx1T+9uX5i\nfsQ5AvGi3oDJRXcp9UzZA/jWwbqnDFP5XwcNZXtzr2fLD+CtDkz+4FYbDAwBDdNi\nT5Kt/TZpfSzOOKNAJjHoCpLs9SvxxW469jvfv87+PAfXy9+EscKiw2E88DmKRKnU\nqRIDXNaABybTX62ufDUF107JX/bGpUyLz5w81npBVUhfDaWMpaPPrissfnrCtnbA\nKhwayjcWXDLiyzU1gTFWkItZIlBOpoMBVFTnd4s5DyfSaQYzU5pALhghRUD5z6z8\nCRBX5FaYbP455neVvXw21YQCrhKF5wCgUDfgnIp9K+N76XZ9Y/Dakc91NmofNFA5\nEnkxjR/aIzCptgEUz6I+1bKxfxG7vM7EaZujmvJWvwoN/JzPsHWgTnOdALM7gdSl\nw4uE9/E7tATnq0YmrgXFD58vBDPlI/L6yuusLcnf2Tw2xOWpoWuiV8RatKEG/dke\ni7q54ckPhcGsvtaqOkW1cFukIEfPUT74RPVSiaufdhp8iWouJKjvvsfLtoqsABtr\nIL/mqa2Z1gOtLUa0+LQJvYz+KL2WwJh38o9eic5HxUaUlj0Nu6Ctmujda9fLn3Pv\ng7OJeICdT4hqXpiRtanio5hYs3sk4/p3aWBtFMv0iCeFuGTYRuH1i+QSdEPImCCJ\nYtsw7FbQI2RuTFjSpkyH\n=xgWc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T13:19:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDUzZDFlNzE3YjgyOWUwZWQ2OWRkOWJmMjI4YzJkNzhhOGQwYmZjZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750","sha":"21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750"}],"sha":"53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/53d1e717b829e0ed69dd9bf228c2d78a8d0bfcec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T19:02:30Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T19:02:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1087 always display correct session-time-remaining in banner (#1751)\n\nIf Stripes is initialized or tokens rotated close to the end of the\nsession in the interval when the \"warning, session is ending in MM:SS\"\nbanner is displayed, the countdown timer needs to be correctly\ninitialized with the actual time remaining. Previously, it was always\ninitialized with the config-value, e.g. 30s, then if the page is reloaded\nwith only 15s remaining in the session, the display would be inaccurate.\n\nRather than reading the config value when the timer pings in\nSessionEventContainer, this implementation performs the calculation when\nthe ResetTimers are configured during Stripes-init and during rotation,\nand then passes that value through when the timer pings. This keeps\ntimer-related logic centralized in the token-util functions, and\ninsulates SessionEventContainer from having to lookup session-expiration\ndata when responding to events.\n\nThe minor rearrangement of functions in OIDCLanding is so that\nSessionEventContainer has a chance to render and configure its event\nlisteners before the rotation handler is called to configure the\nend-of-session timers. If RT expiration is very short, or the RT-warning\nTTL is very long, it''s possible the timers could ping immediately on\nsetup, before the listeners have been configured, causing the event to\nbe ignored.\n\nAn initial implementation simply added an effect to\nSessionEventContainer, looking up the end-of-session timestamp and doing\nthe math there. This was a little simpler, but it felt icky. 1. It added\nan effect. 2. It polluted SessionEventContainer with logic that felt\nunrelated.\n\nRefs STCOR-1087","tree":{"sha":"5809b22019cdb3f2ea1686c9cc3478f98820d9d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/5809b22019cdb3f2ea1686c9cc3478f98820d9d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750","verification":{"payload":"tree 5809b22019cdb3f2ea1686c9cc3478f98820d9d4\nparent 73c2f97b2d59ec59ef910c5caec64b308d85bcf7\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1785524550 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785524550 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1087 always display correct session-time-remaining in banner (#1751)\n\nIf Stripes is initialized or tokens rotated close to the end of the\nsession in the interval when the \"warning, session is ending in MM:SS\"\nbanner is displayed, the countdown timer needs to be correctly\ninitialized with the actual time remaining. Previously, it was always\ninitialized with the config-value, e.g. 30s, then if the page is reloaded\nwith only 15s remaining in the session, the display would be inaccurate.\n\nRather than reading the config value when the timer pings in\nSessionEventContainer, this implementation performs the calculation when\nthe ResetTimers are configured during Stripes-init and during rotation,\nand then passes that value through when the timer pings. This keeps\ntimer-related logic centralized in the token-util functions, and\ninsulates SessionEventContainer from having to lookup session-expiration\ndata when responding to events.\n\nThe minor rearrangement of functions in OIDCLanding is so that\nSessionEventContainer has a chance to render and configure its event\nlisteners before the rotation handler is called to configure the\nend-of-session timers. If RT expiration is very short, or the RT-warning\nTTL is very long, it''s possible the timers could ping immediately on\nsetup, before the listeners have been configured, causing the event to\nbe ignored.\n\nAn initial implementation simply added an effect to\nSessionEventContainer, looking up the end-of-session timestamp and doing\nthe math there. This was a little simpler, but it felt icky. 1. It added\nan effect. 2. It polluted SessionEventContainer with logic that felt\nunrelated.\n\nRefs STCOR-1087","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbPFGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+WsQABrlSaQKnKXKA1+hGbRmrMnr\ni7xOPL6qAiVSsmZkre46u+sssxcdbjXEgPGxGl/aECxnq8mJYPEHS08KzMNOlGBV\nvZcVqTHq+RcqWkNJ46zUxRNrV2HCd5QeJGG2lpYR0osHBv+JyV652VLwLisrcRYh\nSxR+amC852g8Li4aoSkfP3+PwPWhc1XgfZRj8B6cTa7F/IkadWOhArKwMExlRJ6N\nbr93mQ1cMv/Hd9fj/2+lSFB9A8pG534hhRmjQSeYrKyPHWBpDKXe6vBDL2U7VEtv\nbgFwVHPoZH/9I5jKEXCSBfAZjV83kBN7F/Y2THoir43qZAyfenlaJb4Z45jiyOon\nHnS9L253/0XzoJv2stutFatAKQt1kL6woo0A0qfelKvdut6KYC4uP3lW1aKh9ROp\nSZQwH0kUlipmuI2wfiKDG5+6QDAvEWuvRfrf+B0p0R7iu7znw6E3RJxO/d4RKDVA\nmYxafKeIUKxhCFq4QIIWDGXPmiOo3of7Sjztjiuad/USpSIsJDEYbJbjUSseNKIe\nNzIKzZi9dNJLjSsDoD5qmoG4n1AMztzlpO+ORzmme5nUc07zHrfUuVShNoCBEkN7\nOWjiljFGeRgs+W+re7OoVoVflKp2pj+zZmNvNdK+akBxdeXa16NGupfmOCP8OOwP\nKJiXZcdxjs+XnUHFXae1\n=94Rg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-31T19:02:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDIxYjU2OGFkZTJhYzdjN2JlODQxNDM3MzQwZTYyODg0ODFkYjk3NTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/73c2f97b2d59ec59ef910c5caec64b308d85bcf7","sha":"73c2f97b2d59ec59ef910c5caec64b308d85bcf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/73c2f97b2d59ec59ef910c5caec64b308d85bcf7"}],"sha":"21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/21b568ade2ac7c7be841437340e6288481db9750"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/73c2f97b2d59ec59ef910c5caec64b308d85bcf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-11T12:48:48Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-11T12:48:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-780 show a \"please reload!\" banner when entitlement changes (#1749)\n\nPeriodically poll the entitlement endpoint\n`entitlements/${tenant}/applications` and compare the previous/current\nlist of application versions. When there are changes, show an\ninteractive \"please reload\" banner.\n\nThis implementation borrows heavily from StaleBundleWarning but is\ndifferent in several important ways:\n* Only poll the entitlement API, not an arbitrary path. Because this\n  path is dynamic (it contains the tenant as a path param) it could not\n  easily be listed as a config param in `stripes.config.js`.\n* Only compare changes to entitlement, not the entire API response. The\n  entitlement response contains a lot of data. A LOT. Much of it is\n  operational, e.g. memory allocation, port bindings, etc., which could\n  change but which do not correpond to an entitlement change.\n\nRefs STCOR-780","tree":{"sha":"869f36e77cbf6f13889ef4a5f8cfbcda1f09789a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/869f36e77cbf6f13889ef4a5f8cfbcda1f09789a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/73c2f97b2d59ec59ef910c5caec64b308d85bcf7","verification":{"payload":"tree 869f36e77cbf6f13889ef4a5f8cfbcda1f09789a\nparent 808b2f092f85abb543cc256a209bf07d3cd5b071\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1783774128 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783774128 -0400\n\nSTCOR-780 show a \"please reload!\" banner when entitlement changes (#1749)\n\nPeriodically poll the entitlement endpoint\n`entitlements/${tenant}/applications` and compare the previous/current\nlist of application versions. When there are changes, show an\ninteractive \"please reload\" banner.\n\nThis implementation borrows heavily from StaleBundleWarning but is\ndifferent in several important ways:\n* Only poll the entitlement API, not an arbitrary path. Because this\n  path is dynamic (it contains the tenant as a path param) it could not\n  easily be listed as a config param in `stripes.config.js`.\n* Only compare changes to entitlement, not the entire API response. The\n  entitlement response contains a lot of data. A LOT. Much of it is\n  operational, e.g. memory allocation, port bindings, etc., which could\n  change but which do not correpond to an entitlement change.\n\nRefs STCOR-780","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUjuwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJTEQAFWxMVC2Zl9n0Z/XW7ZJw0FH\nydXeTFnsATabcDxkPgR5EAtx5fYb6imSzqqh5EqJFxCFRvfyKd23s5KejB2H7KIr\nX1+jfH8EaOh4H8nuLha5Jvt4ccs7dHMgbhyV54+25PuZ2Qm01u2b0arDOEZ4ELQk\nUU16jYxmz/+st5WMERqiaCcxZbgEIpla1JnDWbTu6XOX6uqNrQjPsJubGEHuJiXu\nmvsDP3v3FczjUnWshmXvAxQS0pIcT8UHm+5TjN26RFWVslIcw2YokuXqcM4yAv59\nhENGgNZi8jGKOgB9dl+z9SG4K9sf2jc3XmbHSi/QkHh74Z5VA/7WqDVE4m0P6tMX\nJZ4Twt8v22+w3anISSNmeeIlAHgdTcOwdUENPcqC1cr2TkwliHJ3ftsmLN1Qr3tR\nq21lkn+hA2zZFBM47IRgsz4FFu+RMWVXF+uHwTFPwRGy2Vt1hi4uBAihFNlzIfAu\nnFuI3zzN2W4A9qBHWoXRtkjwLPSfBQaWG5c0eVUYmCFnAYFPVm1BbLAASGZ262Sl\nPXZjprI9KR4OLFynwlvL0HLL5KBqt1GxT2w4dNDN8F4DPSpDxeBkbOIDAs5ohq5a\nXtQ6vKKfwrOutwRB1VKfxlXbXGlxW51fgGDf7XBv3EbvMidiUQCT2VUy9HxryllY\nBdPBMi5ZJb3yN2RCWkvF\n=TQBM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-11T12:48:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User",