f for paneTitleRef instead of element for focus-management fix. (#1747)\n\n## [STCOR-1083](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1083)\nThis resolved the focus-management issue where focus should move to the\nlisting pane when the user navigates to Settings from the Apps dropdown\nin the main navigation.\n\nThis was a simple fix of providing a ref instead of the `ref.current`\nfor `paneTitleRef` on the listing pane of Settings.","tree":{"sha":"6c2b28bb51467c770d2950f532bd6388386c6d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/6c2b28bb51467c770d2950f532bd6388386c6d9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/808b2f092f85abb543cc256a209bf07d3cd5b071","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c2b28bb51467c770d2950f532bd6388386c6d9c\nparent 5bfe52819b4118d340ac80bda477404a63cc2a78\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1783604381 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783604381 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1083 - Use ref for paneTitleRef instead of element for focus-management fix. (#1747)\n\n## [STCOR-1083](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1083)\nThis resolved the focus-management issue where focus should move to the\nlisting pane when the user navigates to Settings from the Apps dropdown\nin the main navigation.\n\nThis was a simple fix of providing a ref instead of the `ref.current`\nfor `paneTitleRef` on the listing pane of Settings.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6SdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvbIQAGfEaHBoYYApWuHvF1PQ7/KH\nSDTDzW7K4eWkwxO50/+2l4TgJX82X4k4jMI0GicJWNda+MEv92A+ijDBKzIAQ1qi\nk4dbldtgfmfwp1wufr7zaq52FTDaFSABu/AyyVqsCeJkQq9OdTTj1owi3kIWUIDh\nqa6aBqc5KRftt6pgHBOBOemB9v0Zo4Uf4eGLchYf266sOtF4Dg9eKWMeuK1QitLx\ncSphawpF42GlTRNOk/MW0nz4BjBg6UYYee/xkgLMM7BkvmKsE5PyRsRv30BHWSEC\noL8Pk5wxLJ1rPmC4VFXlIP9+aPQBRrK5iZhJo8BXOzcsCINr3/WHc6z+Wati6GqX\n/a/MntFL8MfBjAtNeQqspacHf96gpowX5StbA2KfurrjPm4eYTtBZI5hsI7XhklS\nNgHxISQiO0ndecvMWKEmi9od/9ll12SsYhZ6948HDKXBZHty1SRHfbXW