pos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/bac7b7578fd3f86a2c80ea02330c7a9b154a614e"}],"sha":"700a4ac304e94f834793c0dc49479c17b58b81ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/700a4ac304e94f834793c0dc49479c17b58b81ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/bac7b7578fd3f86a2c80ea02330c7a9b154a614e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T21:21:39Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T21:21:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1080 do not handle non-rotation errors as fatal errors (#1742)\n\n`rotateAndReplay()` has two jobs: rotate and replay. Rotation-related\nerrors are fatal, but replay-related errors are not. For example, if the\nrotation request itself fails, or times out, or the response data cannot\nbe stored, those are all fatal errors that need to cause session\ntermination. But if a replay request fails, then such errors should\nbubble back to the caller, same as they would if the request failed\noutside `rotateAndReplay()`. Until this PR, this PR, both failures\ncalled `config.onFailure()`, effectively treating non-rotation\n(non-fatal) errors as fatal errors. Whoops.\n\nThis PR wraps all rotation-related errors in `RTRError` in order to make\nit easy for the `rotateAndReplay()` catch-block to distinguish fatal\nrotation errors from non-fatal fetch errors, calling\n`config.onFailure()` only for the former.\n\nA common-cause of fetch-failures appears to be AbortControllers used to\ninterrupt fetch calls when navigating away from the route that fired the\nfetch. For example, some stripes-smart-components provide `useQuery`\nfunctions that accept a `signal` argument that react-query can use to\ncancel an in-flight fetch. As noted in MDN''s AbortSignal documentation:\n> When abort() is called, the fetch() promise rejects with a\n> DOMException named AbortError.\n\nThere are two approaches we could take in the catch clause:\n1. call `config.onFailure()` only when we find specific errors we know\n  are fatal (e.g. an RTRError)\n2. call `config.onFailure()` by default, skipping it only when we find\n  specific errors we know are non-fatal (e.g. an AbortError)\n\nGiven the severe consequences of a fatal error (i.e. forced logout),\nthis PR implements the former, choosing to look only for the specific\nerrors we know to be fatal. The tradeoff is that this allows non-fatal\nerrors to escape back to the application where it may not be completely\nclear how to handle them. At present, this feels like an acceptable\ntradeoff.\n\nRefs STCOR-1080","tree":{"sha":"c29488269c4c6f4cd04c5794dfaf924e237c9ff2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/c29488269c4c6f4cd04c5794dfaf924e237c9ff2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/bac7b7578fd3f86a2c80ea02330c7a9b154a614e","verification":{"payload":"tree c29488269c4c6f4cd04c5794dfaf924e237c9ff2\nparent c7f97ab1115d74dadf93f12ab25cb2956ac2f511\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1782508899 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782508899 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1080 do not handle non-rotation errors as fatal errors (#1742)\n\n`rotateAndReplay()` has two jobs: rotate and replay. Rotation-related\nerrors are fatal, but replay-related errors are not. For example, if the\nrotation request itself fails, or times out, or the response data cannot\nbe stored, those are all fatal errors that need to cause session\ntermination. But if a replay request fails, then such errors should\nbubble back to the caller, same as they would if the request failed\noutside `rotateAndReplay()`. Until this PR, this PR, both failures\ncalled `config.onFailure()`, effectively treating non-rotation\n(non-fatal) errors as fatal errors. Whoops.\n\nThis PR wraps all rotation-related errors in `RTRError` in order to make\nit easy for the `rotateAndReplay()` catch-block to distinguish fatal\nrotation errors from non-fatal fetch errors, calling\n`config.onFailure()` only for the former.\n\nA common-cause of fetch-failures appears to be AbortControllers used to\ninterrupt fetch calls when navigating away from the route that fired the\nfetch. For example, some stripes-smart-components provide `useQuery`\nfunctions that accept a `signal` argument that react-query can use to\ncancel an in-flight fetch. As noted in MDN''s AbortSignal documentation:\n> When abort() is called, the fetch() promise rejects with a\n> DOMException named AbortError.\n\nThere are two approaches we could take in the catch clause:\n1. call `config.onFailure()` only when we find specific errors we know\n  are fatal (e.g. an RTRError)\n2. call `config.onFailure()` by default, skipping it only when we find\n  specific errors we know are non-fatal (e.g. an AbortError)\n\nGiven the severe consequences of a fatal error (i.e. forced logout),\nthis PR implements the former, choosing to look only for the specific\nerrors we know to be fatal. The tradeoff is that this allows non-fatal\nerrors to escape back to the application where it may not be completely\nclear how to handle them. At present, this feels like an acceptable\ntradeoff.\n\nRefs STCOR-1080","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPu1jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfyoQAH+PZpx7lEBE/WDiDEwmKQe4\n3EOscxVJpvzSDrUibctCrgO+bSSNXr9PKLa3rY7nXAegHzIy9xLKyw/zqJJYt6/L\n7PC+N8yYH4biIuBibiCRvssz1+pqgAlZE6GMrZvWmbV1t56Ks7Ix+fwE3mdDD7pt\nrCSXHYQpBr2tXEtnAnpdSdpUebSrnyg1YjLu83td7GgESkVDV8Aelgj/eeSRLcqT\nCwFc5csQHVFju+yZg6BmbS7ycQk1K6rPja7NWq+GTd7Wluc487HrSCOXwOxFsRre\nE/sjbqOMQbKb9eeVwzZuCA1+V5gEOMGkIFqCxjsmXiU+HRcT16SyWk1JKVJvCx6s\nfRyhoWdRmstK9o0liiypDvWnS3bLdNAPZUsAlTN5ylQhH/sKWf0HTIh9/I6uaSih\nHCkeQ8pewfUroeGtYT/CQC/GNnDHaDorvTi8NiDlv1PccYCXWlaHfH1Ri6fJBfDK\nliqPzpib+Tlb1tR7i6PfsMky8WCIP+wrRl4kCSYLyC69LHxIh0Mf6IgaKwOhFogn\nIKrgKI+AGVZsVbcSoWb9JH61gRU9w7Wy8tRabldVb2OPPMOqfNT43xNwd4+F6O1M\nrkYt7n49FctqBzSaxLbE46A7Z1n8/N1hyDy2Q/FXtkfd6QPlGfZCrs6m39Izszfk\n/svm65xQUngK4TEGzbmZ\n=s5IW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T21:21:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/bac7b7578fd3f86a2c80ea02330c7a9b154a614e","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGJhYzdiNzU3OGZkM2Y4NmEyYzgwZWEwMjMzMGM3YTliMTU0YTYxNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/c7f97ab1115d74dadf93f12ab25cb2956ac2f511","sha":"c7f97ab1115d74dadf93f12ab25cb2956ac2f511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/c7f97ab1115d74dadf93f12ab25cb2956ac2f511"}],"sha":"bac7b7578fd3f86a2c80ea02330c7a9b154a614e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/bac7b7578fd3f86a2c80ea02330c7a9b154a614e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/c7f97ab1115d74dadf93f12ab25cb2956ac2f511/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-26T11:08:42Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-26T11:08:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1081 label Root.js as having side-effects (#1743)\n\nAs described and solved by @Dmytro-Melnyshyn:\n> `webpack` 5.108.0 introduced a `LazyBarrelController` optimization\nthat defers side-effect-only imports (`import ''./Root.css''`) inside\nmodules marked as side-effect-free. Since sideEffects: `[''*.css'']` marks\nall JS files (including `Root.js`) as side-effect-free, `Root.css` gets\npermanently deferred and is dropped from the bundle.\n>\n> Fix: add `\"**/Root/Root.js\"` to the `sideEffects` array in\n`package.json`. This marks `Root.js` as having side effects, so the\noptimization is skipped for it and the CSS import is processed normally.\n\nLazyBarrelOptimization has not made it into the webpack documentation\nyet, but is described in other bundlers\n([rspack](https://rspack.rs/guide/optimization/lazy-barrel),\n[rolldown](https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/lazy-barrel-optimization)).\n\nRefs STCOR-1081","tree":{"sha":"38286656a49817654bc5591fb7e864da94c58de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/38286656a49817654bc5591fb7e864da94c58de5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/c7f97ab1115d74dadf93f12ab25cb2956ac2f511","verification":{"payload":"tree 38286656a49817654bc5591fb7e864da94c58de5\nparent 3598bfe1cbfe7350718434cb6c47cb00f7a5fc4a\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1782472122 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782472122 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1081 label Root.js as having side-effects (#1743)\n\nAs described and solved by @Dmytro-Melnyshyn:\n> `webpack` 5.108.0 introduced a `LazyBarrelController` optimization\nthat defers side-effect-only imports (`import ''./Root.css''`) inside\nmodules marked as side-effect-free. Since sideEffects: `[''*.css'']` marks\nall JS files (including `Root.js`) as side-effect-free, `Root.css` gets\npermanently deferred and is dropped from the bundle.\n>\n> Fix: add `\"**/Root/Root.js\"` to the `sideEffects` array in\n`package.json`. This marks `Root.js` as having side effects, so the\noptimization is skipped for it and the CSS import is processed normally.\n\nLazyBarrelOptimization has not made it into the webpack documentation\nyet, but is described in other bundlers\n([rspack](https://rspack.rs/guide/optimization/lazy-barrel),\n[rolldown](https://rolldown.rs/in-depth/lazy-barrel-optimization)).\n\nRefs STCOR-1081","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPl26CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5SAQAJ++XYDpJQuoRVlrS84CYpOk\nX+WfzY76B+7H3W4iTrprh3bOlAD7lYMClYayfWVIsg9mke/ENGz55zrLp3B0nqpp\nIh98bwU+pgqZRjJmjfAYDhKTyJm6BHTcjEeb8vlZil2/9RrWk7ki+2+zFmFZCFgo\n7J4cSnULivxxdAyKFwhC6ntbwlhY/0/pnMJoBhpshXoc0JL57DjFMqPHvHvDh0yV\nXu8H8apMuD7dDBWYfnW7BJOSLFYQFb05INAV+kKHOqZ6ZdbLGaVFruXexDN0lk1W\n7WERvBTdXDuOs2AyJ2rsslZ98GIbeuH3q6YRsK2GEK4GFgO2M+uppoupL61iYWR/\nNxAaJzkhNOuc7/1DKdWR5RwqzlJOUAPat9AL+eIEwoIT5cSbwgaKnfOx9S2WQW2m\nLjGTWrZNhorz72j03pghPOci1QjyQIA5nwwQmDj4yCvtFSuViseD/kWCQniPQf41\nQ40l1R0QkGbP45gmgIH1w+SqaMZdwLTUQKyr7Npn/J8IbF/bkkb9sy50iTiv0ZfT\naaiCxHYYYIQL1zvY9uHX5Sq0JpdnC7nJIVJlMQ+9W/rznA/8Aw27iikFchG3ncH/\na7NW6VIbAXpETaLPBoetPlWPQ1KJ9lh8yWNTbal0bjOqF/HsFwXR3rr2G0hDqn/i\nNRHWBEbNo93nvdQk0HDw\n=E+Sr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-26T11:08:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type"