out-redirect URI (#1739)\n\nWhoops, don''t hard-code the post-logout redirect URI passed to Keycloak.\nThe correct value is the current hostname. Somehow, I missed this in the\noriginal PR, #1737.\n\nRefs STCOR-1067","tree":{"sha":"7284f1eb752d39a7c55bb67e9385549b696ccaef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/7284f1eb752d39a7c55bb67e9385549b696ccaef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/3598bfe1cbfe7350718434cb6c47cb00f7a5fc4a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7284f1eb752d39a7c55bb67e9385549b696ccaef\nparent d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1781705854 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781705854 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1067 followup: pass dynamic post-logout-redirect URI (#1739)\n\nWhoops, don''t hard-code the post-logout redirect URI passed to Keycloak.\nThe correct value is the current hostname. Somehow, I missed this in the\noriginal PR, #1737.\n\nRefs STCOR-1067","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMqx+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPgIQAGMd3CKn2QawkYGdi7LOp6lI\nnUTbInvP5S+CvJ/dy1Gp4JmKAuW/Hg0ORhi9AL1bmQuRRFZMcCsgmMhRuJQlC0VL\nEr2Gzg6M3ektasf2zRcM7Km577lP36BS4/T+t0VtghBS7aA0Iwb3qal24YGW+r6/\nckE1xI6OUR66DQB44or318s3ftFrn/zMALFzmpAHTUL0C0L1xpHcupU1V8Ys+cDA\nukPGXnuBj5DZONF0JgwyBcQOwhK9QFdGujiwbMW7iWiWKf8S3l/DLiNWcGwPhTe0\nG/i5Nr1Q0Wc9uYxnpHiTvnsnsuSuV7pP0UrcKUF5RU2pqkJEy7bGhlE40KyQS0+I\ngE82fmG0F6/xaQo6+/njZwrLAopSd41lkJHaRhMv67PpT5y+jVN7p/4xq6QBDPE8\ngup//o/5RuznALc+od0W9FWNmmO3CByccVhhyYdlqTeyQp1m5P5JLc1JmvFgRSY+\n7CvnbU+k5xEj+DSckcKERPjfrrxheK/54bgXPxwudctO77unMhymk9Kl1mJom/HN\nbanXGP83Yp68kD3dnUqXN0AJ8KAC1tGssrmSwJTL/JoWoK6xyq0VpKzTROzTmRAM\nPuyWZICuIEZDHaGYfCl1Pvag+TLD/SH+bjJ7O5CTB7DnlQGWlMs4ZsHYn7jszx6t\n1Gg7euEYsSjjRcZVI7fu\n=sl/z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-17T14:17:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/3598bfe1cbfe7350718434cb6c47cb00f7a5fc4a","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDM1OThiZmUxY2JmZTczNTA3MTg0MzRjYjZjNDdjYjAwZjdhNWZjNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7","sha":"d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7"}],"sha":"3598bfe1cbfe7350718434cb6c47cb00f7a5fc4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/3598bfe1cbfe7350718434cb6c47cb00f7a5fc4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T14:53:07Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T14:53:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1067 reliably sync browser, FOLIO, and Keycloak sessions on logout (#1738)\n\nReliably terminate both the FOLIO and Keycloak sessions on logout and\nwhen there is an error during OTP-exchange on login.\n\nThree things need to be in sync for a session to function correctly:\n* FOLIO cookies (used to make API requests)\n* Keycloak cookies (used to track authentication)\n* Browser storage (use to track user state)\n\nStripes only has access to browser storage and has to intuit whether the\ncookies are present based on API responses. Effectively, data in storage\nis a signal to Stripes that cookies are present, and therefore that API\nrequests should succeed. During logout, if storage is populated but API\nrequests fail, Stripes interprets this as \"sessions are out of sync\" and\nwill redirect to Keycloak to guarantee that its session gets terminated.\n\nStripes makes the same assumption, and handles things the same way,\nduring login if OTP exchange fails, e.g. if Keycloak is available but\nthe API gateway is down. In this situation, the user will be able to\nauthenticate and start a Keycloak session but will not be able to start\na FOLIO session. Previously, Stripes simply displayed an error message\nin this situation; now, Stripes recognizes the OTP exchange failure as a\nsync error and redirects to Keycloak accordingly to terminate that\nsession.\n\nThe most important changes here are in useLogoutMutation, now structured\nlike this:\n```\ntry {\n  API call to /logout\n}\ncatch {\n  if error, redirect to Keycloak\n}\nfinally {\n  clear browser storage\n}\n```\nWhen storage is populated and the `/authn/logout` API request fails,\nStripes treats this as a session-sync error and redirects to Keycloak to\nforce that session to terminate. If storage is empty, as it will be on a\nsecondary tab after the primary tab has already made the API call and\nthen cleared storage, Stripes recognizes this as an expected outcome.\n\nRefs STCOR-1067","tree":{"sha":"54ce37cfee7011ddf906bc751c9b25c2ed064019","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/54ce37cfee7011ddf906bc751c9b25c2ed064019"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 54ce37cfee7011ddf906bc751c9b25c2ed064019\nparent abaa4dee1f0c47a29f4b853a1e9816c15c919812\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1781621587 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781621587 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1067 reliably sync browser, FOLIO, and Keycloak sessions on logout (#1738)\n\nReliably terminate both the FOLIO and Keycloak sessions on logout and\nwhen there is an error during OTP-exchange on login.\n\nThree things need to be in sync for a session to function correctly:\n* FOLIO cookies (used to make API requests)\n* Keycloak cookies (used to track authentication)\n* Browser storage (use to track user state)\n\nStripes only has access to browser storage and has to intuit whether the\ncookies are present based on API responses. Effectively, data in storage\nis a signal to Stripes that cookies are present, and therefore that API\nrequests should succeed. During logout, if storage is populated but API\nrequests fail, Stripes interprets this as \"sessions are out of sync\" and\nwill redirect to Keycloak to guarantee that its session gets terminated.\n\nStripes makes the same assumption, and handles things the same way,\nduring login if OTP exchange fails, e.g. if Keycloak is available but\nthe API gateway is down. In this situation, the user will be able to\nauthenticate and start a Keycloak session but will not be able to start\na FOLIO session. Previously, Stripes simply displayed an error message\nin this situation; now, Stripes recognizes the OTP exchange failure as a\nsync error and redirects to Keycloak accordingly to terminate that\nsession.\n\nThe most important changes here are in useLogoutMutation, now structured\nlike this:\n```\ntry {\n  API call to /logout\n}\ncatch {\n  if error, redirect to Keycloak\n}\nfinally {\n  clear browser storage\n}\n```\nWhen storage is populated and the `/authn/logout` API request fails,\nStripes treats this as a session-sync error and redirects to Keycloak to\nforce that session to terminate. If storage is empty, as it will be on a\nsecondary tab after the primary tab has already made the API call and\nthen cleared storage, Stripes recognizes this as an expected outcome.\n\nRefs STCOR-1067","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMWNTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfm8QAGAMAsOwaAOmXFs2paFu44N5\n9pt5QYCG9Z8Q8Dvh1FZ7nNCpAUm1YQrUhPPauUo1X7BqBaUGqxLld1Af+DVDFSEg\ndSpdBlpybRLkglt0WhxnedV5wpYW2gj1YaCZE2tWCpncqsUcFuM9c8+Purx+yLWZ\nfMplYwowv0p16xjzVrKzMFcYSzCh1FQmCV70ZUo4JQZxdvXHD6rTJEeHU5yNR5Mv\nQXhBbQCZ9QY+5zysV8BwJ1om92mv9zWJLcmubqpZyCOBK+D81T5EmYn+PEb97L+r\ntRUvZNpv/bd1MP5BZCawgyA5vP0Z4+fScgNld96E1QOexvn0fUlQvHLAyITce3H9\nnJ9Kw1yznI4i+iFZjXH25Idrks/QnoEdN6somGlChtv/1JO0EihiqJxXKIKUhuig\nd34r36pCURO1lsnVVvdXQjqQcQSehECXZKcDAwVOfGeVqgPLW88gknGHz2Kghiwa\nae+wDxXXLQFeeozpOE670QkgPVi+Gy52sUi3FWXyvovHYwRb98qIaSeLWFzcjAOU\nbtrE9Qf5WHoS41AFWqhrOVnc2ey//GUYj1AKxuIxBJzcQRzCT6euSr6QjiIbibnv\np4+guamLnKkXkE+KTs9ltEFJM5e7TV1pcE885us/J4e73DnqH6z7/lnjiaFcW3vY\nYUImBe4EbglP9MlCsygw\n=WcKL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-16T14:53:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGQ3NWM4ZDBjNTJiN2NhZTQwZTg2YmY5MGRiY2RlZWUyZTJlMzc2Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/abaa4dee1f0c47a29f4b853a1e9816c15c919812","sha":"abaa4dee1f0c47a29f4b853a1e9816c15c919812","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/abaa4dee1f0c47a29f4b853a1e9816c15c919812"}],"sha":"d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/d75c8d0c52b7cae40e86bf90dbcdeee2e2e376c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/abaa4dee1f0c47a29f4b853a1e9816c15c919812/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T12:55:38Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T12:55:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1069 proactive rotation skips initial play (#1737)\n\n## setup\n\nRequests can enter `rotateAndReplay()` for two reasons:\n1. inspecting storage shows expired tokens, so we are rotating\n  preventively\n2. response inspection suggests expired tokens, so we are rotating\n  reactively\n\nPrior to this PR, the steps in `rotateAndReplay()` were roughly these:\n1. attempt replay of the request in case tokens have been refreshed\n2. rotate\n3. replay\n\n## approach\n\nThis PR addresses a logic flaw in step 1: When a request invokes\npreventive rotation, there should not be a pre-rotation replay.\nPreventive rotation amounts to \"I''m invoking rotation due to a current\nproblem with storage\". As long as that problem persists, there is no\nvalue in replay because we would expect replay to fail. Reactive\nrotation amounts to \"I''m invoking rotation due to past problem with\nstorage\". In this situation, it''s worth inspecting storage and replaying\nif the problem appears to have cleared. Of course, it''s possible storage\nappears to be ok but is actually out of sync, in which case the replay\nwill fail, and we will proceed with rotation.\n\nThe new function, `shouldPreRotate`, enables preventive rotation. \n\n## gory details/additional work\n\n* `usePasswordRules.js` retrieve `ky` from a common hook\n* `PasswordValidationField.js` trivial lint cleanup\n* `useOkapiKy.js::usePublicGatewayKy()` new hook to supply `rtrIgnore`\nto native fetch; previously, ky-based requests with this property were\nnot actually bypassing RTR; instead, they were triggering RTR and then\nsucceeding during the (now-removed) pre-rotation replay (whoops)\n* `loginServices.js::getSSOEnabled()` supply missing `rtrIgnore`\nattribute\n* `withOkapiKy.js` retrieve `ky` from a common hook\n* `PasswordValidationField.js` remove this failing test since the\ncomponent is orphaned; at some point, we should remove the component too\n* `profile-dropdown-test.js` must supply `userLoggedIn` to cause storage\nto be properly populated so that when a fetch is triggered, RTR''s new\npreventive-rotation inspector finds data in storage to inspect\n\nRefs STCOR-1069","tree":{"sha":"3e46a7deb7d97626a8c9a1b034b4d49527863db7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/3e46a7deb7d97626a8c9a1b034b4d49527863db7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/abaa4dee1f0c47a29f4b853a1e9816c15c919812","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e46a7deb7d97626a8c9a1b034b4d49527863db7\nparent da52648a85b95dacf1a1ce27f3a55508258b405b\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1781268938 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781268938 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1069 proactive rotation skips initial play (#1737)\n\n## setup\n\nRequests can enter `rotateAndReplay()` for two reasons:\n1. inspecting storage shows expired tokens, so we are rotating\n  preventively\n2. response inspection suggests expired tokens, so we are rotating\n  reactively\n\nPrior to this PR, the steps in `rotateAndReplay()` were roughly these:\n1. attempt replay of the request in case tokens have been refreshed\n2. rotate\n3. replay\n\n## approach\n\nThis PR addresses a logic flaw in step 1: When a request invokes\npreventive rotation, there should not be a pre-rotation replay.\nPreventive rotation amounts to \"I''m invoking rotation due to a current\nproblem with storage\". As long as that problem persists, there is no\nvalue in replay because we would expect replay to fail. Reactive\nrotation amounts to \"I''m invoking rotation due to past problem with\nstorage\". In this situation, it''s worth inspecting storage and replaying\nif the problem appears to have cleared. Of course, it''s possible storage\nappears to be ok but is actually out of sync, in which case the replay\nwill fail, and we will proceed with rotation.\n\nThe new function, `shouldPreRotate`, enables preventive rotation. \n\n## gory details/additional work\n\n* `usePasswordRules.js` retrieve `ky` from a common hook\n* `PasswordValidationField.js` trivial lint cleanup\n* `useOkapiKy.js::usePublicGatewayKy()` new hook to supply `rtrIgnore`\nto native fetch; previously, ky-based requests with this property were\nnot actually bypassing RTR; instead, they were triggering RTR and then\nsucceeding during the (now-removed) pre-rotation replay (whoops)\n* `loginServices.js::getSSOEnabled()` supply missing `rtrIgnore`\nattribute\n* `withOkapiKy.js` retrieve `ky` from a common hook\n* `PasswordValidationField.js` remove this failing test since the\ncomponent is orphaned; at some point, we should remove the component too\n* `profile-dropdown-test.js` must supply `userLoggedIn` to cause storage\nto be properly populated so that when a fetch is triggered, RTR''s new\npreventive-rotation inspector finds data in storage to inspect\n\nRefs STCOR-1069","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLAHKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+jEQAFY4GsecGXgBsswbhiIdTk/k\nvtS0MpgXuSLF1lA3ptn+SNmv/F4K1mBfCtX0tIL574wXNzXTY7FrmJPWziycbRN3\n6W8ryR8O2gjtqab4Xnyojry+miRcD7PXvjKS/sYn8e1uF714VJYvJfPookvsThuB\nZE