flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/da52648a85b95dacf1a1ce27f3a55508258b405b","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGRhNTI2NDhhODViOTVkYWNmMWExY2UyN2YzYTU1NTA4MjU4YjQwNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305","sha":"2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305"}],"sha":"da52648a85b95dacf1a1ce27f3a55508258b405b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/da52648a85b95dacf1a1ce27f3a55508258b405b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T19:22:02Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T19:22:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1068 call /authn/refresh prior to /authn/logout (#1730)\n\nCall `/authn/refresh` immediately prior to calling `/authn/logout`,\nincreasing the chances of successfully terminating the session.\n\nWhen a normal API call fails due to lack of an AT, it returns 401. When\nthe `/authn/logout` API call fails due to lack of an AT, it returns 422\nand destroys the RT, preventing rotation and thus preventing the\noriginal request from being replayed, which prevents the Keycloak\nsession from being terminated.\n\nIn an effort to prevent this cascade of calamaties, calling\n`/authn/refresh` during logout helps increase the likelihood that the\nentire process will succeed. It''s not a guarantee, but every little bit\nhelps.\n\nRefs STCOR-1068","tree":{"sha":"d7cc0f229cac81dbc5a701d73e64d6f9dcc5ad1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/d7cc0f229cac81dbc5a701d73e64d6f9dcc5ad1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305","verification":{"payload":"tree d7cc0f229cac81dbc5a701d73e64d6f9dcc5ad1a\nparent 6e9ade8ef39643404a076dc82564e05ff9c7ecd7\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1780514522 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780514522 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1068 call /authn/refresh prior to /authn/logout (#1730)\n\nCall `/authn/refresh` immediately prior to calling `/authn/logout`,\nincreasing the chances of successfully terminating the session.\n\nWhen a normal API call fails due to lack of an AT, it returns 401. When\nthe `/authn/logout` API call fails due to lack of an AT, it returns 422\nand destroys the RT, preventing rotation and thus preventing the\noriginal request from being replayed, which prevents the Keycloak\nsession from being terminated.\n\nIn an effort to prevent this cascade of calamaties, calling\n`/authn/refresh` during logout helps increase the likelihood that the\nentire process will succeed. It''s not a guarantee, but every little bit\nhelps.\n\nRefs STCOR-1068","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIH7aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqyAQAC7HrJA08mrLuo/KwX7gPyqC\ne3gfqUEJdclaolNG9pYNTa4kiUc9ojVZ6VjbIiNM84t1Ys6zkYlHOdrh82BBixe/\nn+u7NG6m0Ike8u9DliuPksLmJuAmeSBwub3CwPC4snqF9EDPKv6/W42t+FqJ+z2c\nkzLYyJbURyXKxQH5kEhurJGNsf+nyUpILRZzZSEBRZIJcM+rDC7ZNBfS2blQB5x9\n9BxsIk38NcwfPJ3mStUGrBRhYqCzHOM7/eOWgp/ffDjVqQqyuHtNs/jroWqq1fR3\n4n70KiETaJZJsDMwvFKk9E+EwlceL+b/yrN5WefR2kXa3KAa15EFm2I7FnvmmAXo\nsXKMZRjxyBp+HVHXRDkYQq0+HnUQtLd4oUbZ8/E14sxZDORA5sGUdR1nvMenRQbf\nATrGxR+KpOJkqT57nr7pGwWj0QYiue5p5TzYcXZUb68iu6Dav9ct6J4l+yA9YgVf\nrTlQWnNIA7BqfVItF4hXokTlKI+Xs2Bu1pasOkhMtQQLLzqrQN3MJ4xRy/yoV55G\nJ2CG+6G3cIbdN4a+PndQWGTE526X97jmkPqjtKpBsW4bk96pI+9qAd4+WBJw4BnR\nyjYkYhfW0r490ScIxsw1nl0TlKibfpspRzp2G/2vq5I9RlfqgES4+xdTHi74CiD4\nF1AlWOLN0nmPL1iOkcK2\n=OflT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-03T19:22:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDJjZTVlNzQxNTBmYTUxMWQwMTZjYjBkYzE4ZjMyN2QxMTk2ZjkzMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/6e9ade8ef39643404a076dc82564e05ff9c7ecd7","sha":"6e9ade8ef39643404a076dc82564e05ff9c7ecd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/6e9ade8ef39643404a076dc82564e05ff9c7ecd7"}],"sha":"2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/2ce5e74150fa511d016cb0dc18f327d1196f9305"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/6e9ade8ef39643404a076dc82564e05ff9c7ecd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T16:06:05Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T16:06:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1069 - Check AT pre-emptively on fetches to avoid lots of 401''s (#1732)\n\n## [STCOR-1069](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1069)\n\nGiven that we''ve got good expiry information stored, we''ll leverage it\nto reduce the number of initial 401''s.\n\nThis approach reduces the pile of initial 401''s from the `shared` lock\nby circumventing their initial request and putting it off until rotation\nhas happened.\n\nApproach:\nCheck atExpiry before each initial fetch. \nIf the token is expired, set an `atExpired` flag and pass it to\n`rotateAndReplay` as part of the `original` object.\nRotate if `original.atExpired` is true, rather than inspecting the\noriginal response (circumvent the `shouldRotate()` call.)\n\nFXHR: left as-is... there''s nothing async about XHR - if we DO want this\ncheck prior to, then we have to move the expiry from indexDB to\nlocalStorage and check that directly - our wrapping utility in\n`loginServices` was well-intended, but not usable in this case.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","tree":{"sha":"cccd1a2cc0693e76aa51d0d60e69e0b8e1b6cbd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/cccd1a2cc0693e76aa51d0d60e69e0b8e1b6cbd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/6e9ade8ef39643404a076dc82564e05ff9c7ecd7","verification":{"payload":"tree cccd1a2cc0693e76aa51d0d60e69e0b8e1b6cbd6\nparent df5a44159accd29939aa1c0cf32d67c8d4c47340\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1780502765 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780502765 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1069 - Check AT pre-emptively on fetches to avoid lots of 401''s (#1732)\n\n## [STCOR-1069](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1069)\n\nGiven that we''ve got good expiry information stored, we''ll leverage it\nto reduce the number of initial 401''s.\n\nThis approach reduces the pile of initial 401''s from the `shared` lock\nby circumventing their initial request and putting it off until rotation\nhas happened.\n\nApproach:\nCheck atExpiry before each initial fetch. \nIf the token is expired, set an `atExpired` flag and pass it to\n`rotateAndReplay` as part of the `original` object.\nRotate if `original.atExpired` is true, rather than inspecting the\noriginal response (circumvent the `shouldRotate()` call.)\n\nFXHR: left as-is... there''s nothing async about XHR - if we DO want this\ncheck prior to, then we have to move the expiry from indexDB to\nlocalStorage and check that directly - our wrapping utility in\n`loginServices` was well-intended, but not usable in this case.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIFDtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKCgQAFSj0tLYXTez66jnyB5FVK8i\ne2KSvb8vNTLX05JyiEDcgMjj26jBRQraNpGNSTB5nQQEfkDDvvsVNECVSmuX/nS8\nfYWCH7CRCvSeZBH9J2DiNiJdmlPqnteJxinm7qONSQhbyhhkN7Gs/PU8IoGcvC7y\nqS/Cs8TYZ7NnOS0WTUXH9L5biNmXWsukZwrtP1YkTQUMxnX6nPmqVIK3aUqBTSO0\nhMjAP/lHp8JOeiyokT9KVtEgz3yCPIYmG4L6JTLDC1uaFxtTDOCbXxKQIxcgkWWQ\nvwb8lOR+y2WhlJ8y5wO7Ws9eqkTqobhVmgYJClHmBJ6BwgYeS6gsWu3zS/d2UWyY\nlKqy+yetGre9hOGlszDcJMz7+yxuaZqet2bdtFoGTS8aNOhiponOBVdKqIWINClx\nTd46lAizQuf/XaZat2Sf5w4kEfBufIL4kZFt/NTEoKrY/gxBDqJUMkixY427Zrhh\nSNUeYJ+aYyhHTxpnwJk3zvUBxkgtd0hyePJd8bDi8GLXtRyAPKGBDvSmGDh8pmve\n8riDIGPEJ30ztNw9vyTm856+qisGhYDrevF/Debr6kmjsMe3Y8MWDuXNGrVOmOjg\nzgp2TuOmq6ac8PxaWC86gA3CAUkFPGPahv0OhCLVKS+sB5Hc6kyhkF1Wl9wxCZGx\nnTsYh7NR3ERL7AkfDmyn\n=+YA6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-03T16:06:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id