-org/stripes-core/commit/81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818","sha":"81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818"}],"sha":"3c81d5b19d6e364782ef6316495e215d6303380b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/3c81d5b19d6e364782ef6316495e215d6303380b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T15:51:19Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T15:51:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1061 consolidate logout functionality into <Logout> (#1724)\n\nThis looks messy, but it''s actually a clean up job:\n\n1. If Stripes initialization fails, redirect to `/logout` and allow the\n  `<Logout>` component to take care of cleaning up.\n2. Consolidate all logout functionality into a hook called from\n  `<Logout>`. Don''t invoke logout functions from anywhere else; instead,\n  redirect to `/logout`.\n3. If the Stripes and Keycloak sessions go out of sync (e.g. a user\n  removes their cookies), redirect to Keycloak to sync the sessions, then\n  automatically logout to terminate them.\n\nThe most important thing changing here is the first: the error-handling\nfunction passed from `checkOkapiSession()` to `validateUser()` no longer\ncalls `logout()`; instead it redirects to `/logout`, allowing all\nlogout-related functionality to be consolidate there.\n`checkOkapiSession()` is called via a lifecycle method on `Root.js`.\nStarting the logout process there, and then picking it up a second time\nwhen `<Logout>` renders, was the RCA behind the terrible behavior\ndescribed in this ticket. Thus, this is very much a follow up to PRs\n#1713 and #1720, addressing the unexpected session termination that\ncould occur when opening a new tab, initializing a new instance of\nStripes, which will fail if the `_self` API query fails due to an\nexpired cookie. Those PRs improve handling of the API query; this one\nimproves error handling if something still goes awry.\n\nAdditionally, this PR moves `<Logout>` up in the component hierarchy,\npulling it out from under `<MainContainer>` for authenticated users. The\n`/logout` route needs to be accessible both to authenticated users (so\nthey can use it to logout) and to unauthenticated users (to indicate to\npreviously-authenticated users that the logout process was successful).\nWhen it was inside `<MainContainer>`, untrapped errors during sign-out\ncaused `<Logout>` to display within the main container, a jarring\nglitch. Both problems are now resolved: we trap the errors AND\n`<Logout>` is rendered above/alternatively to `<MainContainer>`,\neliminating the possibility of showing \"you have logged out\" inside the\napplication navigation that clearly demonstrates you are still logged\nin.\n\nRefs STCOR-1061","tree":{"sha":"4699ce9ceb20d3e91b763bf39ac4afa94ab293b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/4699ce9ceb20d3e91b763bf39ac4afa94ab293b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818","verification":{"payload":"tree 4699ce9ceb20d3e91b763bf39ac4afa94ab293b5\nparent dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1778773879 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778773879 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1061 consolidate logout functionality into <Logout> (#1724)\n\nThis looks messy, but it''s actually a clean up job:\n\n1. If Stripes initialization fails, redirect to `/logout` and allow the\n  `<Logout>` component to take care of cleaning up.\n2. Consolidate all logout functionality into a hook called from\n  `<Logout>`. Don''t invoke logout functions from anywhere else; instead,\n  redirect to `/logout`.\n3. If the Stripes and Keycloak sessions go out of sync (e.g. a user\n  removes their cookies), redirect to Keycloak to sync the sessions, then\n  automatically logout to terminate them.\n\nThe most important thing changing here is the first: the error-handling\nfunction passed from `checkOkapiSession()` to `validateUser()` no longer\ncalls `logout()`; instead it redirects to `/logout`, allowing all\nlogout-related functionality to be consolidate there.\n`checkOkapiSession()` is called via a lifecycle method on `Root.js`.\nStarting the logout process there, and then picking it up a second time\nwhen `<Logout>` renders, was the RCA behind the terrible behavior\ndescribed in this ticket. Thus, this is very much a follow up to PRs\n#1713 and #1720, addressing the unexpected session termination that\ncould occur when opening a new tab, initializing a new instance of\nStripes, which will fail if the `_self` API query fails due to an\nexpired cookie. Those PRs improve handling of the API query; this one\nimproves error handling if something still goes awry.\n\nAdditionally, this PR moves `<Logout>` up in the component hierarchy,\npulling it out from under `<MainContainer>` for authenticated users. The\n`/logout` route needs to be accessible both to authenticated users (so\nthey can use it to logout) and to unauthenticated users (to indicate to\npreviously-authenticated users that the logout process was successful).\nWhen it was inside `<MainContainer>`, untrapped errors during sign-out\ncaused `<Logout>` to display within the main container, a jarring\nglitch. Both problems are now resolved: we trap the errors AND\n`<Logout>` is rendered above/alternatively to `<MainContainer>`,\neliminating the possibility of showing \"you have logged out\" inside the\napplication navigation that clearly demonstrates you are still logged\nin.\n\nRefs STCOR-1061","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBe93CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAASoQAE29ItPunr9+hQ5aNwAVOcAA\n6cWjEdggOmAEZYTnrmAsmEqQDa6tUo74XQWlvdGx6GmW0OqsgcyJUbk8zowyXQti\natVKatS8PDU2WGnZ7sxEGAHfv6jXNWgvIuFqn9Aa8vX1rH5UyEDQ9seB8rml+SRK\nxRYxRzZ93LVtd5Q//yxnQ8q+MQqWN3R51DbWLS4HPDcXYYVYmRubJiKoNv+NHE2A\nAyYpi46VR2vtDqKRAewWlhx6OC+FUbDikw2oAiTye+1oxlDWdHIziMV0ezr22mTD\nIdCPgCmRvY4y9faGJ2QBZ2g4pQDRpLGQLaw7zmbq2S0zxW3C/4xqaweassrI9Lsj\nBGJ3VnnXJnP0Rge42tcxO83YFzZ+7ZU8HsllDJ1bvcsTDVbOekTsGUx2rbz+3NsJ\nHI3QNddW7woSPb+llfnJOnSL4HLBRh9aDAsE8KvIEON5xnFSQxMLggR7qq85Ak3n\njAV6ceyJwzWNu92zrDbzhqoMhxlIQntdnTm1w2zXNuBLuB0yeyE6tGbf/CSBSB6K\nU7MUtBq2AH349CooRo2AxtEPu0eV8TFLyh7gTUu50QVTi5O031X6bSYyUbWA3XY6\n4RfuorS9AFxqucCuT4GYiq4wT17Gz7jdEZOc+eGiR6lVubvLdx7otDCMbRlKNB2q\nSq0FEV0TgTnQ0NRCCu3V\n=VLl/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-14T15:51:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDgxYjFiZjk2YmM5OTQ2YjU1YWE5NmJiNDExNTFmZWE3NzcyNzc4MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef","sha":"dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef"}],"sha":"81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/81b1bf96bc9946b55aa96bb41151fea777277818"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T23:04:02Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T23:04:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-717 Address Sonar''s Software Quality > Reliability complaints (#1727)\n\nThere''s nothing of real interest here; most changes are either\ncompletely inconsequential (e.g. replacing `throw Error()` with `throw\nnew Error()` or `string.replace(/.../g)` with\n`string.replaceAll(/.../g)`) or generally obvious (e.g. replacing\n`list.sort()` with `list.sort(comparatorFunction)`), all to appease\nSonar''s \"Software Quality > Reliability\" complaints.\n\nThe only potentially interesting thing is changing `async cDM()` to\n`cDM()` in `Root.js`, but even this is not really interesting, since all\nit does is restore the correct reporting of `cDM`''s signature: it is not\nasync. I wonder what idiot added that. Or, right, the usual idiot in PR\n#1696. 🤦 👊\n\nRefs STCOR-717","tree":{"sha":"3a18316b4e6b5cf7f4b00fe280c600e4b90a3bbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/3a18316b4e6b5cf7f4b00fe280c600e4b90a3bbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a18316b4e6b5cf7f4b00fe280c600e4b90a3bbc\nparent e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1778713442 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778713442 -0400\n\nSTCOR-717 Address Sonar''s Software Quality > Reliability complaints (#1727)\n\nThere''s nothing of real interest here; most changes are either\ncompletely inconsequential (e.g. replacing `throw Error()` with `throw\nnew Error()` or `string.replace(/.../g)` with\n`string.replaceAll(/.../g)`) or generally obvious (e.g. replacing\n`list.sort()` with `list.sort(comparatorFunction)`), all to appease\nSonar''s \"Software Quality > Reliability\" complaints.\n\nThe only potentially interesting thing is changing `async cDM()` to\n`cDM()` in `Root.js`, but even this is not really interesting, since all\nit does is restore the correct reporting of `cDM`''s signature: it is not\nasync. I wonder what idiot added that. Or, right, the usual idiot in PR\n#1696. 🤦 👊\n\nRefs STCOR-717","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBQNiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdmUQAHJ3+tDFskNHvmcAdMoMeGY4\nF3wojcMwfdxvWT5ADnD0yB8njO5FvS4t/WmYXn6MEbg9gx0mrd1KHc8WOG30d7u4\nLWSTyQbitoeo6bLhpVEFKbAA1jPygNLk6IAEZPA9IncWGALmFeBBT/WCKRGvzLKs\niRZo89Z+oxPKkWBnA3DpTTuk7OUI5TY5Zb7d7jOPRfzUUevfqeO29u1LFyxabmMv\nAKp49o2h88iwSUVL+2/4b/809++A6UhoC9NYDOLn4IMv4d83WSGH8hOhsuOYj27h\nqn66TZwrb2BN7zYR2aRKRWZvmT3y7gV3BrXCM2w2d43TFeQwi8Bbw8XTHp+D4Rtr\nRHZAfG9YSR7WH0ZpGDdBF+nVTynSklDKv5Oh+IWds3CodROfsGMOf1Hb3LjtSO4h\nTPdP/jYJcJf3kYBORT7e3J9u2geIl91fVXpAw+Te5U4W8xP4l7X1zY18QVyLB9rs\nFg6JjH+UYN2V7TiHQGeySKtywS6cjofESK3vjJhqqW33nP49MGypezhWMV2r5L8Q\npt82nZD1RDoJLBm9sl3tgU7E2wbSZwsXNsvYkhpwPZ0ud8VwNc8cFXLb1R+9ybXF\nNsupNmcRN8DetmT/vHc1bm90dle8kOtTqr3vrwuKheVzt0gVlPjvy1gktlhh2arc\n4031ay1Ki71HqErX6Y2q\n=lTSk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T23:04:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGRhZDVjMzYwNjU2YTZhM2EzMzE1MDUyOWFlMGM1YzFlN2ZkYzI5ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6","sha":"e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6"}],"sha":"dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/dad5c360656a6a3a33150529ae0c5c1e7fdc29ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T20:47:43Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T20:47:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1002 handle Error input in OIDCLandingError (#1728)\n\n`error` may contain structured JSON from a failed API response, or a\nsimple string, or an Error object if the API request itself fails.\nHandle them all. Previously, Error-object props caused a failure because\nthe object was simply supplied as a child in render, which React does\nnot support.\n\nRefs STCOR-1002","tree":{"sha":"2c0adc07015ab671dc0be61ac99b7aa5ec714a15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/2c0adc07015ab671dc0be61ac99b7aa5ec714a15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c0adc07015ab671dc0be61ac99b7aa5ec714a15\nparent dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1778705263 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778705263 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1002 handle Error input in OIDCLandingError (#1728)\n\n`error` may contain structured JSON from a failed API response, or a\nsimple string, or an Error object if the API request itself fails.\nHandle them all. Previously, Error-object props caused a failure because\nthe object was simply supplied as a child in render, which React does\nnot support.\n\nRefs STCOR-1002","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBONvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9QUQABIMox+RuGWwLg3GW3R3D6Ul\nat6/fWoI+J62KVQMsEV2ON07/5wYqhsJzqL5Rbr63KmjovGQcKhRN3GWBQmh5CGG\n9VihpqgVLwerRlNr6RUf9gVrJ0/yJhvluMA1G8EAQHJd8JJT1dWT6KzCnvhI9OuK\nsr2Y+JFla1pyE65ZI8gPkA0nL500gGBTJQJma789G2xRQcr/2l4xuCdn6I8GCnkw\n7+9oaP5KnOveNKjYL9UWqU+2rQbERW0lXIwgf2k209ejN6yjv0g9az7lnjQjDqln\ng0jLuQMPZGL3paT2kP74HQebDqccVQxGTgaDGhpkN/iJTflfVO/ZXnaB3CTAMbf3\nk+BMoNFMQgAnLhTA/rDpnpMwp1FxT9YUiWsM3DWLJb5BeBQHK5CHsv9pclYEaGNE\nx6HvaFNC/+Kd/1vNwgSNczqbsoqLrSlejRqa2vreK/57Y/wd4TngDDtBiD0/YdvJ\nCkuff7w8radUAbItPQwIcnpQOnyx7UeRlk4d/QxHewLSnqOGswuN2cPtU0515Oc5\n4JAa8UfIZaVf5lecyM7bC0iXxyT6pjtWPKCGv1xGnS9mjYojxTJxPBpqtiRfR4Bk\nOoqrS/gXB9m6Wv59LlBE4u3KgTNE3hGFhI/GhXZLZhUHnNQJ+ZjAG01dTefnN9+I\nQnyZ1vpCuiM0ax1l4YOz\n=t2IP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T20:47:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGU1YWVlNmJjMWNmODU0YzI0NTAzN2NhNGU4NjJiNDA1M2M3ODdlZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4","sha":"dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4"}],"sha":"e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/e5aee6bc1cf854c245037ca4e862b4053c787ef6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T19:10:19Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T19:10:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1064 Add cleanup methods to FFetch, use them in Root''s unmount. (#1726)\n\n## [STCOR-1064](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1064)\nHaving StrictMode turned on will cause the existing RTR implementation\nto hang in the init process since multiple fetch calls courtesy of\n`checkOkapiSession` will be made, and `<Root>` will unmount and remount\nbefore any rotation even occurs. Speculatively, this is causing the\nfirst `exclusive` rotation request to suspend indefinitely, so it never\nunlocks and the UI is frozen.\n\nThe solution - Abort the fetch when `<Root>` unmounts during the\nstrict-mode double-lifecycle. This will kick out the request before\nrotation gets started so once normal functionality resumes the exclusive\nlock can be unclogged.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d1b102e1eb191f66b50f9e12efc051b77ed257a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/4d1b102e1eb191f66b50f9e12efc051b77ed257a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d1b102e1eb191f66b50f9e12efc051b77ed257a\nparent 8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1778699419 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778699419 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1064 Add cleanup methods to FFetch, use them in Root''s unmount. (#1726)\n\n## [STCOR-1064](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1064)\nHaving StrictMode turned on will cause the existing RTR implementation\nto hang in the init process since multiple fetch calls courtesy of\n`checkOkapiSession` will be made, and `<Root>` will unmount and remount\nbefore any rotation even occurs. Speculatively, this is causing the\nfirst `exclusive` rotation request to suspend indefinitely, so it never\nunlocks and the UI is frozen.\n\nThe solution - Abort the fetch when `<Root>` unmounts during the\nstrict-mode double-lifecycle. This will kick out the request before\nrotation gets started so once normal functionality resumes the exclusive\nlock can be unclogged.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBMybCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkokQAFoN3py0+aS8ifle/395D9Q5\nX3Ru/EadVsIN6Ax+A6Ux2jMGMuj9WhyU51oopWOr4peeqSj5dqYpjbvy9HfdXhek\n/SOZ7xfuSsMg29j8xAcBcVUgLPaqMUFDyqE4JW+F7RVxvY13UivFIKCvjdntLMgt\nkvE6syTHx+JV0U83yp0OiXQDelHWMqySpqL2SYYU+8C5in4YF3ToWeyYhu0SA1eK\nQEXNlPs/Xx9T18j1JJ+IdcchISkaqIC8KbTDwy8IqN0f5ymo9sbkD+0lKqgA/VQr\nA5zJR89THOHr6KBMnA3cZMnI1hKfbfrjvqI32mCHsAQIzFUjKDz+yL77d7WsbGiH\nXNPMMFNzLVtnkUIWkdnitBGFjidOQaHk7ckFON9rym3uRI2cebCpcIHR5W/taM6i\nGP9t/MzzsL5P+AYcHGoRL0NUJYagz6FUrZkPrRwHDNGWVEY0Vw/SbAqbHtGYNIcg\nYDMwb31/uQ8Gz9jDPuB80QO5IWMF0I2Wl1iM5IVCsaWYP8iB24Dy/oWMMVp3NKx/\njsI3nayL/aCrsyphwnTSfUTP/+7V6Uw2lgqlrerfI5N9jDuCslG3J5moD8kSSinS\nXg4YGx9vOFhxfZSq6vLjoteRaRM1S9x1dFYroElFVEg+wSCnkAWFEoidOR16km0b\nOSrSAlg+E9E4bz+OXEfu\n=KAEJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T19:10:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGRmYjg2OTc0YTAzZGQyZTAxOTA1MWJkY2RmYTA5NjQ3ZDc1YzdhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347","sha":"8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347"}],"sha":"dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/dfb86974a03dd2e019051bdcdfa09647d75c7af4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T14:47:33Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T14:47:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1055 FXHR functionality refactor (#1723)\n\nThis new breed of rtr calls for a version of `FXHR` that will work -\nideally with similar flow to FFetch''s rotation. The nature of XHR is way\ndifferent from `fetch` - it doesn''t have any real response and relies\nmostly on event handlers to provide any feedback to the caller.\n\nWe tried implementing with `onerror` (PR #1714) - but onerror is for\ntransport-level failures (network problems) not auth problems. It says\n''well, you got a response, so this isn''t that, no handler call for\nyou!''.\n\nThis solution works like this:\n\nAdd an internal event handler for `onreadystatechange` that we run prior\nto any user-provided handlers - so we keep the auth failures from\nbubbling up to the UI. If rotation/retry fails, we''ll pass those errors\nalong.\n\nsince `open` is an initializer function, we store parameters passed\n(withCredentials, etc) in order to attempt a replay of `open` and `send`\nfunctions for after rotation completes.\n\nSince XHR doesn''t have the `response` like `fetch`, we adapt in the\nfollowing ways:\n- implement similar logic to `ffetch`''s `shouldRotate` - checking the\nready state status for `400`''s `401`''s.\n- send no 3rd parameter (the original request, response etc) to\n`rotateAndReplay()` so that necessary token rotation still leverages the\ncentralized locking mechanism.\n\nAn example of XHR usage can be found at\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-data-import/blob/master/src/components/UploadingJobsDisplay/UploadingJobsDisplay.js#L288-L338\n\nRefs [STCOR-1055](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1055)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","tree":{"sha":"1beb47bb4c7d4bbc45df5e29ab3138ececac1008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/1beb47bb4c7d4bbc45df5e29ab3138ececac1008"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347","verification":{"payload":"tree 1beb47bb4c7d4bbc45df5e29ab3138ececac1008\nparent 6b191a109936ef47605e068c3ac539d56592739c\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1778597253 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778597253 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1055 FXHR functionality refactor (#1723)\n\nThis new breed of rtr calls for a version of `FXHR` that will work -\nideally with similar flow to FFetch''s rotation. The nature of XHR is way\ndifferent from `fetch` - it doesn''t have any real response and relies\nmostly on event handlers to provide any feedback to the caller.\n\nWe tried implementing with `onerror` (PR #1714) - but onerror is for\ntransport-level failures (network problems) not auth problems. It says\n''well, you got a response, so this isn''t that, no handler call for\nyou!''.\n\nThis solution works like this:\n\nAdd an internal event handler for `onreadystatechange` that we run prior\nto any user-provided handlers - so we keep the auth failures from\nbubbling up to the UI. If rotation/retry fails, we''ll pass those errors\nalong.\n\nsince `open` is an initializer function, we store parameters passed\n(withCredentials, etc) in order to attempt a replay of `open` and `send`\nfunctions for after rotation completes.\n\nSince XHR doesn''t have the `response` like `fetch`, we adapt in the\nfollowing ways:\n- implement similar logic to `ffetch`''s `shouldRotate` - checking the\nready state status for `400`''s `401`''s.\n- send no 3rd parameter (the original request, response etc) to\n`rotateAndReplay()` so that necessary token rotation still leverages the\ncentralized locking mechanism.\n\nAn example of XHR usage can be found at\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-data-import/blob/master/src/components/UploadingJobsDisplay/UploadingJobsDisplay.js#L288-L338\n\nRefs [STCOR-1055](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1055)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAz2FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8MoQADXs+Kdl0fPGy2Y9OGQZUH/F\nxfuaNasaZ0Dz+U1HzBJ2MAFKBIeIozWJQIBcepwiF4OxIdzYAx4NsYT/DEMjritK\nrwDhzwA6xfM6kBRZaOKIj3rb2THiz7rC/0+WyErnOsxkN8gOnMUESai18L5uJznd\n/rvB+c22EEnrMO0XaM32q8OLiYEkyfQomIdSROSWbll0QsPVvl3CDvI0MFCXlorg\nO/vTemo0/7DAmDib1FWm9Ro5Fl1G98S7eYHCn9LGC0BZ8MM4OtWrwHqT2kFJ0XEI\nrPS5bNBbWpC7jS3aG7Z4yZ0GOy25qMOfAJJMJBoitF/rs9VP6ei5u/O7RH6KdRhs\nc7c699MHTYubuKO6AwyDufYiJxFdj+nxxU3Sa1jGVnAJzLShdGrUCOxm0f6DvAmG\nFiXU0CiHWdkW/PJgr0MHPVQUsC/miXPkh4KvG+SCZ/KizY/m9sinrGMgSsNaUNjU\nYvfsay0/rFvDZrdo7k/b2/dWRKAzcSzOZInDJ6x5JTPyNuvzlSmcqNDmDcmG2kvM\nWwvtIFsl2sflQSEs5ojB83IB6mf959GcbgQTdQsyI+MaBeoajl/nLxrYjXbPCUkI\nq3DWENSGLVs4YBrBAFPfeg5VKXxDHB9cVwIbojvvrsH4Xmtn5sJ7Ht6Gznt4fKAH\n/opXx0UNg91RlVcZNeWd\n=tojd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T14:49:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDhjZWNmMzBhNjU2MmMzZGIwMjk4NDYxYTEyYzRkMDI3OGMwOTgzNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/6b191a109936ef47605e068c3ac539d56592739c","sha":"6b191a109936ef47605e068c3ac539d56592739c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/6b191a109936ef47605e068c3ac539d56592739c"}],"sha":"8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/8cecf30a6562c3db0298461a12c4d0278c098347"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":1