605e068c3ac539d56592739c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/6b191a109936ef47605e068c3ac539d56592739c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/e78fd29ac2b0f5357536ffaf322ea709dd8b1b7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-04T00:02:08Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-04T00:02:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1060 - clone response again prior to attempting a request before rotation. (#1718)\n\nThis is a follow-up to PR stripes-core/pull/1710, addressing an issue\nthat slipped through the cracks there: when a request is a literal\nRequest object, it can only be consumed once, but the rotate-and-replay\nprocess will replay a request twice (once to test the short-circuit in\ncase rotation already completed elsewhere, and second time after\nrotation if the short-circuit failed).\n\nThis PR addresses the problem by always cloning Request objects inside\nreplayRequest(). This means requests that require rotation will be\ncloned an extra time since the second time they are replayed is the\nfinal time they are replayed, but this feels like an acceptable price to\npay for keeping the logic simple.\n\nRefs STCOR-1060\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ed3eeca3069cfcbcf7b566af0f16e12eb687c2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/8ed3eeca3069cfcbcf7b566af0f16e12eb687c2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/e78fd29ac2b0f5357536ffaf322ea709dd8b1b7d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ed3eeca3069cfcbcf7b566af0f16e12eb687c2f\nparent d0d2926281ec64acc64673e1d8f178e7fec3472a\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1777852928 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777852928 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1060 - clone response again prior to attempting a request before rotation. (#1718)\n\nThis is a follow-up to PR stripes-core/pull/1710, addressing an issue\nthat slipped through the cracks there: when a request is a literal\nRequest object, it can only be consumed once, but the rotate-and-replay\nprocess will replay a request twice (once to test the short-circuit in\ncase rotation already completed elsewhere, and second time after\nrotation if the short-circuit failed).\n\nThis PR addresses the problem by always cloning Request objects inside\nreplayRequest(). This means requests that require rotation will be\ncloned an extra time since the second time they are replayed is the\nfinal time they are replayed, but this feels like an acceptable price to\npay for keeping the logic simple.\n\nRefs STCOR-1060\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9+IACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyc8QAKwUu6kw2qehvgeMfrBG3Mlz\nCn9e8hEwtbeNzzRAyPxxpkaTiVFF/9osczg3wHaW/mIXAYKVqD91g1wNr38/lhLZ\nwX6eu/YzMINrNIkCiwWdI4sIjVHrss9bgbX5Ft9L2nLGkLgHP5gmTxpVlPLG6E2A\nZMaphfvrMiWMcEEA1oYU2iW4Q4yz5IjSf4