hubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/33ba03fe7c4c15652d742809b041623231259972/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T20:30:20Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T20:30:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1048 correctly handle unreliable AT metadata during RTR (#1710)\n\n## Summary \n\nIf the AT cookie and its corresponding expiration data in the session\nobject in local storage get out of sync (e.g. somebody deletes cookies),\nStripes will be in an inconsistent state: its AT is missing, but its\nsession data indicates that a valid AT is present. This PR addresses\nthat inconsistency, allowing RTR to recover and proceed with rotation.\n\n## Approach\n\nFavor simplicity over cleverness: we know the token''s metadata can be\nunreliable, so we don''t rely on it. If a cookie was deleted prior to\nexpiration but metadata in storage is never updated, there''s nothing we\ncan do to detect that. In that situation, the previous algorithm worked\nlike this: all requests through the queue would check storage, find it\nvalid, replay, and return the response without inspecting for success,\nallowing 401s to bubble to their origin (whoops). This PR simplifies and\ncorrects the logic: all requests through the queue attempt replay and\nall responses are inspected. The first one will fail, rotate, and\nreplay. Subsequent requests replay and (assuming they are successful)\nshort-circuit.\n\nThis means the first request in the queue pays a performance penalty (an\nextra failed replay attempt) but every other request in the queue goes\nthrough more efficiently (no async storage check). It also simplifies\nthe logic because we don''t spend any effort trying to figure out \"Do we\nthink this request is likely to succeed because we have an unverifiable\nbelief that our token is valid?\" We just make requests and deal with the\nconsequences.\n\nThis PR also addresses a wart with the earlier implementation regarding\nthe handling of non-ok responses that entered the rotation queue but\nwere determined not to have failed due to a missing AT (e.g. a 404, 403,\netc). Now, if rotation is determined to be unnecessary,\n`rotateAndReplay()` returns the response instead of throwing it. Not\nrotating is not an exceptional condition, it''s just ... not rotating.\nBack in `FFetch`, we would check for this and return the response from\nthe `catch` clause. By not throwing this non-error, `FFetch` can be\nsimplified too, omitting the now-unnecessary `catch` that would do\nnothing except rethrowing.\n\nRefs STCOR-1048","tree":{"sha":"cb35b836faf3dad91d3b0d64cbd84ff00b1e5f52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/cb35b836faf3dad91d3b0d64cbd84ff00b1e5f52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/33ba03fe7c4c15652d742809b041623231259972","verification":{"payload":"tree cb35b836faf3dad91d3b0d64cbd84ff00b1e5f52\nparent 571e0c9c0ec0c1640284826a58f2982d31d2f3bd\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1777494620 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777494620 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1048 correctly handle unreliable AT metadata during RTR (#1710)\n\n## Summary \n\nIf the AT cookie and its corresponding expiration data in the session\nobject in local storage get out of sync (e.g. somebody deletes cookies),\nStripes will be in an inconsistent state: its AT is missing, but its\nsession data indicates that a valid AT is present. This PR addresses\nthat inconsistency, allowing RTR to recover and proceed with rotation.\n\n## Approach\n\nFavor simplicity over cleverness: we know the token''s metadata can be\nunreliable, so we don''t rely on it. If a cookie was deleted prior to\nexpiration but metadata in storage is never updated, there''s nothing we\ncan do to detect that. In that situation, the previous algorithm worked\nlike this: all requests through the queue would check storage, find it\nvalid, replay, and return the response without inspecting for success,\nallowing 401s to bubble to their origin (whoops). This PR simplifies and\ncorrects the logic: all requests through the queue attempt replay and\nall responses are inspected. The first one will fail, rotate, and\nreplay. Subsequent requests replay and (assuming they are successful)\nshort-circuit.\n\nThis means the first request in the queue pays a performance penalty (an\nextra failed replay attempt) but every other request in the queue goes\nthrough more efficiently (no async storage check). It also simplifies\nthe logic because we don''t spend any effort trying to figure out \"Do we\nthink this request is likely to succeed because we have an unverifiable\nbelief that our token is valid?\" We just make requests and deal with the\nconsequences.\n\nThis PR also addresses a wart with the earlier implementation regarding\nthe handling of non-ok responses that entered the rotation queue but\nwere determined not to have failed due to a missing AT (e.g. a 404, 403,\netc). Now, if rotation is determined to be unnecessary,\n`rotateAndReplay()` returns the response instead of throwing it. Not\nrotating is not an exceptional condition, it''s just ... not rotating.\nBack in `FFetch`, we would check for this and return the response from\nthe `catch` clause. By not throwing this non-error, `FFetch` can be\nsimplified too, omitting the now-unnecessary `catch` that would do\nnothing except rethrowing.\n\nRefs STCOR-1048","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8mpcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALHQQAChjhsLTVQGsy0zmEhlEk8ng\n68CqEr9ZPQVIA2ypLwA/hWgiDNjT6JaVw60m5WmOXTIRxp+v/2BRDnfypSH/43vg\nx74mr4reEl29MefoKRAfOeqpyYZRB/QexWkRhays/5Ae5PMpIickZl+vpgxqlDP+\nVYE0o1ydToMSO3cD67d0/BW6KA1Tkwug68+Q4EgutoY+864ykKY0LlaZUH/q7wa4\n+4KuacjRWGUMdeSW1ncpfmTWnaXMb5a14P09gAN/NyR1GcKEjBF+sYCPMfnECCRO\ne8B1afuw1oU1Pa7tx5qjSWvB9m1I9ib6AnQzi1rRMbo2aYJFpqi4aJWE10+4bpN9\n43mPBYrBFtcHno2yjcGybOUWJ1i3nGSUhhDDnbd42TwbYnb+/MLWsPZYUgq90wil\n2yYyOS06Aw8RxMxLVFVtDgPoWXXFUr3cW/oU4veTww09vdXME2qZ8E2kzvm4QRf+\ntqpPy476HsYlq4vuYU9ekK1iMrUaPLpUOXywWhFAmspQCOJ7FNJNzzVWj+B9kPBW\nXGj83blHOCPqr74ocMyseOoJWsZDmorLj6zvHyUSa68Fr/ywcP6eAJ1iwQEZ+Pxi\nqSlUHlQsrOVT8lCwD0E8hHPGudY+Yw2YkOjhgmAtvPGYHcRZ+xydjGKgjR5+12wK\n3wj8qlN56L2Nllg2DhJA\n=PfRN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-29T20:30:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"star