gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/cba8744ab9e647b7df56fc372ab9aa3ecc67056e","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGNiYTg3NDRhYjllNjQ3YjdkZjU2ZmMzNzJhYjlhYTNlY2M2NzA1NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa","sha":"a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa"}],"sha":"cba8744ab9e647b7df56fc372ab9aa3ecc67056e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/cba8744ab9e647b7df56fc372ab9aa3ecc67056e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-13T18:28:10Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-13T18:28:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STRIPES-901 - validate for conflicting peer dependencies. (#1705)\n\n## [STRIPES-901](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STRIPES-901)\n\nCurrently, we strip out shared singleton dependencies from ui-module\nbuilds with the [`import: false` configuration in\n`stripes-webpack`](https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-webpack/blob/main/module-federation-config.js#L53)\nso that there''s no chance they''ll be loaded in the bundle.\nThey''re all mapped (forced) to use the host app''s loaded dependency, so\nthey don''t make the request for a conflicting version (as they would if\n`import: false` were not used. Without that request, Module-federation''s\nbuilt-in dependency check/warn won''t fire - and so we have to implement\nour own via this very PR!\n\nDespite being missing from the bundled code, the version that the\nui-module was built with is maintained within its generated\n`mf-manifest.json` file. The code here loads that file for each remote,\ninspects the JSON and checks for compatibility on the versions of shared\ndependencies. If an incompatibility is detected, a warning is emitted in\nthe console.\n\nThis check does *not block the rest of the modules from loading, nor\ndoes a module failing the check.\n \nThis PR does include the addition of the `semver` library to\n`stripes-core`.\n \nThe console warning:\n<img width=\"802\" height=\"64\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a20fc323-19bd-4544-8318-f1d25dd4a64a\"\n/>\n\nExample `mf-manifest.json` from compatible `react` dep:\n```\n  \"shared\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"folio_users:react\",\n      \"name\": \"react\",\n      \"version\": \"18.3.1\", // version ui-module is built with...\n      \"singleton\": true,\n      \"requiredVersion\": \"~18.3\",  // @folio/stripes-core''s version...\n      \"assets\": {\n        \"js\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        },\n        \"css\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        }\n      },\n      \"fallback\": \"\"\n    },\n```\n\nOffending app `mf-manifest.json`:\n```\n  \"shared\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"folio_minimal_r_19:react\",\n      \"name\": \"react\",\n      \"version\": \"19.2.4\",  // version ui-module is built with...\n      \"singleton\": true,\n      \"requiredVersion\": \"~18.3\",  // @folio/stripes-core''s version...\n      \"assets\": {\n        \"js\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        },\n        \"css\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        }\n      },\n      \"fallback\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n```","tree":{"sha":"db2998ea76f3c0e9a8e54966f2ff594af8cb89de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/db2998ea76f3c0e9a8e54966f2ff594af8cb89de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa","verification":{"payload":"tree db2998ea76f3c0e9a8e54966f2ff594af8cb89de\nparent bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1776104890 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776104890 -0500\n\nSTRIPES-901 - validate for conflicting peer dependencies. (#1705)\n\n## [STRIPES-901](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STRIPES-901)\n\nCurrently, we strip out shared singleton dependencies from ui-module\nbuilds with the [`import: false` configuration in\n`stripes-webpack`](https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-webpack/blob/main/module-federation-config.js#L53)\nso that there''s no chance they''ll be loaded in the bundle.\nThey''re all mapped (forced) to use the host app''s loaded dependency, so\nthey don''t make the request for a conflicting version (as they would if\n`import: false` were not used. Without that request, Module-federation''s\nbuilt-in dependency check/warn won''t fire - and so we have to implement\nour own via this very PR!\n\nDespite being missing from the bundled code, the version that the\nui-module was built with is maintained within its generated\n`mf-manifest.json` file. The code here loads that file for each remote,\ninspects the JSON and checks for compatibility on the versions of shared\ndependencies. If an incompatibility is detected, a warning is emitted in\nthe console.\n\nThis check does *not block the rest of the modules from loading, nor\ndoes a module failing the check.\n \nThis PR does include the addition of the `semver` library to\n`stripes-core`.\n \nThe console warning:\n<img width=\"802\" height=\"64\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a20fc323-19bd-4544-8318-f1d25dd4a64a\"\n/>\n\nExample `mf-manifest.json` from compatible `react` dep:\n```\n  \"shared\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"folio_users:react\",\n      \"name\": \"react\",\n      \"version\": \"18.3.1\", // version ui-module is built with...\n      \"singleton\": true,\n      \"requiredVersion\": \"~18.3\",  // @folio/stripes-core''s version...\n      \"assets\": {\n        \"js\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        },\n        \"css\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        }\n      },\n      \"fallback\": \"\"\n    },\n```\n\nOffending app `mf-manifest.json`:\n```\n  \"shared\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"folio_minimal_r_19:react\",\n      \"name\": \"react\",\n      \"version\": \"19.2.4\",  // version ui-module is built with...\n      \"singleton\": true,\n      \"requiredVersion\": \"~18.3\",  // @folio/stripes-core''s version...\n      \"assets\": {\n        \"js\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        },\n        \"css\": {\n          \"async\": [],\n          \"sync\": []\n        }\n      },\n      \"fallback\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n```","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3TW6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9s4QAHBTt7F7NMcaV4ku2zzWgpEn\nAuAOEnbhujFiL0XZokeCqXGAxH3XSNxSkY8rVPO3rqeX3SG1jP9KKAuOm9SBQIND\nIu2Eg233Ebwd6rmawzX1AvotsvqSDNrulKqy9+aZD8WQ4aS4arr8qemUhJddc61P\n6t7y8pwSEz96xjD+bGuwoYzdcF7v0nKD8iOwXkn77Pfm6c6f6d+dC9D9BPsT3ndq\nFQXdq++FOMcV4YDgY6ID4oIolnRWQm0GoRyh1JAinoZ9aPjbSM1icnK6wLd+7T6X\nmSb1qdN7YyoqbBK30R8A7Rj3Rkx9O+6ue+rXe0iB+nTPzrrBld+/J38keiPx0CEy\nzXtRkDhj8Oij/weU7rcS2dz/FeTjMtTABZZZSDLv8Cb8F0UbiiArUItqL/w5EKrB\n2B5nNdhh1WP9pA7FCxbz4Y8FopDWx7j8XznlcbYt7niy52bzL/aENwNvO1PDqzmi\n0LqUVmMonKqhla8/h+scc5J8eAKn4WcS/FLqHXwzuFzzjKJcsZTIzh1jfbo54zVU\nxqp+ScsNcKDT3xyC7YNzT6Tlc9M2/I7I+FNsaOThjLMENKvdaAZ+7Fe/K0q293Yx\nzwSCwzvAJke6zCQtXmea8UOZjIvRWtzZeWPOOnNt+BzPg9NFBjHDs1J+P6Hs8iAv\nnih8QWubbUpG9qgTXNSz\n=YlOz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-13T18:28:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGE5NThhMmFjZDllYWVjMGIwNGIyMGIxMDBkNTY3ODM2M2ZlNmQ3YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068","sha":"bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068"}],"sha":"a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/a958a2acd9eaec0b04b20b100d5678363fe6d7aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-31T19:24:36Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-31T19:24:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1040: switch to non-webpack mod-fed libraries. (#1701)\n\nThis PR is similar to #1694 w/o the history overhead from mod-fed POC.\n\n## [STCOR-1040](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1040)\n###  This PR:\n- adopts non-webpack `@module-federation/runtime` library.\n- replaces our own `loadRemote` function.\n\n ### How it works\n`EntitlementLoader` logic registers the remote modules with the host\n`ModuleFederation` instance.\nIt then carries forward, loading translations and icons for each remote,\nthen loads the remote using the `@module-federation/runtime` library''s\n`loadRemote` method.","tree":{"sha":"7feaa9b06cea7a2df1cb3f000ccee48c21ed9819","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/7feaa9b06cea7a2df1cb3f000ccee48c21ed9819"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068","verification":{"payload":"tree 7feaa9b06cea7a2df1cb3f000ccee48c21ed9819\nparent d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1774985076 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774985076 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1040: switch to non-webpack mod-fed libraries. (#1701)\n\nThis PR is similar to #1694 w/o the history overhead from mod-fed POC.\n\n## [STCOR-1040](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1040)\n###  This PR:\n- adopts non-webpack `@module-federation/runtime` library.\n- replaces our own `loadRemote` function.\n\n ### How it works\n`EntitlementLoader` logic registers the remote modules with the host\n`ModuleFederation` instance.\nIt then carries forward, loading translations and icons for each remote,\nthen loads the remote using the `@module-federation/runtime` library''s\n`loadRemote` method.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpzB90CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7nUQAJ52819j4Dob/Uj/EEwMQ1aV\nhLjepGCSPR7EL83Fbke7+A+/X4l5QkbVA9IRaXlbXws6l1lduC4WrSanvbO8FoO+\nVf5YKlu86pSBuejTii2390FWHB+/fsoDCjs88WqkN87BLftaN2mnL1zsrmZiMpp5\nNJjdrd+dqfgdkR1jGvePb8xyGUc4AzyeaLz7O85SExHB542yRu+mdZUGAQFSAA7a\n0jVxCiUYqTa+cx7oKl/WUf1VfJWq3XDFa7uXEHXN/LGLT/9r2m+2Q7TqrlMsJhYX\nkZSzWxo4T+bCxq+CGBVjSVjBEUJDo2FqVm35F6Zb2DyKgxggbGN7MsVJNlpUOWg2\nXapZhN0gKw//yVd+CHK/U1YWlwvTPCoH9LIrLVDfkqpp2Yg1ZcLX5c6rb2ZGcAyK\nyTmmxyXVbkX4DUWIMkfLXs6h3GknrEOuAq40AnbQOSXGiduYSIefGeRTvHMT8aHT\nrEtIh+gSgHhAyIi2ctB5WaiFZMI1Fe50hsRJ1uAOYBBpfWYE9h5dAFp9k1Dny+CN\nPExNHcpPYWMls9UwzBTCph1nQayHJK7uMxOvZ3g8UpZXoIQoBrCA7G+rVnY8F/kf\n2SL8DNKuvx0O9yaZXVXcIwfBa2OM6cNTnfHT3PFd4bJdutJhB1/xL2hdLX91grov\nOvZKtjOyaVZqfgmPQUxb\n=8kfl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-31T19:24:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKGJiMWQ3YjNhNGUwYjM5NWJhNWYwNTQwNTA5NDJmYmI2NTg5NGUwNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc","sha":"d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc"}],"sha":"bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/bb1d7b3a4e0b395ba5f054050942fbb65894e068"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T10:40:43Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T10:40:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1043 load translations only once (#1703)\n\nDo not call `await loadTranslations()` if we have, ya know, _already\ncalled `await loadTranslations()`_. The double-call is a long-standing\nbug, but we didn''t notice it earlier because of the additional bug of\nnot consistently `await`ing our promises. We added many of those missing\n`await` calls in PR #1696, and discovered this lurking in the shadows.\n\nWhen a session is active, the `Root::cDM()` call to\n`checkOkapiSession()` would end up calling it indirectly, and then\ncalling it again directly immediately after. Now that we await the call\nin `checkOkapiSession()`, we can check whether the `cDM()` call is\nnecessary instead of always blindly calling it.\n\nh/t @Dmytro-Melnyshyn for identifying this problem and handing me the\nsolution on a silver platter.\n\nRefs STCOR-1043","tree":{"sha":"84259549b5127d4e8f353c36bad2ab600222ea8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/84259549b5127d4e8f353c36bad2ab600222ea8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc","verification":{"payload":"tree 84259549b5127d4e8f353c36bad2ab600222ea8a\nparent 5da642e464169260aed0e37a341a82eec82867a2\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1773657643 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773657643 -0400\n\nSTCOR-1043 load translations only once (#1703)\n\nDo not call `await loadTranslations()` if we have, ya know, _already\ncalled `await loadTranslations()`_. The double-call is a long-standing\nbug, but we didn''t notice it earlier because of the additional bug of\nnot consistently `await`ing our promises. We added many of those missing\n`await` calls in PR #1696, and discovered this lurking in the shadows.\n\nWhen a session is active, the `Root::cDM()` call to\n`checkOkapiSession()` would end up calling it indirectly, and then\ncalling it again directly immediately after. Now that we await the call\nin `checkOkapiSession()`, we can check whether the `cDM()` call is\nnecessary instead of always blindly calling it.\n\nh/t @Dmytro-Melnyshyn for identifying this problem and handing me the\nsolution on a silver platter.\n\nRefs STCOR-1043","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt94rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWv4QAGVZhF3AHi1dbSWhT4L3seeX\nQX8MfxUFF4SA/e0GLBHljmg5See0AYpi9GeUz0yDa9nMnKQRrhEWnQD+Hffuz3P7\nNkQGhuJRYx/N5OT+uhHqJLUQMA0jhrazGMLfofpLXRfGc5m7Gxp7Ip9nyQT87435\nYMbTHyiUln+ouOcBuM3JERAxvZRQiD03gqbI0Ul0vOfh1dpk9vefVZBgSj01koe/\nDMwW4NmUsjDVJ+xyvOErFzyqRL