3bcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/d8e8348cd07c77b94af9d5f7a825fe434e583bcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28395235?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ryandberger","id":28395235,"login":"ryandberger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4Mzk1MjM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryandberger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/5da642e464169260aed0e37a341a82eec82867a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T01:09:24Z","email":"rberger@ebsco.com","name":"Ryan Berger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T01:09:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[STCOR-1039] Read Stripes Config data from Stripes Hub if available (#1700)\n\n- Fulfills\n[STCOR-1039](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1039).\n- Read Stripes Config and Branding data from `localStorage` provided by\nStripes Hub. If available, this becomes the source of truth for\nconfiguration. If not available, then default to `stripes.config.js` and\ncarry on.\n- Stripes Hub for writing data to `localStorage` for stripes-core to\nconsume is completed here:\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/stripes-hub/pull/12.\n- Renamed key from `stripes-hub` `hostLocation` to be `hostUrl`, since\nthe value is a URL. Partnering PR is here:\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/stripes-hub/pull/17","tree":{"sha":"1dd73905418412bc2e8b29770ed672197604ff52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/1dd73905418412bc2e8b29770ed672197604ff52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/5da642e464169260aed0e37a341a82eec82867a2","verification":{"payload":"tree 1dd73905418412bc2e8b29770ed672197604ff52\nparent 5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c\nauthor Ryan Berger <rberger@ebsco.com> 1773623364 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773623364 -0400\n\n[STCOR-1039] Read Stripes Config data from Stripes Hub if available (#1700)\n\n- Fulfills\n[STCOR-1039](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1039).\n- Read Stripes Config and Branding data from `localStorage` provided by\nStripes Hub. If available, this becomes the source of truth for\nconfiguration. If not available, then default to `stripes.config.js` and\ncarry on.\n- Stripes Hub for writing data to `localStorage` for stripes-core to\nconsume is completed here:\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/stripes-hub/pull/12.\n- Renamed key from `stripes-hub` `hostLocation` to be `hostUrl`, since\nthe value is a URL. Partnering PR is here:\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/stripes-hub/pull/17","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt1hECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA958QAJ4+x1tPKGR9+Knlyd9HSe13\n41ZtQ/bq/byvllJ48Jd1jANoDOAmtthRtNTJZvF2EGHytZyChg2GGGgrYZsph0hc\nnE2uuUPbu9C1GAXUib70+tzEhHY7O215VZMvGZjsdNCVUyQk2s112xcGKr16xKHE\n3WMuc/rjlEwcQqtyXIrjXTMoroMN812G6n/cFiHPf0rbikLrG9r96BBm40BC0fyu\n3O/T2pTe4qkz+aLO6LjdDfZPW2zMIByDMUdnaRfHYm2SdR+UiRJ5uukQ5f/1E3F+\nBy9VZ6P8YkTXPXa7xMgNAsena3SP9d6Hj2TH/kzVF/2o2a8QMIwwi/EtW+EzYkg9\nB3w5ceBRat6fS0BVU/TaN+Dx9MhRr0WcrQYaFeXT1gt/7W5kpPX9o/l0b4SFWAv9\nY3jyClL4gGWLyRt0Is9KH7JPvz6RugEVD1mj0mLxUfTv53gTgvD7EueYbtiFivQh\n5EvQ29X3sFPJ+rjC8yTJNdW1GY12HbI+wfXK3bRHOKLX3usJhcbk2rmwRCYnOk6A\n0rYtSgAB/7hKxtUi1a4nnzSihGOWQ8RLampLSk7tRY/FVFEQ4y8JA11N3567aBs4\nlofEtp5L5Vwxo7s/NjhPgq2ZbBY3yX208W3Ifta0NJcFPC6AWymOw7T6LgN6yRKg\nTvXpwTi6C8XLaYIxKijA\n=1D97\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-16T01:09:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/5da642e464169260aed0e37a341a82eec82867a2","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDVkYTY0MmU0NjQxNjkyNjBhZWQwZTM3YTM0MWE4MmVlYzgyODY3YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c","sha":"5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c"}],"sha":"5da642e464169260aed0e37a341a82eec82867a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/5da642e464169260aed0e37a341a82eec82867a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T22:06:24Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T22:06:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1042 handle non-string fetches in RTR (#1702)\n\n`fetch()` accepts either a string or a Request object as its first\nargument. A Request object, like a Response, can only be consumed once.\nThe previous implementation did not account for this. Here, the\narguments are inspected and if a Request is present it is cloned before\nthe original request fires, allowing the clone to be passed to\n`rotateAndReplay()` if rotation is necessary.\n\nI could not come up with a good way to test this. A Request body is\nthenable, but by mocking `fetch()` we don''t end up consuming the\nRequest. I can stick an assertion inside `rotateAndReplay()` that\n`error.resource.bodyUsed` is `false`, but even the previous\nimplementation would pass that test. I am open to suggestions on how to\ntest this, or a better (i.e. more testable) implementation.\n\nRefs STCOR-1042, STCOR-1012","tree":{"sha":"f7696094bb5b209f217db5ce285b5f3ef273a8c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/f7696094bb5b209f217db5ce285b5f3ef273a8c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c","verification":{"payload":"tree f7696094bb5b209f217db5ce285b5f3ef273a8c3\nparent 0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1772834784 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772834784 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1042 handle non-string fetches in RTR (#1702)\n\n`fetch()` accepts either a string or a Request object as its first\nargument. A Request object, like a Response, can only be consumed once.\nThe previous implementation did not account for this. Here, the\narguments are inspected and if a Request is present it is cloned before\nthe original request fires, allowing the clone to be passed to\n`rotateAndReplay()` if rotation is necessary.\n\nI could not come up with a good way to test this. A Request body is\nthenable, but by mocking `fetch()` we don''t end up consuming the\nRequest. I can stick an assertion inside `rotateAndReplay()` that\n`error.resource.bodyUsed` is `false`, but even the previous\nimplementation would pass that test. I am open to suggestions on how to\ntest this, or a better (i.e. more testable) implementation.\n\nRefs STCOR-1042, STCOR-1012","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpq0/gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3bcQAKlYcrIkMLAl7dxRpdC4lmrR\nU0ds91UzucQNu9vvlJs+2knciacON4CwOS77ZkKk7iJq/HJjKNBdt5fk2PQWbmaf\ngo+1T99rro6XuAsjRCgtV06GjMUM9mMt4WMT6lZ5qtx79qI13osgy72AexcmOUYn\nSGO+3BENmifzzSzJg7/8dswftsHvskI/3vSbm2SuTkghiDssxnhGKb+ezYNYRnMu\naCtuj0TQYQ3ATkXoXbnxxGZjLVGGVf6UqLRJWKV5vNPYAhT4mNV83TfLhcIjNN9k\nAgFJqVW5GAW1/zAyRlhy9hViQwvjC+P2wy7WiO60+Gwtn1iSEini5rcfk+kXjLlJ\nlv/JSU5ZIngba/qc2adHeYSJJvi5D+Sen5t0D/b2KH+ZolKoq6T/1eY8dRFRQ7/6\nYq6rKqc98S9JumaOboDSW+2sNvGHEyLcDI+Wxtz9YvM+f1bPOJTwKFqwhaRna8Y5\ngbp2QHjRzdGqS5H8C10Kyz3iN2Ldfufns6eMvf4075WvQ4Xu1To5r19qnrrlrjp+\nuW34riXNFdA3kb1+BMCEwj65fwesclCGYhKeEH/H3EN75y2BQ3CH9N+6WhIkRTaD\nHIACFkxiDC6X5mfpN65uV5QMQ9NmIN9A4wii44ikyBAqnTtnnC/SWht3cOhb2pwC\n8apGaMM4AK7r6Axlmzlr\n=t1Hz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-06T22:06:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDU0NDllMzliOTExOTc2NDA2MjdjOGZhZjgyZmZlMDBhZTA3ODEwNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287","sha":"0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287"}],"sha":"5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/5449e39b91197640627c8faf82ffe00ae078105c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-03T21:04:43Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-03T21:04:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1012 💉 botox for the botched RTR implementation (#1696)\n\nRTR, boy oh boy, where to start? \n* #1340? Nah, that never even got off the ground.\n* #1346? Oh hell no! 🧄 ✝️ Do you not remember that hellfire? Mothers\ncried. Children screamed. One of my chickens actually died. 🪦 We killed\noff this implementation in #1371.\n* That brings us to #1376 (but also #1417, and #1423, and #1547, and\ndon''t forgot #1579, #1642, #1643, #1647, and #1688).\n\nThe implementations thus far all worked by setting a timer that pinged\nshortly before the AT expired, executing a callback that paused API\nrequests while executing the rotation request. Of course, it was never\nthat simple; starting rotation after authenticating was subtly different\nthan starting rotation for an existing session because the\nlogin-response includes token-expiration data but the `/bl-users/_self`\ndoesn''t. All those extra tweaks made the code even messier, and while\nthey each made the UX a little better, none of them made it actually\nmake it _good_. And then STCOR-1012 showed up, telling us things were\nnot only not good; they were, in fact, pretty bad. It was a mess. It was\njust a mess. 💩\n\nAnd that brings us here, to the fourth full-blown rewrite of RTR.\nHopefully, the logic here is simpler, better isolated, and easier to\nreason about. At the highest level, things are still the same: we''re\nreplacing native-fetch with FFetch, which transparently handles\nrotation. The FFetch algorithm now works like this:\n* get a shared lock, preventing API requests from firing while rotation\n  is in progress\n  * make the API request\n  * release the lock\n* if the response isn''t `ok`, call `rotateAndReplay()` to rotate the\n  tokens and replay the original request\n* return the response\n\n`rotateAndReplay` works like this:\n* inspect the original response. if it doesn''t look like an\n  authentication failure, reject with the original response, allowing it\nto bubble back to the code that made the original request\n* get an exclusive lock, preventing any API requests from firing while\n  rotation is in progress\n* request token-expiration data from storage; if it appears valid,\n  replay the original request and return its response\n  * make the rotation request\n  * callback to store the updated token-expiration data\n  * replay the original request\n  * release the lock\n\nChecking, while inside the lock, whether the tokens have already been\nrotated is a crucial step that handles the situation of many requests\nfiring simultaneously after the tokens have expired. The Web Locks API\nelects one request, allowing rotation, storage, and replay to proceed\nfor that request only while all others wait for the lock''s promise to\nresolve. After that first request releases its lock, the next request in\nthe queue proceeds through `rotateAndReplay()`, but this time it will\nreturn early since the token-expiration data in storage will be valid.\nNote: this means requests that are queued together proceed\nsingle-threaded through the lock. This sounds worse than it is since\n`rotateAndReplay()` short-circuits after the first request, jumping\nimmediately to \"replay\" since valid tokens are now available.\n\nBut wait! There''s more! The original implementation stored the\nend-of-session timer-IDs in redux. It''s important to keep track of those\nIDs so they can be cleared if the user logs out early or session\nexpiration is configured as a window that slides on rotation, as\nnon-keycloak sessions are. Anybody remember UICHKOUT-869?\nUsing redux was problematic for two reasons:\n1. Mind-bogglingly, clearing the old timer was buried inside the redux\n  action, which, just, why??? 🤯 Dude, have you never heard of\n  single-responsibility? Redux actions should be responsible for redux and\n  only redux.\n2. Bigly-mind-bogglingly, keeping timer data on the okapi slice of redux\n  meant that Root re-rendered every time tokens rotated, which was a real\n  head-scratcher (STCOR-1008 et al), until @vashjs made things plain to us in\n  UITEN-333 🙇. Like I said, it was a mess. 💩 💩\n\nThe self-contained, self-clearing timer ResetTimer (maybe I should''ve\ncalled it SelfClearingTimer? 🤔) resolves both: redux actions are once\nagain pure, and Root no longer re-renders with each rotation.\n\nRefs STCOR-1012, UITEN-333, STCOR-1025, STCOR-999\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"24203b4597502e92f4be6cac09571d69aea5f588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/24203b4597502e92f4be6cac09571d69aea5f588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287","verification":{"payload":"tree 24203b4597502e92f4be6cac09571d69aea5f588\nparent 774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1772571883 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772571883 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1012 💉 botox for the botched RTR implementation (#1696)\n\nRTR, boy oh boy, where to start? \n* #1340? Nah, that never even got off the ground.\n* #1346? Oh hell no! 🧄 ✝️ Do you not remember that hellfire? Mothers\ncried. Children screamed. One of my chickens actually died. 🪦 We killed\noff this implementation in #1371.\n* That brings us to #1376 (but also #1417, and #1423, and #1547, and\ndon''t forgot #1579, #1642, #1643, #1647, and #1688).\n\nThe implementations thus far all worked by setting a timer that pinged\nshortly before the AT expired, executing a callback that paused API\nrequests while executing the rotation request. Of course, it was never\nthat simple; starting rotation after authenticating was subtly different\nthan starting rotation for an existing session because the\nlogin-response includes token-expiration data but the `/bl-users/_self`\ndoesn''t. All those extra tweaks made the code even messier, and while\nthey each made the UX a little better, none of them made it actually\nmake it _good_. And then STCOR-1012 showed up, telling us things were\nnot only not good; they were, in fact, pretty bad. It was a mess. It was\njust a mess. 💩\n\nAnd that brings us here, to the fourth full-blown rewrite of RTR.\nHopefully, the logic here is simpler, better isolated, and easier to\nreason about. At the highest level, things are still the same: we''re\nreplacing native-fetch with FFetch, which transparently handles\nrotation. The FFetch algorithm now works like this:\n* get a shared lock, preventing API requests from firing while rotation\n  is in progress\n  * make the API request\n  * release the lock\n* if the response isn''t `ok`, call `rotateAndReplay()` to rotate the\n  tokens and replay the original request\n* return the response\n\n`rotateAndReplay` works like this:\n* inspect the original response. if it doesn''t look like an\n  authentication failure, reject with the original response, allowing it\nto bubble back to the code that made the original request\n* get an exclusive lock, preventing any API requests from firing while\n  rotation is in progress\n* request token-expiration data from storage; if it appears valid,\n  replay the original request and return its response\n  * make the rotation request\n  * callback to store the updated token-expiration data\n  * replay the original request\n  * release the lock\n\nChecking, while inside the lock, whether the tokens have already been\nrotated is a crucial step that handles the situation of many requests\nfiring simultaneously after the tokens have expired. The Web Locks API\nelects one request, allowing rotation, storage, and replay to proceed\nfor that request only while all others wait for the lock''s promise to\nresolve. After that first request releases its lock, the next request in\nthe queue proceeds through `rotateAndReplay()`, but this time it will\nreturn early since the token-expiration data in storage will be valid.\nNote: this means requests that are queued together proceed\nsingle-threaded through the lock. This sounds worse than it is since\n`rotateAndReplay()` short-circuits after the first request, jumping\nimmediately to \"replay\" since valid tokens are now available.\n\nBut wait! There''s more! The original implementation stored the\nend-of-session timer-IDs in redux. It''s important to keep track of those\nIDs so they can be cleared if the user logs out early or session\nexpiration is configured as a window that slides on rotation, as\nnon-keycloak sessions are. Anybody remember UICHKOUT-869?\nUsing redux was problematic for two reasons:\n1. Mind-bogglingly, clearing the old timer was buried inside the redux\n  action, which, just, why??? 🤯 Dude, have you never heard of\n  single-responsibility? Redux actions should be responsible for redux and\n  only redux.\n2. Bigly-mind-bogglingly, keeping timer data on the okapi slice of redux\n  meant that Root re-rendered every time tokens rotated, which was a real\n  head-scratcher (STCOR-1008 et al), until @vashjs made things plain to us in\n  UITEN-333 🙇. Like I said, it was a mess. 💩 💩\n\nThe self-contained, self-clearing timer ResetTimer (maybe I should''ve\ncalled it SelfClearingTimer? 🤔) resolves both: redux actions are once\nagain pure, and Root no longer re-renders with each rotation.\n\nRefs STCOR-1012, UITEN-333, STCOR-1025, STCOR-999\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpp0zrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZeIQAH9tzQKx0UOXMLpualnViojM\nKdTZu4thYwrRBdBxIV9pB+ekm52ewIbwNxgJEvkxEgbE7LhsaMHvldlzl/FrTkpI\n0ZxkpjBtQoYHD6e9yui++rJbNp6CdfmQVCU3YaNWkjeyl7LZW/9jRN15YiIeQBaD\nWNKrq2igGpnbZ4vIgK5FX0IV/bIH4pk96evXKTgDC9V82DNCNARC/DOU1ZUjfOtU\nB0scshv0mtG25AF7BgVbUGmHmFRdk9lBse6PWlNy1n445mN4gdJuIgps/WM8nz/L\nHXYIbDaldHFo5Z8biDxXleWO4r6XprkuKJ4qtleSlDLZHi3RCS4DKxZes9thJ4tH\nh/cIE82jhBg4Ws1Pvm9mNpDIeKaaTY8/4JgOsjKPVl937zGpMj1HaCtOITA1Ilsr\nxc99tQ/mrJfM6hh8fQd8s+O3N7mj12fxQp4O043jA/uKzJsPCh3+OO/eJnaMRfwn\nX+Eaz4nr2eamFFSgrtgTOfhvPujmQXX/hNgmgZKoCwuV4kNpXjDZY34VnOzpkyEG\nuv307f6aHSU9KFkyno0bKCShGMalowXT3AKOGC9Xy3LsfHYWfrHb6tZ+EwxDzMTk\niGU1i8UfvGa+iT8WILo/G7nmhYmxBPzYBIrHppaKzSfDsL7EI0Qzj8+ZLb3Lwr1c\njVg7zKjyyrV37PaPeYp+\n=R2vS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-03T21:04:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDBkZWY5YzIwMDM2MTYyY2IyNzEzMTYyNDgzNjVhYzBiM2ZiODkyODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c","sha":"774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c"}],"sha":"0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/0def9c20036162cb271316248365ac0b3fb89287"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20704067?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JohnC-80","id":20704067,"login":"JohnC-80","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNzA0MDY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohnC-80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-02T20:12:41Z","email":"jcoburn@ebsco.com","name":"John Coburn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-02T20:12:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1037- granular mod-fed error handling, non-fatal (for now) (#1697)\n\n[STCOR-1037](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1037)\n\n<img width=\"1203\" height=\"540\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd5d62b6-a396-409f-aa5f-d2aad33c3774\"\n/>\n\nApplying the non-fatal granularity now, but expecting adjustment to the\nUX later... throw, show alert, config-based, whatev.\n\nAdded callouts. Got into a fight with the race condition on the callout\ncontext for the Callout ref to finalize. So there''s a reason for a\nCalloutProvider for you that can maintain a queue and then clear the\nqueue once the `<Callout>` from `<RootWithIntl>` mounts.\n\n<img width=\"1146\" height=\"418\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/200fa506-78e7-4802-a6f5-e7204c90d9e3\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"84b7f5fc035564108b7760fdc5fd8bd52bd0dc8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/84b7f5fc035564108b7760fdc5fd8bd52bd0dc8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c","verification":{"payload":"tree 84b7f5fc035564108b7760fdc5fd8bd52bd0dc8c\nparent 87d7e253a142419bed2e98491f99a426624c9724\nauthor John Coburn <jcoburn@ebsco.com> 1772482361 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772482361 -0600\n\nSTCOR-1037- granular mod-fed error handling, non-fatal (for now) (#1697)\n\n[STCOR-1037](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1037)\n\n<img width=\"1203\" height=\"540\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd5d62b6-a396-409f-aa5f-d2aad33c3774\"\n/>\n\nApplying the non-fatal granularity now, but expecting adjustment to the\nUX later... throw, show alert, config-based, whatev.\n\nAdded callouts. Got into a fight with the race condition on the callout\ncontext for the Callout ref to finalize. So there''s a reason for a\nCalloutProvider for you that can maintain a queue and then clear the\nqueue once the `<Callout>` from `<RootWithIntl>` mounts.\n\n<img width=\"1146\" height=\"418\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/200fa506-78e7-4802-a6f5-e7204c90d9e3\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJppe85CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq+8QACxgfaURREa/nx3bIt6cHM56\nDYgtX1UTHI0YLbW6CkbwaLWFmyyjTw1mhGBTeFZ9FVrvMu6EFaKyjT8ivHnuZmqP\nk9fAe4lbt59CZxRkGigVzdZ9LZ9TUMr/VjWRzOBTtN3Wq9K5XCtrbUf0J/IGM/ow\nAbzgXGnQy23jEAdOBKD/iaVffuKmmYCNfTfQ3PXpB6JpIGU+ZUpRq+SfHQmgDxvp\nl1SNXEKLQBy89iJeqxl10P0YPPrdL8TA5uuDEsCbVoTrarMOYTvwCp3UOHlcm0Xp\nLdVRG6lVPz4dyoMhBMv193bufZoc9vzpkfVhrZWT2365z23OoICvqBnU5xNVelIH\n1gyIXDbupMo7BH8ZQhcS9bQc6dtLOdX1CnfFh75QoekrY6uh+UXFcWlqCZ3PjrjS\nsaRJFpJ8acWUJyT22fmG40gLMtI1YY+epwxLZkr6yh6Jm8wdQzVnSca/XJ7S17gk\n9BUuipAM0WO93QrYt+ntZbhECS97qeF9VWBEpvYuNgP9bC0FQVOyikB/oiESmuGl\nbddubLST/1VNHvV/Quzoa9z3UnZMhngRyUMOctbTJonS1ZuykWYBig6AGXXrRdnp\nceDGtH/bJdwiKWqQMmZX/cIKTXalsLAP1JMsSeNzRBQT5f6eyBffHnvB7my/HOKr\nk39fEyVhnuWWjv8TWTp8\n=QUIf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-02T20:12:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDc3NGUyZmI5ZWU0ZjYxZDQ2ZDAzMDIxMzBlY2QxZDk1ZDllYmYxMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/87d7e253a142419bed2e98491f99a426624c9724","sha":"87d7e253a142419bed2e98491f99a426624c9724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/87d7e253a142419bed2e98491f99a426624c9724"}],"sha":"774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/774e2fb9ee4f61d46d0302130ecd1d95d9ebf11c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19309423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanDenis","id":19309423,"login":"BogdanDenis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzA5NDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/87d7e253a142419bed2e98491f99a426624c9724/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-24T11:00:31Z","email":"denys_bohdan@epam.com","name":"Denys Bohdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-24T11:00:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1027 Use GET mod-settings `/locale` API to get tenant language & locale settings (#1691)\n\n## Description\n\n**Context**: With the Trillium release, Language & locale settings were\nmoved from mod-configuration to the /locale API of mod-settings. These\nsettings are tenant level (a user can also set user preference for\nlanguage at some other API).\n\n- Front-end modules that use these tenant settings need to call the\n/locale endpoint to get these settings.\n- Update required interfaces and required permissions from\nmod-configuration to mod-settings.\n- If this work is not completed in Trillium then any workflows using\nlocale settings will not work as expected.\n\nAlso this work is required for mod-configuration deprecation.\n\n## Approach\n- Fetch tenant locale settings from `/locale` API.\n- Removed calls to fetch tenant locale settings from `/settings/entries`\nand `/configurations/entries`\n- Removed calls to fetch user locale settings from\n`/configurations/entries`\n- User locale settings are now fetched from `/settings/entries`\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-1027](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1027)\n\n## Related PRs\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-tenant-settings/pull/486","tree":{"sha":"fb41b46027cda739adef56371ff1d066158dc4fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/fb41b46027cda739adef56371ff1d066158dc4fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/87d7e253a142419bed2e98491f99a426624c9724","verification":{"payload":"tree fb41b46027cda739adef56371ff1d066158dc4fc\nparent 2d18e2ae76fd7b9cc08da07fa91546b4ee0eb7cf\nauthor Denys Bohdan <denys_bohdan@epam.com> 1771930831 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771930831 +0100\n\nSTCOR-1027 Use GET mod-settings `/locale` API to get tenant language & locale settings (#1691)\n\n## Description\n\n**Context**: With the Trillium release, Language & locale settings were\nmoved from mod-configuration to the /locale API of mod-settings. These\nsettings are tenant level (a user can also set user preference for\nlanguage at some other API).\n\n- Front-end modules that use these tenant settings need to call the\n/locale endpoint to get these settings.\n- Update required interfaces and required permissions from\nmod-configuration to mod-settings.\n- If this work is not completed in Trillium then any workflows using\nlocale settings will not work as expected.\n\nAlso this work is required for mod-configuration deprecation.\n\n## Approach\n- Fetch tenant locale settings from `/locale` API.\n- Removed calls to fetch tenant locale settings from `/settings/entries`\nand `/configurations/entries`\n- Removed calls to fetch user locale settings from\n`/configurations/entries`\n- User locale settings are now fetched from `/settings/entries`\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-1027](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1027)\n\n## Related PRs\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-tenant-settings/pull/486","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpnYTPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYKQQACSFgEDNroLpjCsqMiUQ1+mh\n0ykh9Pdf41UC7dmGuyoNlTifd8UQwgpqByoXXauQ49CfeO5XxOwS60g6ZNgkZmXh\nVrc61vQ2UpY3V/UQvj4k4vy4Z8K53Y5CYs8V5oH6y7PYX3yKRC78ujbXQrZfx9L0\n9UkYxd+GtuhaNA1vkv/ifFNChTMdB9+abERTaV+QdXwSYajI9y88aRQfd/o4OKYj\nO/vBizlAx202/QE0IZft+eCGmP9PPXStF5ZbEoM3XYqrSjmCvf7sPdWGp2IDcDky\nS88hCWH/mZ5rB9PLUOtkjKt1ebAWRFAXZnVEDAPQOG1XwVvBHE/13yedJMP0HndF\n8vO3q9HLLZuN7mCA2FNlBusZhLhducVN3hOSfxVIqafgzbI0VdJUKycG9ntxxKNC\nB6U91hbGdfw2d316smxlae3kafgKpwpQLoe/OdMaR7AXwapsq1fRTwGa2ZMkcTdf\nOgdSB6hJ6lTTITDczX/pyj6AUd/hYwKlW+1IY2fBxKCg8ryT5vE99nUmgHoqZmEE\nEU3lcGY69wwXJFZ9G7B5gdk9Fjex1DgtF8YSj63OJ8ci/xl45o5TfNZxkP5TF/bq\nWsaV9kJ5MSbPbjcuBCR+POWtJt252QpQLb/RQ64pxKblnvE9UC75FyryZFQ9