e":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-05T14:00:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1022: Increase default timeout to 60 seconds in `useOkapiKy` to match the value in Kong. (#1685)\n\n## Description\nThe `ky` returns an error after 30 seconds, but the request actually\ndeletes the role. This happens because `useOkapiKy` has a timeout of 30\nseconds, while Kong has a timeout of 60 seconds. This fix should address\nthe issue described at\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/MODCONSKC-101.\n\nIf everything is good, please release it for Sunflower or does it also\nneed to get a CSP approval?\n\n## Issues\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1022\n\nThanks @zburke for this detailed analysis.\nIt was reported on the Mobius environment with 60+ tenants, and it is hard to reproduce because, in most cases, 30 seconds is enough. It was not reproduced on the etesting environment or bagfest because those have a maximum of 10 tenants.\n\nI considered the option to increase the timeout only on the ui-consortia-settings side, but the reasons why we created a PR in Stripes are as follows:\n\n- We checked on Mobius pre-prod and confirmed that the default Kong timeout of 60 seconds was not changed.\n- The next-generation ApisixRoute also has a default timeout of 60 seconds (see: https://apisix.apache.org/docs/ingress-controller/1.8.0/concepts/apisix_upstream/).\n- Since all hundreds(thousands) of Folio flows are tested commonly on environments with 10 tenants, there may be potential cases we are not aware of where 30 seconds is not enough. For example, we just observed an issue with deleting a sharing role yesterday.\n- Some environments may have more resources than others and can respond more quickly, so it is difficult to set the correct timeout value for everyone.\n- Since we do not know the ideal timeout value, and both Kong and Apisix use 60 seconds by default, as for me it makes sense to set our core Stripes timeout to the same value.\n\nHowever, if you are not comfortable with these details, we can set this 60-second timeout only for one call in the ui-consortia-settings module.","tree":{"sha":"75fcd9be7c8d37cec156d1aa5347c14b264dd459","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/75fcd9be7c8d37cec156d1aa5347c14b264dd459"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/0900cfcee839cfe513ca20d83fa77cc05cf8eb1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 75fcd9be7c8d37cec156d1aa5347c14b264dd459\nparent c240ac6022c1761bf2ac9e60c75b4bfedcfe906d\nauthor Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com> 1767621648 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1767621648 +0200\n\nSTCOR-1022: Increase default timeout to 60 seconds in `useOkapiKy` to match the value in Kong. (#1685)\n\n## Description\nThe `ky` returns an error after 30 seconds, but the request actually\ndeletes the role. This happens because `useOkapiKy` has a timeout of 30\nseconds, while Kong has a timeout of 60 seconds. This fix should address\nthe issue described at\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/MODCONSKC-101.\n\nIf everything is good, please release it for Sunflower or does it also\nneed to get a CSP approval?\n\n## Issues\nhttps://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1022\n\nThanks @zburke for this detailed analysis.\nIt was reported on the Mobius environment with 60+ tenants, and it is hard to reproduce because, in most cases, 30 seconds is enough. It was not reproduced on the etesting environment or bagfest because those have a maximum of 10 tenants.\n\nI considered the option to increase the timeout only on the ui-consortia-settings side, but the reasons why we created a PR in Stripes are as follows:\n\n- We checked on Mobius pre-prod and confirmed that the default Kong timeout of 60 seconds was not changed.\n- The next-generation ApisixRoute also has a default timeout of 60 seconds (see: https://apisix.apache.org/docs/ingress-controller/1.8.0/concepts/apisix_upstream/).\n- Since all hundreds(thousands) of Folio flows are tested commonly on environments with 10 tenants, there may be potential cases we are not aware of where 30 seconds is not enough. For example, we just observed an issue with deleting a sharing role yesterday.\n- Some environments may have more resources than others and can respond more quickly, so it is difficult to set the correct timeout value for everyone.\n- Since we do not know the ideal timeout value, and both Kong and Apisix use 60 seconds by default, as for me it makes sense to set our core Stripes timeout to the same value.\n\nHowever, if you are not comfortable with these details, we can set this 60-second timeout only for one call in the ui-consortia-settings module.\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpW8QQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6/EQADtNwGWpyLJytz77BTdgAzcr\nsWkv/B6bqcW26C9W+jrxWGeGMCKsO7gsBW/I1L1Txsn3YXUKq4ArP6ojlCj/qfRi\nfULG0HOleUNyjhmlfZ1ieA1xnDpX8/D2yYpxlMSUQZ0pQ/CKBEEcGF/zVp1BKtcn\nteDj6P1Ots20VdPmvbkxEf9RDK5gKJW+SmfjhuVAxxpws/2id1q6x52UJc367XJa\nKX5oG4SlIbTBOwHEzfu4bG0QpNjIi/0pFFqU8srHk6+uMwkaiffM2s8KzcBji/kO\nBFTAu4MzaAi9APXqnyhf0cYFk9zJ+iElnroZeJ71+n/rSonbkHj61J1kMNuiaCs7\nBDVhpoLmrJICud+M3KZE2VsyXRAWPBC4S6edFi3UjgprGp4n3ZkwOJJRtTnjRhmP\n5voFWICYMSA+WcPYfqWePC+CBiUrd79GzIII1v0tI2h+nzgFHKPeqWrMxNkM3LZx\nS2rIxFjFLcQ29J5R/YmWAK9eg4sjoB2DPY3dOcTUcXik5Ov2ZZC485Lxu6Nyo3dZ\njjMcHtx87gMK95I6CL4maQAcM9fpwlSDDgKZXK1BBvy4Z7Ez8SfsDJkTDYWdEMRA\nlFcoze/ic3dX7UreyaDC4eZHm7kat9mYKap3d8AsYXzR7OxA9JYXAc69bziG+PO3\nEL2J5hX1sfBn00QhpoEc\n=LLdQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-01-05T14:00:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/0900cfcee839cfe513ca20d83fa77cc05cf8eb1c","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDA5MDBjZmNlZTgzOWNmZTUxM2NhMjBkODNmYTc3Y2MwNWNmOGViMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/c240ac6022c1761bf2ac9e60c75b4bfedcfe906d","sha":"c240ac6022c1761bf2ac9e60c75b4bfedcfe906d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/c240ac6022c1761bf2ac9e60c75b4bfedcfe906d"}],"sha":"0900cfcee839cfe513ca20d83fa77cc05cf8eb1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/0900cfcee839cfe513ca20d83fa77cc05cf8eb1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/c240ac6022c1761bf2ac9e60c75b4bfedcfe906d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-05T12:12:01Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-05T12:12:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1021 load modules in parallel (#1684)\n\nInstead of looping through modules and calling `await` in series on each\none''s loader-function, use `Promise.all()` to call `await` on a batch,\nallowing the promises to be handled in parallel. Unscientific testing\nshows a ~30% performance boost.\n\nRefs STCOR-1021","tree":{"sha":"d9b1be0f41f02000e17ca8966874005c6dc9618b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/d9b1be0f41f02000e17ca8966874005c6dc9618b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/c240ac6022c1761bf2ac9e60c75b4bfedcfe906d","verification":{"payload":"tree d9b1be0f41f02000e17ca8966874005c6dc9618b\nparent 3a1a7ded878eb8997e41eb3896487c81ca27c6e3\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1767615121 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1767615121 -0500\n\nSTCOR-1021 load modules in parallel (#1684)\n\nInstead of looping through modules and calling `await` in series on each\none''s loader-function, use `Promise.all()` to call `await` on a batch,\nallowing the promises to be handled in parallel. Unscientific testing\nshows a ~30% performance boost.\n\nRefs STCOR-1021","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpW6qRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiucQABl75m0H8XsRsZ9yt97FA1Sz\n24fE7g6HFbEJf3PPNkfhDvDDAWfMvEQmkbuyTlWRe6BEkqLBrYubrNOdS1xYJ/wv\nOjLCmMArYtauA+cK7L5PZRO6qD0hMXcGIkxn3nF78NFSCcIoTXCYBXSv4uq2+2mJ\nLr42LxjniUNE6MeCxyXcNPO3PUgefYHR2t8KbOZlwlSrhXsQnYXV00TnxPVzIYBe\nSMPi6NLLxdO1