g/stripes-core/commits/212db1b0d494c5aa3e2a9ba7019186ecc3301698"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77053927?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","id":77053927,"login":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDUzOTI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/714559e0618b649dfcbbba17fd52e46c6af2f940/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-22T08:31:17Z","email":"77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-22T08:31:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-1000: Take `tenant` from URL for multi-tenant setup in `getLoginTenant`. Make `makeCall` method async to avoid displaying an error message when loading the password reset page. (#1670)\n\nMulti-tenant setup. \nIt can be reproduced in Sunflower ECS.\n\n## Purpose\nWhen entering a new password on the `/reset-password` page, the password\nrequirements should appear under the field.\n\n## Description\nThe requirements are not displayed because the `/rules` request fails\ndue to the absence of a tenant. The tenant could be taken from the URL,\nbut this doesn''t happen bacause the client id is missing, and the\n`(tenant && clientId)` condition prevents the tenant from being returned\nfrom `getLoginTenant`.\n\n## Approach\nRemove the `(tenant && clientId)` conditions and derive tenant and\nclientId from URL and from the next source (tenantOptions/stripesOkapi)\nonly if they are empty.\n\n## Out of the scope of this ticket\nFixed an issue where the `System error. Please wait a few minutes and\ntry again.` message would momentarily appear when loading the password\nreset page. The fix was to return a Promise in the `makeCall` method.\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-1000](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1000)\n\n## Screencasts\nRecording of the bug\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8251e97c-8b2b-4d88-a546-8aa5dec9b6cb\n\n\nRecording after the fix is applied (without the fix of `makeCall`)\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9bb2a94f-3ac0-4c03-b3a7-e1e03666babf","tree":{"sha":"46d30a1264fee79482fa60587d7d22a2cd0d3694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/46d30a1264fee79482fa60587d7d22a2cd0d3694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/714559e0618b649dfcbbba17fd52e46c6af2f940","verification":{"payload":"tree 46d30a1264fee79482fa60587d7d22a2cd0d3694\nparent 338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686\nauthor Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com> 1761121877 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1761121877 +0300\n\nSTCOR-1000: Take `tenant` from URL for multi-tenant setup in `getLoginTenant`. Make `makeCall` method async to avoid displaying an error message when loading the password reset page. (#1670)\n\nMulti-tenant setup. \nIt can be reproduced in Sunflower ECS.\n\n## Purpose\nWhen entering a new password on the `/reset-password` page, the password\nrequirements should appear under the field.\n\n## Description\nThe requirements are not displayed because the `/rules` request fails\ndue to the absence of a tenant. The tenant could be taken from the URL,\nbut this doesn''t happen bacause the client id is missing, and the\n`(tenant && clientId)` condition prevents the tenant from being returned\nfrom `getLoginTenant`.\n\n## Approach\nRemove the `(tenant && clientId)` conditions and derive tenant and\nclientId from URL and from the next source (tenantOptions/stripesOkapi)\nonly if they are empty.\n\n## Out of the scope of this ticket\nFixed an issue where the `System error. Please wait a few minutes and\ntry again.` message would momentarily appear when loading the password\nreset page. The fix was to return a Promise in the `makeCall` method.\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-1000](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-1000)\n\n## Screencasts\nRecording of the bug\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8251e97c-8b2b-4d88-a546-8aa5dec9b6cb\n\n\nRecording after the fix is applied (without the fix of `makeCall`)\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9bb2a94f-3ac0-4c03-b3a7-e1e03666babf","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo+JZVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeWcQACnmqKyU6VhR72XYlprX4XDf\n/NSZklckMSanXMNSituczv4V58v5TaVKqtppZFHsziehx/+HfJ0STB1bT9I2mMHs\nLltz7oDMeHYtl+yuwwwxIlJIfQfe4QPLpAITlCdsGo9Z9mDjEMoLBsbbQnvUrnDG\nwnc5PjwZUS4wASF41HCGK4rFt1xFdOoSQGoEZbtEsGIw+iskxxEcgiAgJXCYA7HD\nz2qDJCMKKRStYIyBsPOKLw4qAbLG1i5fYzabaB+MbUV3C5qBjygtsnFXeyzzzgfo\n3UCHN629qiCBfDVj1+SrRmSjy8S//UyeqaYzuj1H7ItcoKyiTWZ7DCFK8GA19xOv\nBfJ9NTuOHivJnHSaFXmxmIny1mjomwvlD8Shk0I0Hvp/qiA7WeMC5ufwjWffYJ+q\nUictO7yUYC9LhzBdi/EKvtgkObFfS/w+NUxyRKuRPsBM2sgaldgRdWq9x2Of+F3l\nHiMN5EFcNmpYSCYBJ1fTWP2eNFiQDud7mzp6geo94e1hZSJOMrdyet9DSsnixm+b\nh74LiDWSezhbdXg92QTn0cM8MS2Ber8e7ThiUfTG0zyISN1dednIo77vPGc7Bxh3\nNaTelJqg0GqCXWWRu88V9hG5K3joGMRHXmfinwHBTwgEvvs8UwiuCrjqOrVGDxXR\nUqBk3ZAK0Ti8yNQxt7Li\n=GRMs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-22T08:31:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/714559e0618b649dfcbbba17fd52e46c6af2f940","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDcxNDU1OWUwNjE4YjY0OWRmY2JiYmExN2ZkNTJlNDZjNmFmMmY5NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686","sha":"338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686"}],"sha":"714559e0618b649dfcbbba17fd52e46c6af2f940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/714559e0618b649dfcbbba17fd52e46c6af2f940"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77053927?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","id":77053927,"login":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDUzOTI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-13T10:59:25Z","email":"77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-13T10:59:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-976: Prevent re-rendering Root component before session validation, addressing login flicker and unnecessary Keycloak redirects (follow-up).  (#1668)\n\n## Description\n**Bugs:**\n1. When an _authenticated_ user reloads the page, the login page appears\nfor a short time. This happens when there is _more_ than one tenant.\n2. When an _authenticated_ user reloads the page, the Keycloak route\nappears for a short time. This happens when there is _only_ one tenant.\n\nThese bugs can only be reproduced when, in the `Root` component,\ntranslations are loaded _first_, and modules are loaded _second_, and\nthe session check is not finished yet (`okapiReady` is `false`).\n\nThe issue caused by the `shouldComponentUpdate` logic, specifically by\nthe newly added `nextProps.modules !== modules`.\n\n**The problematic sequence:**\n1. **App starts:** `isAuthenticated` = `false`, `modules` = initial\nstate, `okapiReady` is `false`.\n2. **Translations load:** Component doesn''t re-render (no trigger) due\nto `shouldComponentUpdate`.\n4. **Modules load:** `nextProps.modules !== modules` becomes `true` →\nComponent re-renders.\n5. **At this point:** `isAuthenticated` is still `false`, so\n`RootWithIntl` renders login routes.\n6. **Session check completes:** `isAuthenticated` becomes `true` →\nComponent re-renders again with main app routes.\n\n## Approach\nPrevent premature re-render by removing recently added\n`nextProps.modules !== modules` in `shouldComponentUpdate`. The\ncomponent won''t trigger a re-render when modules load if the session\nisn''t ready yet. This prevents the double-render issue that caused the\nroute switching.\n\n## Recording of bugs:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c852c98d-12c9-431c-9658-2e00fe58486e","tree":{"sha":"820197c2621a0b3e2f8189ebc8f901d7cf04d682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/820197c2621a0b3e2f8189ebc8f901d7cf04d682"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686","verification":{"payload":"tree 820197c2621a0b3e2f8189ebc8f901d7cf04d682\nparent 19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced\nauthor Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com> 1760353165 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1760353165 +0300\n\nSTCOR-976: Prevent re-rendering Root component before session validation, addressing login flicker and unnecessary Keycloak redirects (follow-up).  (#1668)\n\n## Description\n**Bugs:**\n1. When an _authenticated_ user reloads the page, the login page appears\nfor a short time. This happens when there is _more_ than one tenant.\n2. When an _authenticated_ user reloads the page, the Keycloak route\nappears for a short time. This happens when there is _only_ one tenant.\n\nThese bugs can only be reproduced when, in the `Root` component,\ntranslations are loaded _first_, and modules are loaded _second_, and\nthe session check is not finished yet (`okapiReady` is `false`).\n\nThe issue caused by the `shouldComponentUpdate` logic, specifically by\nthe newly added `nextProps.modules !== modules`.\n\n**The problematic sequence:**\n1. **App starts:** `isAuthenticated` = `false`, `modules` = initial\nstate, `okapiReady` is `false`.\n2. **Translations load:** Component doesn''t re-render (no trigger) due\nto `shouldComponentUpdate`.\n4. **Modules load:** `nextProps.modules !== modules` becomes `true` →\nComponent re-renders.\n5. **At this point:** `isAuthenticated` is still `false`, so\n`RootWithIntl` renders login routes.\n6. **Session check completes:** `isAuthenticated` becomes `true` →\nComponent re-renders again with main app routes.\n\n## Approach\nPrevent premature re-render by removing recently added\n`nextProps.modules !== modules` in `shouldComponentUpdate`. The\ncomponent won''t trigger a re-render when modules load if the session\nisn''t ready yet. This prevents the double-render issue that caused the\nroute switching.\n\n## Recording of bugs:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c852c98d-12c9-431c-9658-2e00fe58486e","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo7NuNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXv0QAKlUOPyP+mJ0BmschgMBVw/w\nVkzLeAM7qKbQ1kOqIUJrk3wd4OOV40lip4gc/1m2Oaia8D19Md5vwGcfeTa9DF6q\nF/tCZYIaV/hcAzFuHlbT9d6ibyJ/7ApboStmJCvrniu1t+NJU1xYafxhhwl8CfnR\n0Zo1jeRNmWiOWzC3p2/GcmiVurwTNq3ExNRm6Um/JPeAh5oFTDk7THUHCt9zuunN\nbAKRnzA/Vpn5yyQwUWIbVcj8X7moTM6yZimRJxkwcn4b50R3jHqu43IVA3rpiDab\nJ2hSQ9F2QvNuYS7fJ3x24H/x/VCwZr1U9pnIu3huDUyXUGzQoN2u0/hQvhY+2UIy\nkP8KATuWhQ08GZemlmS4FHEc58RfJ2wcdfKS2FvmE50qTateRrlIPl0if45lvbg9\n+D4xpnOYSSgyh92YSsqZKVMznxMlbsWW21rAGfEDbSIioPOcbSOgnjeU1R7drhrj\nI9bkxZiWz3lYui0TiOvOqe+jcHxG+LD8WsBTCaAfIlAU1t0f28Cs6aBkChUjCh6Z\n32b2qzXSsW2uPl1NPDot8tRz018hLYnKet6QhsS5Pex2wzFtI4hO2IjExd2pP+ch\neJWGBOLW6DAvaTuT6LTLKBx0jZufZbQccQRuMFXyZUAtNXOWzUyq0FDl85zH/7IX\ncsYKwtIcaIe+z7SeMK/0\n=AIYP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-13T10:59:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDMzOGE3NTJiM2U5YTAxZjE4YjE0NTcwYmE3NWNmZTY1ODk1NTk2ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced","sha":"19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced"}],"sha":"338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/338a752b3e9a01f18b14570ba75cfe6589559686"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77053927?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","id":77053927,"login":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDUzOTI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-10T06:56:32Z","email":"77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-10T06:56:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-977: Listen for SessionReady events and update state to trigger re-render. (#1667)\n\n## Description\n> **Summary**: Listen for a `SessionReady` event in `RootWithIntl` and\nre-render when it is detected (as provided by `@folio/stripes-loader` in\n`mod-fedified-stripes`), in addition to re-rendering when\n`props.isAuthenticated` changes (as provided by redux in `stripes-core`\nin legacy-stripes).\n\n> **Details**: add an event handler that leverages `setState()`, i.e.\nwhen it detects a given event it calls a `setState()` based-function,\nand that piece of state (along side `props.isAuthenticated`) will cause\nthe component to re-render.\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-977](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-977)","tree":{"sha":"ce876959e695952d9ea5b2c5e4bcac4faa17b8a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/ce876959e695952d9ea5b2c5e4bcac4faa17b8a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced","verification":{"payload":"tree ce876959e695952d9ea5b2c5e4bcac4faa17b8a3\nparent 86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055\nauthor Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com> 1760079392 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1760079392 +0300\n\nSTCOR-977: Listen for SessionReady events and update state to trigger re-render. (#1667)\n\n## Description\n> **Summary**: Listen for a `SessionReady` event in `RootWithIntl` and\nre-render when it is detected (as provided by `@folio/stripes-loader` in\n`mod-fedified-stripes`), in addition to re-rendering when\n`props.isAuthenticated` changes (as provided by redux in `stripes-core`\nin legacy-stripes).\n\n> **Details**: add an event handler that leverages `setState()`, i.e.\nwhen it detects a given event it calls a `setState()` based-function,\nand that piece of state (along side `props.isAuthenticated`) will cause\nthe component to re-render.\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-977](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-977)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo6K4gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgq0QAFe6FNzCvYWmYnJ6Wc/52qQS\nQ9jE6+dEyPw0WCxdKFlgHVxA3DBjXl9bU/nMKqI9YTgj58TOufkMANMTC2q65ggX\nEam8LwNgDTviIdU21rBkjpzyVNfMe5CMlFkfspFwYeI8bTExXAsPLF+q8IrqfiVb\na5xiQwwNRmYEZ0axK7HHz3PiroTEsLFo9+XBrMhuVM0fvZX4zaEEtNHIz4rZifXf\nPnr1INoodEMgfgllB+OJzewZUvYiuw1hPfSabJzFKN+ORj0A9flHMI2ClqzsNK89\nbo/MMQj854i9Gd5qiyareEKEGd6lsf2isKJ+JdixGKHHBt3ztMZSuNi3/Om8iOnz\ntm+0zN6Y/ngkHXhuJ2jS9ifxBd3WT5iiLJtzyHXzrml/bLNLehYEDlNCMCswrjSY\nrp6tcDo2bQJX1a8TX7WZPFYwlNIXshkBqESHrIn9eofaMZWOwccwzGtdjDazwX79\n+ExVo9bmkfO1X8bZEPg87LBnz6lfrLBAG0ojd4sttRFtWjjGLA8HcPirGrv39t1/\nOZTLOsa+fS87fRNKn6RUp3ITXYYwHaiZCkWz8Y4QO4AYmHyTOXwyAmwse5Jk6rvl\nwQTnmfukaWmQ2u3J26KCMFXODN3/0owtPWwK4ckpMtI+fGWyuVApP3k3h125WU+u\nagHa67H4Pevkagw/+S9M\n=NlX1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-10T06:56:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDE5ZjY1MDZkMTc2NmQ1M2YzMzQyOWFhNDQwYzdmMmEzOWM5YmVjZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055","sha":"86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055"}],"sha":"19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/19f6506d1766d53f33429aa440c7f2a39c9beced"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54310740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/EthanFreestone","id":54310740,"login":"EthanFreestone","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzEwNzQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EthanFreestone","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-08T14:26:28Z","email":"54310740+EthanFreestone@users.noreply.github.com","name":"EthanFreestone"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-08T14:26:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-989: Generalise useChunkedCQLFetch hook to allow for other chunked id transformations (#1653)\n\n## feat: useChunkedIdTransformFetch hook\n\n### Current state\nuseChunkedCQLFetch is a pre-existing hook which aims to allow for\nfrontend joins, taking in some list of UUIDs and performing a fetch for\nthose objects in a chunked and reliable manner.\n\n### Premise\nThis hook, as its name suggests, is currently only applicable to\nendpoints making use of CQL, where the bulk of the internal logic for\nactually chunking said requests is API agnostic.\n\nHence this PR aims to generalise that logic, leaving the API for\nuseChunkedCQLFetch in place to avoid backwards compatibility issues, but\nallowing for frontends pointing at services using other API shapes to\nmake use of the same underlying chunked-fetch logic.\n\n\n### Use case\nIn particular, ui-agreements has an upcoming use case where a list of\nIDs is presented from an external service, and we have to check whether\nthose match anything in our internal DB. The API for this already\nexists, but the list of IDs can become very long, and the query requires\nfiltering on a couple of fields, so the query string grows very quickly,\nand regularly returns `414 URI Too Long`.\n\nIn particular  the query string is something like:\n```?filters=((pci.identifiers.identifier.status == approved && pci.identifiers.identifier.namespace == ''gokb_uuid'' && pci.identifiers.identifier == ID_1) || (... ID_2) || (... ID_3))```\n\n### Approach\nThis PR moves the bulk of the logic which previously lived inside useChunkedCQLFetch up to a new generic hook: `useChunkedIdTransformFetch`, and keeps all CQL-specific logic confined to the old hook (such as the presence of the `query` and `limit` parameters, as well as the specific way to map a list of Ids into such a query)\n\n\n### Considerations\nThere is absolutely a case here to suggest that part of the problem is that there ought to be a backend API to handle the namespacing and approved status matching parts, but fundamentally we have an unknown size list of ids coming in, and unless we include those in a HTTP body, the risk of seeing a 414 is there, and the argument about whether it''s acceptable to fetch records via some kind of `POST` with a body is a different kettle of fish.","tree":{"sha":"cc1762bee4cc1786caf302eac270a2932cb276e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/cc1762bee4cc1786caf302eac270a2932cb276e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055","verification":{"payload":"tree cc1762bee4cc1786caf302eac270a2932cb276e1\nparent 687f122d5df66b5a17d16e3cbd8049a8c9a75fba\nauthor EthanFreestone <54310740+EthanFreestone@users.noreply.github.com> 1759933588 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1759933588 +0100\n\nSTCOR-989: Generalise useChunkedCQLFetch hook to allow for other chunked id transformations (#1653)\n\n## feat: useChunkedIdTransformFetch hook\n\n### Current state\nuseChunkedCQLFetch is a pre-existing hook which aims to allow for\nfrontend joins, taking in some list of UUIDs and performing a fetch for\nthose objects in a chunked and reliable manner.\n\n### Premise\nThis hook, as its name suggests, is currently only applicable to\nendpoints making use of CQL, where the bulk of the internal logic for\nactually chunking said requests is API agnostic.\n\nHence this PR aims to generalise that logic, leaving the API for\nuseChunkedCQLFetch in place to avoid backwards compatibility issues, but\nallowing for frontends pointing at services using other API shapes to\nmake use of the same underlying chunked-fetch logic.\n\n\n### Use case\nIn particular, ui-agreements has an upcoming use case where a list of\nIDs is presented from an external service, and we have to check whether\nthose match anything in our internal DB. The API for this already\nexists, but the list of IDs can become very long, and the query requires\nfiltering on a couple of fields, so the query string grows very quickly,\nand regularly returns `414 URI Too Long`.\n\nIn particular  the query string is something like:\n```?filters=((pci.identifiers.identifier.status == approved && pci.identifiers.identifier.namespace == ''gokb_uuid'' && pci.identifiers.identifier == ID_1) || (... ID_2) || (... ID_3))```\n\n### Approach\nThis PR moves the bulk of the logic which previously lived inside useChunkedCQLFetch up to a new generic hook: `useChunkedIdTransformFetch`, and keeps all CQL-specific logic confined to the old hook (such as the presence of the `query` and `limit` parameters, as well as the specific way to map a list of Ids into such a query)\n\n\n### Considerations\nThere is absolutely a case here to suggest that part of the problem is that there ought to be a backend API to handle the namespacing and approved status matching parts, but fundamentally we have an unknown size list of ids coming in, and unless we include those in a HTTP body, the risk of seeing a 414 is there, and the argument about whether it''s acceptable to fetch records via some kind of `POST` with a body is a different kettle of fish.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BE