arents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/687f122d5df66b5a17d16e3cbd8049a8c9a75fba","sha":"687f122d5df66b5a17d16e3cbd8049a8c9a75fba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/687f122d5df66b5a17d16e3cbd8049a8c9a75fba"}],"sha":"86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/86f2e2ad8056356e2fdb71f42e10a5a117227055"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/687f122d5df66b5a17d16e3cbd8049a8c9a75fba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-06T11:12:10Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-06T11:12:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-986 handle OTP in StrictMode (#1659)\n\n## Summary \n\nRefactor the OIDC landing page to avoid making the OTP exchange request\nvia `fetch()` in an effect, which failed in `<StrictMode>`.\n\n## Details\n\nOTP exchange has to happen exactly once (a repeat request causes the\ntoken and related sessions to be invalidated), which caused the original\nimplementation to fail under `<StrictMode>` where effects always run\ntwice.\n\nHere, the OTP exchange is removed to a hook, with the remaining\nsession-init tacked onto the end of that promise chain. This permits\nboth the effect, and the code to sync its results to state, to be\nremoved. Bonus: the loading-spinner is now accompanied by a status\nmessage, relaying the current state: exchanging the token, or\ninitializing the session.\n\nReplaces PR #1652 / PR #1656\n\nRefs STCOR-986","tree":{"sha":"a2424df74df88e394bf21042fc2c7471bde8ce7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/a2424df74df88e394bf21042fc2c7471bde8ce7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/687f122d5df66b5a17d16e3cbd8049a8c9a75fba","verification":{"payload":"tree a2424df74df88e394bf21042fc2c7471bde8ce7f\nparent 7d9b1638c93fa8a5021e138d6ad6ea4a8a8d2596\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1759749130 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1759749130 -0400\n\nSTCOR-986 handle OTP in StrictMode (#1659)\n\n## Summary \n\nRefactor the OIDC landing page to avoid making the OTP exchange request\nvia `fetch()` in an effect, which failed in `<StrictMode>`.\n\n## Details\n\nOTP exchange has to happen exactly once (a repeat request causes the\ntoken and related sessions to be invalidated), which caused the original\nimplementation to fail under `<StrictMode>` where effects always run\ntwice.\n\nHere, the OTP exchange is removed to a hook, with the remaining\nsession-init tacked onto the end of that promise chain. This permits\nboth the effect, and the code to sync its results to state, to be\nremoved. Bonus: the loading-spinner is now accompanied by a status\nmessage, relaying the current state: exchanging the token, or\ninitializing the session.\n\nReplaces PR #1652 / PR #1656\n\nRefs STCOR-986","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo46QKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUbsQ