38639a9"}],"sha":"47e62a03ef282d65a73873e47bde5dc4b2836abc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/47e62a03ef282d65a73873e47bde5dc4b2836abc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/706ef085e90614bac9358ea5161265c5d38639a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-09-05T10:32:51Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-09-05T10:32:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Revert \"STCOR-986 handle OTP in StrictMode\" (#1656)\n\nReverts folio-org/stripes-core#1652\n\nInstead of introducing a race condition between the OTP-exchange request\nand component init and then very carefully handling the race condition,\na better approach will not introduce the race condition at all, and will\nnot call `otpExchange()` at the module level.\n\nThis module-level call is particularly gross, a definite anti-pattern\nthat raised eyebrows in the original PR but which I waved away. This\ncall appears to cause particular grief in the end-to-end test\nenvironment, which is to say, my attempt to reliably handle the race\ncondition failed.\n\nA better approach to application init and OTP exchange will avoid the\nmodule-level call. This will avoid the race condition, and avoid\ninvoking this code path except when explicitly called for by accessing\nthe `/oidc-landing` route.","tree":{"sha":"1b39e876f640e0cf8fa0273787966ba17e2567f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/1b39e876f640e0cf8fa0273787966ba17e2567f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/706ef085e90614bac9358ea5161265c5d38639a9","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b39e876f640e0cf8fa0273787966ba17e2567f6\nparent c30d9c1136ea73efc8585df475e85e967e333448\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1757068371 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1757068371 -0400\n\nRevert \"STCOR-986 handle OTP in StrictMode\" (#1656)\n\nReverts folio-org/stripes-core#1652\n\nInstead of introducing a race condition between the OTP-exchange request\nand component init and then very carefully handling the race condition,\na better approach will not introduce the race condition at all, and will\nnot call `otpExchange()` at the module level.\n\nThis module-level call is particularly gross, a definite anti-pattern\nthat raised eyebrows in the original PR but which I waved away. This\ncall appears to cause particular grief in the end-to-end test\nenvironment, which is to say, my attempt to reliably handle the race\ncondition failed.\n\nA better approach to application init and OTP exchange will avoid the\nmodule-level call. This will avoid the race condition, and avoid\ninvoking this code path except when explicitly called for by accessing\nthe `/oidc-landing` route.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJourxTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQw0QAB3HCk0fjg+yoCDnb3VDEFUs\nScQX+7ngbPd3nn/tCZuV0ssVqQutQXax8NyxeU9a9J+Q9Qurk7TteM3OjB1Xq9YQ\n9cMU+6GkogOc1aqCgkL6BhGzTsJ/W6nOhNlS6KlXuJsRPKh6UiuD++m4dKeEcug1