},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19309423?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanDenis","id":19309423,"login":"BogdanDenis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MzA5NDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BogdanDenis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/1ab3e49b15902ebeb4acf59bdfccbf4a04d513d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-05-23T12:20:25Z","email":"denys_bohdan@epam.com","name":"Denys Bohdan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-05-23T12:20:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-972 passing tenant as a URL param to keycloak redirect_uri (#1634)\n\n## Description\nI''m going to use @zburke explanation on this because I couldn''t have\nexplained the issue better myself\n\n> In an ECS setup, there are three required steps to authentication;\nkeycloak is step-2, and skipping step-1 causes step-3 to fail:\n> 1. choose a tenant and save it to local-storage, then redirect to\nkeycloak\n> 2. authenticate in keycloak, then redirect to stripes with an OTP in\nthe URL\n> 3. make an API request to trade the OTP for AT/RT cookies,\n/authn/token?otp=${OTP from step-2} with the X-Okapi-Tenant header set\nto the tenant from step-1\n>\n> Bookmarking the authentication URL in step-2 means the tenant is never\nstored to local-storage, thus causing step-3 to fail.\nIIRC, we can pass values to Keycloak in the URL and it will include them\nalong with the OTP when it redirects back to Stripes.\n\nInstead of storing selected `tenant` and `client_id` in `localStorage`,\nwe can in step 1 pass them as part of `redirect_uri`, so that we can\nread them from url and use in step 3.\nWe''re still keeping code related to storing tenant in localStorage,\nbecause we actually need to keep the tenant that a user has initially\nlogged in with, so if they change affiliation - we can logout with the\ninitial tenant.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c031f1d-5659-4049-99fc-419af59bbce8\n\n\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-972](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-972)","tree":{"sha":"1d818fe7bd5a984460d6dfd4b0d0fbb644785daf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/1d818fe7bd5a984460d6dfd4b0d0fbb644785daf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/1ab3e49b15902ebeb4acf59bdfccbf4a04d513d1","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d818fe7bd5a984460d6dfd4b0d0fbb644785daf\nparent 325d9e3d0810d72a505891b946fbd056271e82a9\nauthor Denys Bohdan <denys_bohdan@epam.com> 1748002825 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1748002825 +0200\n\nSTCOR-972 passing tenant as a URL param to keycloak redirect_uri (#1634)\n\n## Description\nI''m going to use @zburke explanation on this because I couldn''t have\nexplained the issue better myself\n\n> In an ECS setup, there are three required steps to authentication;\nkeycloak is step-2, and skipping step-1 causes step-3 to fail:\n> 1. choose a tenant and save it to local-storage, then redirect to\nkeycloak\n> 2. authenticate in keycloak, then redirect to stripes with an OTP in\nthe URL\n> 3. make an API request to trade the OTP for AT/RT cookies,\n/authn/token?otp=${OTP from step-2} with the X-Okapi-Tenant header set\nto the tenant from step-1\n>\n> Bookmarking the authentication URL in step-2 means the tenant is never\nstored to local-storage, thus causing step-3 to fail.\nIIRC, we can pass values to Keycloak in the URL and it will include them\nalong with the OTP when it redirects back to Stripes.\n\nInstead of storing selected `tenant` and `client_id` in `localStorage`,\nwe can in step 1 pass them as part of `redirect_uri`, so that we can\nread them from url and use in step 3.\nWe''re still keeping code related to storing tenant in localStorage,\nbecause we actually need to keep the tenant that a user has initially\nlogged in with, so if they change affiliation - we can logout with the\ninitial tenant.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c031f1d-5659-4049-99fc-419af59bbce8\n\n\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-972](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-972)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoMGgJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArVUQAG/DBpzAcif8pbEPPntZCJFM\n/FS6fbvGw4wbKNL8ex9f+zzrZ33cDkLe+PaU5ZIby/9YFx4AW4FjfxySicuwpIlD\nJwBdyIVT6Dzmjn25A2FUyVeJLgc5Jfvf8BGH1ITzPniA2QiDgVef6fe8ZIC4qt5b\n3rVgge8GJvIeTwHVYofgezCPNe7UBeyNEOkgFJEvs6t0nGzOc81/aDNvc4xmF06O\nvVoc5CiysP+yhpu+U58XJ2ruM5kpBYFNL4zo+3TyBVnEhLIop3J/SqOwwSFRauzj\nVo0miZAaXUgEEBBOo3jXcNQnz4MV6xGxciJUjn5ZWFdfQ4gd4m/QxUfeCStxnUNE\nogkXGNR00C3T0di+x3eQU2beOHH5+6UzgwJRTDAPqobifNiIp7KNAH4DUuXkrQ6c\n4uRmW8u3VPp417n57WFTrHehkVN+mqkfW55+3McbyDrg203duDmHAjdX6+Z0vV8+\nNdCe5X3jeRmgcL91suLu19a2x1m5MrMnUEy4vMzWqh0q433054u1dwomsBy1zX6n\ndLoh3JUfS+wuICcg1yk8GMFF/d0zKeHeyR8k/6H9W5J9sPpiYMeHL/bgWgv++iW1\n5cgWh24vnKm+EJpNsg4D+IrInXeJVAIUT3qUZ/c0vny+j53b9WXj01bLymudMCJU\nzPbecdKGw/l0vwhaDHc7\n=zBC6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-05-23T12:22:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/follo