m/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/325d9e3d0810d72a505891b946fbd056271e82a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199241?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/zburke","id":199241,"login":"zburke","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5OTI0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zburke","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/81ce56c02770515398235c19f4cf510fed24e42f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-05-12T17:49:22Z","email":"zburke@ebsco.com","name":"Zak Burke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-05-12T17:49:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-970 validateUser should return null on failure (#1629)\n\n`validateUser()` is expected to return session data on success or null\non failure. Previously, it wrongly returned an error message on failure,\ncausing its calling function (`checkOkapiSession()`) to act as though an\nexisting session were being restored (which of course is not the case\ngiven that session restoration had just failed...) and skip the\nSSO-check that happens only once, when stripes is initializing.\n\nRelated, restore the CSS for the \"Log in via SSO\" button so it remains\nprominently visible when it is present.\n\n## Approach\n\nIf cookies are revoked for any reason -- maybe a user deletes them,\nmaybe the backend revokes them -- then the UI will be in a state where\nit has valid session data in redux and in localstorage, but it no longer\nhas the corresponding cookies. This is an awkward state for Stripes,\nbecause it doesn''t know it''s in this state, because the cookies are\nHTTPOnly, so it never knows if cookies are acutally present.\n\nWhen reloading, the valid-session/invalid-cookies state was particularly\nproblematic. Stripes would find session data in storage and thus try to\nrestore the session with a request to `.../_self`, a request which would\nfail due to the missing cookies. Because `validateUser()` was\nincorrectly returning an error message, however, this caused Stripes to\nskip the SSO-check that normally runs when Stripes is initializing\nwithout an active session.\n\nMinor refactoring of `checkOkapiSession()` and `validateUser()` (the\nformer now passes an error-handler to the latter, because DI simplifies\ntesting) is a happy side-effect. The actual bugs being squashed are:\n\n* `validateUser()` now returns undefined on error, and correctly calls an\n  error-handler.\n* \"Log in via SSO\" button CSS is restored.\n\nRefs STCOR-970","tree":{"sha":"679f5a262e82c9c3e609fd541de064476f07369c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/679f5a262e82c9c3e609fd541de064476f07369c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/81ce56c02770515398235c19f4cf510fed24e42f","verification":{"payload":"tree 679f5a262e82c9c3e609fd541de064476f07369c\nparent b49ab6c3843ced96b0914517b5406874f2236068\nauthor Zak Burke <zburke@ebsco.com> 1747072162 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1747072162 -0400\n\nSTCOR-970 validateUser should return null on failure (#1629)\n\n`validateUser()` is expected to return session data on success or null\non failure. Previously, it wrongly returned an error message on failure,\ncausing its calling function (`checkOkapiSession()`) to act as though an\nexisting session were being restored (which of course is not the case\ngiven that session restoration had just failed...) and skip the\nSSO-check that happens only once, when stripes is initializing.\n\nRelated, restore the CSS for the \"Log in via SSO\" button so it remains\nprominently visible when it is present.\n\n## Approach\n\nIf cookies are revoked for any reason -- maybe a user deletes them,\nmaybe the backend revokes them -- then the UI will be in a state where\nit has valid session data in redux and in localstorage, but it no longer\nhas the corresponding cookies. This is an awkward state for Stripes,\nbecause it doesn''t know it''s in this state, because the cookies are\nHTTPOnly, so it never knows if cookies are acutally present.\n\nWhen reloading, the valid-session/invalid-cookies state was particularly\nproblematic. Stripes would find session data in storage and thus try to\nrestore the session with a request to `.../_self`, a request which would\nfail due to the missing cookies. Because `validateUser()` was\nincorrectly returning an error message, however, this caused Stripes to\nskip the SSO-check that normally runs when Stripes is initializing\nwithout an active session.\n\nMinor refactoring of `checkOkapiSession()` and `validateUser()` (the\nformer now passes an error-handler to the latter, because DI simplifies\ntesting) is a happy side-effect. The actual bugs being squashed are:\n\n* `validateUser()` now returns undefined on error, and correctly calls an\n  error-handler.\n* \"Log in via SSO\" button CSS is restored.\n\nRefs STCOR-970","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoIjSiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAibcQAH+wamu4N+jOGMLMv1xlEEdF\nj3wVldA7fLZVZnFfQ9aV1zNdciVL6XP3eRlWsOXpRKxscNIdaMPFrr7JJ3I+I32h\neiAoasR3xD+wBjdQ6ZWh+51lmN/dDtwiZQwmKlOuJxgsy3nymemrDkiv9//qZEtM\nAkWBoy1+/4wa/QBXC7TzglttGuO8oybweM9vjHH5KjdxjNHadsV0yezqVaKduZ/H\nHCJCdgReTTDXQ6z547HZQYPVMb6vaC1eldAe7LXWQ8+7pox/Hz6zUMxUXSxAqaFV\nHQG+v1Y2xmmxEqsaUoXFxenIVK++HGXB31yfAHTmCTO6Kfp2c1abFlpmzfM3D/4+\nC9U2KsyNrVjvouqdNQT5esSKuuena1TmnWqmfRud6oC8l5utPkUnnOi7QLAwbrxJ\nOkGIfAv9m5z7YbenkdSm/RRgEb2FHI1Bc+S0NDLQsTdu19FNhA6BHOafXIYmNn/X\nQT0kYWvL0cQVpwf5C/+6jBUNKdLs/rwps/udVbpYAd1mrZWc/sJNzEPOTTE3LPXU\n24SDfOvokycb5u0RyZxoTC9DaW8Jx92UP6IynqFsWec+hPKfk5/n7qZGPbcyPlSX\nr9+6KJiCWQqIE+9lphmbXZDjgCEdL0zmXzK1ci0lHBUTSl6NQjBy8DK3ldVevghj\nYxZg7RrWpfrAM2wuZsI6\n=tBLZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-05-12T17:51:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/81ce56c02770515398235c19f4cf510fed24e42f","node_id":"C_kwDOBEhK7NoAKDgxY2U1NmMwMjc3MDUxNTM5ODIzNWMxOWY0Y2Y1MTBmZWQyNGU0MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/folio-org/stripes-core/commit/b49ab6c3843ced96b0914517b5406874f2236068","sha":"b49ab6c3843ced96b0914517b5406874f2236068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/b49ab6c3843ced96b0914517b5406874f2236068"}],"sha":"81ce56c02770515398235c19f4cf510fed24e42f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/81ce56c02770515398235c19f4cf510fed24e42f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77053927?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","id":77053927,"login":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MDUzOTI3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dmytro-Melnyshyn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/commits/b49ab6c3843ced96b0914517b5406874f2236068/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-05-08T08:59:08Z","email":"77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dmytro-Melnyshyn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-05-08T08:59:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"STCOR-968: Enhance locale management to support user and tenant locale configurations from both mod-configuration and mod-settings. (#1628)\n\n## Description\nA new setting in `My profile` -> `Language & Localization` is created,\nwhich should use mod-settings API instead of deprecated\nmod-configuration. It was decided not to make a breaking change for\nstripes-core and still support mod-configuration in a\nbackwards-compatible way.\n\nThe main changes are in the `loadResources` function. First, if the user\ncan read mod-settings, it fetches locale information using two endpoints\n(one for tenant and one for the user). When these calls return, it\nchecks if at least one response contains a valid setting. If so, it\napplies those settings; otherwise, if the user has mod-configuration\nreading permission, it fetches locale information using the\nmod-configuration API for both user and tenant settings and applies\nthem. If the user doesn''t have mod-settings permission but has\nmod-configuration permission, it fetches locale information using the\nmod-configuration API. Additionally, if the user has mod-configuration\npermission, it fetches plugins and bindings. It also checks if the okapi\ninstance is not in \"withoutOkapi\" mode, it fetches module information\nusing `discoverServices`. Finally, it returns a flattened array of all\nthe results from the promises.\n\n## Changes in other modules\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-myprofile/pull/251\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-tenant-settings/pull/456\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-developer/pull/468\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/stripes-smart-components/pull/1577\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-plugin-query-builder/pull/246\n\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-968](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-968)\n\n## Screencasts\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1131450-6d43-4e6d-91e8-71d4d0633616","tree":{"sha":"e672d30224a2ee0c3133ee561201c0dbf49daa13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/trees/e672d30224a2ee0c3133ee561201c0dbf49daa13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/folio-org/stripes-core/git/commits/b49ab6c3843ced96b0914517b5406874f2236068","verification":{"payload":"tree e672d30224a2ee0c3133ee561201c0dbf49daa13\nparent 0d559d4375360723a5668581debf731132e91de3\nauthor Dmytro-Melnyshyn <77053927+Dmytro-Melnyshyn@users.noreply.github.com> 1746694748 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1746694748 +0300\n\nSTCOR-968: Enhance locale management to support user and tenant locale configurations from both mod-configuration and mod-settings. (#1628)\n\n## Description\nA new setting in `My profile` -> `Language & Localization` is created,\nwhich should use mod-settings API instead of deprecated\nmod-configuration. It was decided not to make a breaking change for\nstripes-core and still support mod-configuration in a\nbackwards-compatible way.\n\nThe main changes are in the `loadResources` function. First, if the user\ncan read mod-settings, it fetches locale information using two endpoints\n(one for tenant and one for the user). When these calls return, it\nchecks if at least one response contains a valid setting. If so, it\napplies those settings; otherwise, if the user has mod-configuration\nreading permission, it fetches locale information using the\nmod-configuration API for both user and tenant settings and applies\nthem. If the user doesn''t have mod-settings permission but has\nmod-configuration permission, it fetches locale information using the\nmod-configuration API. Additionally, if the user has mod-configuration\npermission, it fetches plugins and bindings. It also checks if the okapi\ninstance is not in \"withoutOkapi\" mode, it fetches module information\nusing `discoverServices`. Finally, it returns a flattened array of all\nthe results from the promises.\n\n## Changes in other modules\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-myprofile/pull/251\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-tenant-settings/pull/456\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-developer/pull/468\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/stripes-smart-components/pull/1577\nhttps://github.com/folio-org/ui-plugin-query-builder/pull/246\n\n\n## Issues\n[STCOR-968](https://folio-org.atlassian.net/browse/STCOR-968)\n\n## Screencasts\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1131450-6d43-4e6d-91e8-71d4d0633616","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoHHJcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASMcQAB4Hq7b8UpYtObeViLHNKP5H\nJJJh6bTJ/E9tuvPyp0fje0XhWnDik+LK3SXzwnW6IvcbWW9mfBeQiOu3h6+mnG