Batuktech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Batuktech","id":149748717,"login":"Batuktech","node_id":"U_kgDOCOz77Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Batuktech","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erxes/erxes/commits/1891e07b5c6d5affb8bb48bd61dd793abea902cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:35:40Z","email":"batuukka@gmail.com","name":"Batuk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:35:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(frontline): a custom domain per help center (#9567)\n\nA SaaS workspace could connect one help center domain. Each help center can\nnow have its own, so one workspace can serve several help centers on several\ndomains.\n\n- erxes-api-shared: organizations keep helpCenterDomains[] (each bound to a\n  helpCenterId); the old single helpCenterDomain is still read and moved\n  into the list on the next write, so no migration is needed\n- frontline_api: custom domain query/mutations take helpCenterId; a\n  hostname can belong to one help center only; pending checks cover every\n  domain; removing a help center disconnects its domain\n- a connected domain serves its own help center (helpCenterGetConfigByDomain\n  looks the binding up first, cached like the resolver), whatever its url\n- an existing domain is bound to the help center that serves it today: the\n  one whose url is the domain, else the one on <sub>.helpcenter, else the\n  oldest\n- frontline_ui: the Custom domain tab works on the help center being edited","tree":{"sha":"4cae1bea6faa7fc526dbb935a37fa2b1c696452b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erxes/erxes/git/trees/4cae1bea6faa7fc526dbb935a37fa2b1c696452b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erxes/erxes/git/commits/1891e07b5c6d5affb8bb48bd61dd793abea902cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 4cae1bea6faa7fc526dbb935a37fa2b1c696452b\nparent ceb0ea00041941649872f90c2f8ace24d101b531\nauthor Batuk <batuukka@gmail.com> 1791192940 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791192940 +0800\n\nfeat(frontline): a custom domain per help center (#9567)\n\nA SaaS workspace could connect one help center domain. Each help center can\nnow have its own, so one workspace can serve several help centers on several\ndomains.\n\n- erxes-api-shared: organizations keep helpCenterDomains[] (each bound to a\n  helpCenterId); the old single helpCenterDomain is still read and moved\n  into the list on the next write, so no migration is needed\n- frontline_api: custom domain query/mutations take helpCenterId; a\n  hostname can belong to one help center only; pending checks cover every\n  domain; removing a help center disconnects its domain\n- a connected domain serves its own help center (helpCenterGetConfigByDomain\n  looks the binding up first, cached like the resolver), whatever its url\n- an existing domain is bound to the help center that serves it today: the\n  one whose url is the domain, else the one on <sub>.helpcenter, else the\n  oldest\n- frontline_ui: the Custom domain tab works on the help center being edited","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw29sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASjAQAEN+FqyFRxYgyXMVmZZda/si\nwyFwreKioBcBs7exm/uIzRZf6rUEZwYABIaohDocHx56g2HK8GtFGVvCN8HEsyqE\n6e09amIolUYQwrrPlMJ2cIW7La1yYuZglZe14LA9b7HQFFjGbCOp80YdIBeh5QtD\nH48Snnu991trykEnGReGu/MVwdhCS8Me4QCbCNfzC+ABx42jI+HT1KY/Yin1fXZW\nceRlc6lPGMQ1Qa5QF8JemdYq3XAgPph3nMHVeV6ct4w2QP21tbkpZeIVPqA46mkC\njfC0bZldhVAf6gyAS9n3iV+/2+ZFip7GJUl