mmits/b60276508514e5e7f8cf925f4fa6038ddacb73a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104069564?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Wlkr123","id":104069564,"login":"Wlkr123","node_id":"U_kgDOBjP5vA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wlkr123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erxes/erxes/commits/d23cfaf9fbf375d36f1c6153977e3bfb9703edbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:13:25Z","email":"104069564+Wlkr123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tuguldur"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:13:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(loyalty): tiers, period runs, birthday coupons via nightly segment broadcasts (#9514)\n\n* feat: add Set Tier action to loyalty automations\n\n- Introduced `SetTierActionConfigForm` and `SetTierNodeContent` components for configuring and displaying the Set Tier action.\n- Implemented `SetTierActionResult` to handle the display of results for the Set Tier action.\n- Updated `LoyaltyActionNodeContent` to support the new Set Tier action type.\n- Refactored `AdjustScoreCampaignActionConfigForm` to remove the action toggle and integrate `EarnRowsField` for managing earning rows.\n- Created hooks for managing campaign earn rows and handling Set Tier action results.\n- Updated validation schemas for adjust score and set tier actions to reflect new requirements.\n- Removed the subtract action option from the adjust score action configuration.\n\n* feat: Refactor loyalty settings navigation and add period run features\n\n- Updated LoyaltySettingsNavigation to dynamically render menu items from LOYALTY_SETTINGS_PAGES.\n- Introduced LoyaltyAccountTypePeriodPreview component to display account type period information.\n- Enhanced LoyaltyAccountTypeExpirySection to include period preview.\n- Added LoyaltyPeriodRunPanel to show the status of loyalty period runs.\n- Implemented GraphQL queries for period run status and account type period preview.\n- Updated hooks to manage state and data fetching for new components.\n- Removed deprecated LoyaltySettings and LoyaltySidebar components.\n- Adjusted routing and breadcrumb logic to reflect new structure.\n\n* feat: add \"Tier changed\" trigger and related functionality\n\n- Implemented a new trigger for tier changes in loyalty accounts, allowing for automation based on tier transitions.\n- Introduced a configuration form for the \"Tier changed\" trigger, enabling users to specify account types, target tiers, and direction of change.\n- Enhanced the automation history to display detailed results for tier changes, including the owner and the specific tiers involved.\n- Added utility hooks and components to manage the state and display of tier change actions within the automation builder.\n- Refactored existing loyalty action results to accommodate the new \"Issue voucher\" action, providing clearer insights into issued vouchers and their recipients.\n- Updated the segment membership logic to support transitions and ensure accurate reporting of member movements.\n\n* feat(broadcast): send after a segment''s nightly refresh\n\nBirthday-style audiences move with the clock, not with record events, so\nthe per-record automation path would take a storm on every bulk change.\nA broadcast can now follow one time-sensitive segment instead: the nightly\nreconcile rebuild announces the segment as materialized and every live\ncampaign following it opens that day''s run for the members it holds.\n\n- shared: `source: ''reconcile''` on rebuild events, `sendSegmentMaterialized`\n- logs: only the nightly rebuild signals, once it finished; the earlier\n  clock-transition approach is removed\n- broadcast: `scheduleDate.type = ''afterSegment''`, one run per day\n  (unique occurrence), \"Nightly run missed\" trace after noon when no run\n  happened, list filter and status\n- UI: \"Nightly\" schedule option for one time-sensitive segment, a\n  \"Send nightly broadcast\" button on such segments, Send now hidden\n- `Segment.timeSensitive` exposed in GraphQL\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(contacts): edit a customer''s birth date\n\nThe field existed on the model and in the mutations but no form offered\nit, so birthday segments had nothing to read. It is now on the customer\ndetail form and the add form, and the detail query returns it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(loyalty): limit vouchers per owner\n\nA voucher campaign may cap what one owner receives per campaign, year or\nmonth, so a changed birth date cannot farm a second birthday coupon.\nEvery issue path enforces it: a single issue is refused, a bulk issue\nleaves those owners out, and the Issue voucher automation action reports\nthem as skipped. Vouchers, spins and lotteries from the campaign all count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fedd203405ff7047305a918446e60aeb63d9372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erxes/erxes/git/trees/9fedd203405ff7047305a918446e60aeb63d9372"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erxes/erxes/git/commits/d23cfaf9fbf375d36f1c6153977e3bfb9703edbd","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fedd203405ff7047305a918446e60aeb63d9372\nparent b7f99893f7f75c15ccb90fea9b8c286ec5bfb185\nauthor Tuguldur <104069564+Wlkr123@users.noreply.github.com> 1790777605 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790777605 +0800\n\nfeat(loyalty): tiers, period runs, birthday coupons via nightly segment broadcasts (#9514)\n\n* feat: add Set Tier action to loyalty automations\n\n- Introduced `SetTierActionConfigForm` and `SetTierNodeContent` components for configuring and displaying the Set Tier action.\n- Implemented `SetTierActionResult` to handle the display of results for the Set Tier action.\n- Updated `LoyaltyActionNodeContent` to support the new Set Tier action type.\n- Refactored `AdjustScoreCampaignActionConfigForm` to remove the action toggle and integrate `EarnRowsField` for managing earning rows.\n- Created hooks for managing campaign earn rows and handling Set Tier action results.\n- Updated validation schemas for adjust score and set tier actions to reflect new requirements.\n- Removed the subtract action option from the adjust score action configuration.\n\n* feat: Refactor loyalty settings navigation and add period run features\n\n- Updated LoyaltySettingsNavigation to dynamically render menu items from LOYALTY_SETTINGS_PAGES.\n- Introduced LoyaltyAccountTypePeriodPreview component to display account type period information.\n- Enhanced LoyaltyAccountTypeExpirySection to include period preview.\n- Added LoyaltyPeriodRunPanel to show the status of loyalty period runs.\n- Implemented GraphQL queries for period run status and account type period preview.\n- Updated hooks to manage state and data fetching for new components.\n- Removed deprecated LoyaltySettings and LoyaltySidebar components.\n- Adjusted routing and breadcrumb logic to reflect new structure.\n\n* feat: add \"Tier changed\" trigger and related functionality\n\n- Implemented a new trigger for tier changes in loyalty accounts, allowing for automation based on tier transitions.\n- Introduced a configuration form for the \"Tier changed\" trigger, enabling users to specify account types, target tiers, and direction of change.\n- Enhanced the automation history to display detailed results for tier changes, including the owner and the specific tiers involved.\n- Added utility hooks and components to manage the state and display of tier change actions within the automation builder.\n- Refactored existing loyalty action results to accommodate the new \"Issue voucher\" action, providing clearer insights into issued vouchers and their recipients.\n- Updated the segment membership logic to support transitions and ensure accurate reporting of member movements.\n\n* feat(broadcast): send after a segment''s nightly refresh\n\nBirthday-style audiences move with the clock, not with record events, so\nthe per-record automation path would take a storm on every bulk change.\nA broadcast can now follow one time-sensitive segment instead: the nightly\nreconcile rebuild announces the segment as materialized and every live\ncampaign following it opens that day''s run for the members it holds.\n\n- shared: `source: ''reconcile''` on rebuild events, `sendSegmentMaterialized`\n- logs: only the nightly rebuild signals, once it finished; the earlier\n  clock-transition approach is removed\n- broadcast: `scheduleDate.type = ''afterSegment''`, one run per day\n  (unique occurrence), \"Nightly run missed\" trace after noon when no run\n  happened, list filter and status\n- UI: \"Nightly\" schedule option for one time-sensitive segment, a\n  \"Send nightly broadcast\" button on such segments, Send now hidden\n- `Segment.timeSensitive` exposed in GraphQL\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(contacts): edit a customer''s birth date\n\nThe field existed on the model and in the mutations but no form offered\nit, so birthday segments had nothing to read. It is now on the customer\ndetail form and the add form, and the detail query returns it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(loyalty): limit vouchers per owner\n\nA voucher campaign may cap what one owner receives per campaign, year or\nmonth, so a changed birth date cannot farm a second birthday coupon.\nEvery issue path enforces it: a single issue is refused, a bulk issue\nleaves those owners out, and the Issue voucher automation action reports\nthem as skipped. Vouchers, spins and lotteries from the campaign all count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRkFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoTUQAIMN4mC/Re4evxlGr0M/uXd6\nIzSrnIN2bTqfWe7P6LfahKWsmsry1ERpra/iHYpuPOB5MH2YFA3ppXGLGlk3oj4y\nn81lUFiPM1WGpK8hrDFKFJ/tkGN4WiHZGLYg2GmU4rDEjIAC4mFjxDSRxHpxTaB7\ngdZ1kdgS7QkrQsDK36icZMqMTNBd1J4i20/ISWfTrE4ExzNZ2AXAnLSwAmi5EtgR\nlcrjwM3umhQZtP9gcrVEg/Hdii37UGfzhZZ/0Sm8YFjDXpga17DNzvEK1VX+rMfl\nIqN2oKM9yT5Yh8KKng5r/qZLEkP3FGL5NWEUAZH9ZuUVwDixz3w1YllICxxDgul9\nFgqVzP2UYVLjY5wTJbQvlERPgvaJxefROw2u7OMA13ejhY8kdSIoqlVtVSB3T3dI\nfcffcDmMR36hNRqVDTnGqREtBhA7YlAusngfWV6ALA5fGMhJ6q6IbDVkvfYxg9mj\nkXFrc68YY8Y5ykPvYSX96YvCwz1yNo59A4/p9iWZAXMwq7ZvQtDRUS+gb5iOeNZv\nu2LDwox70WBCjGkNF3RGrbBf7ASsfiz6pSgMqK2E7GZS3VShXQMpWEH+5Qr7Xpbg\nU0ebjaIfwz8oB+lyd5gjqBLAmOuwhZ0jjraKlVNxCnXqrWDJy7iWgZH6mFAmqd5e\n9Y+ZgBh67ehEjQ8zJ7PS\n=w01z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T14:13:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.c